    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`plugins/stella-research` ships as Track B's first extraction (#3380 §7) and the\nbuilt-in stage stays: `doc:pipeline-as-plugins` §7 sets the bar as \"a\nside-by-side benchmark holds before the built-in path is deleted\", and the two\npaths are **not** equivalent today, in a direction that must be measured rather\nthan argued:\n\n- The built-in answers triage's questions with parallel read-only **model**\n  sub-agents (`crates/stella-pipeline/src/pipeline/research_stage.rs`).\n- The plugin does a deterministic literal scan of the granted workspace\n  (`plugins/stella-research/main.py`) because a plugin cannot cause a model call\n  (#3541) and never receives the questions (#3539).\n\nCheaper and checkable, but weaker input. Which wins on task outcome is an\nempirical question and nobody has asked it.\n\n## What has to exist first\n\n1. The `--pipeline <variant>` flag inversion (#3381), so a run can select\n   `research-v1` against `classic`.\n2. `Wrapper::id` reaching `executions.pipeline_variant` — the column and\n   migration shipped (`crates/stella-store/src/ddl.rs`), and the only writer\n   still passes the constant `PIPELINE_VARIANT_CLASSIC`\n   (`crates/stella-cli/src/agent/persistence.rs`). Without it the two arms are\n   indistinguishable in the store and the comparison cannot be computed.\n\n## How to run it, so the answer means something\n\nPer CLAUDE.md's bench rules: repeats per task, `stella-events.jsonl` as ground\ntruth rather than the summary layer, operational aborts named and excluded, and\nthe unflattering number reported when it is the true one. A five-task solve rate\ncannot resolve this — the mechanism metrics (research findings that appear in\nthe diff's touched files, planner prompt size, stage wall clock, cost per turn)\nare the measurement.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A recorded comparison of `research-v1` against `classic` with repeats per\n  task, written where a later reader can find it.\n- A decision recorded from it: keep both, keep the built-in, or delete the\n  built-in — and if the plugin loses, *why* (the model-call gap #3541 is the\n  hypothesis to falsify first).\n\nRefs #3380, #3381, #3388.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3544[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Benchmark research-v1 (the plugin) against classic (the built-in research stage) before anything built-in is deleted"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
