    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`WrapperDispatch::open_round`\n(`crates/stella-runtime/src/wrapper/dispatch.rs`) calls `before_turn` once per\nstage the resolved `StageProgram` runs, and `SubprocessWrapper::exchange`\nspawns a fresh process per call — one request in, one response out, `kill_on_drop`.\n\nA wrapper declares *stages* in `[wrapper]` (which is the variant's stage order,\nso it is the whole pipeline) and *points* in `[loop].points` (which is\n`before_turn` / `after_turn`). There is no way to declare **which stages** it\nanswers at.\n\n`plugins/stella-research` contributes at exactly one stage (`research`) and\ndeclares the eight-stage classic order, so a round starts `python3` eight times\nand gets `{\"protocol_version\":1}` seven times. It is correct and it is waste\nthat scales with the stage list.\n\n## Why it is worth fixing rather than absorbing\n\n- Interpreter start dominates: a Python or Node plugin pays ~30-80ms per spawn\n  before it reads a byte, and every installed wrapper pays it per stage per\n  round. #3528 (the turn is clock-bound) is the epic this feeds.\n- It gets worse with the thing the design wants: several installed wrappers,\n  each declaring the same order, each spawned per stage.\n\n## Options\n\n1. **Declare the stages a point answers** — e.g. `[loop] before_turn_stages =\n   [\"research\"]`, filtered by the same `permits_*` shape as `permits_point`, so\n   an undeclared stage is never dispatched. Smallest change; keeps one process\n   per call.\n2. **One process per round, several exchanges** — the transport keeps the child\n   alive and frames N requests on stdin. Faster, but it turns a stateless\n   contract into a session and needs a framing decision (`doc:plugin-transport-spike`).\n3. **Accept it** and document the cost so plugin authors declare the shortest\n   honest stage list.\n\nOption 1 preserves everything the current transport guarantees and is the one\n`[loop]`'s existing shape argues for.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A plugin that contributes at one stage is spawned once per round.\n- The filter is authoritative the way `LoopGrant::permits_point` is — an\n  undeclared stage is never dispatched, not merely usually skipped.\n- A witness: a fixture wrapper counting its own invocations across a round with\n  a multi-stage program.\n\nRefs #3380, #3494, #3528.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3543[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"before_turn spawns a plugin's process once per declared stage, so a one-stage plugin pays N process starts per round"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
