    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`BeforeTurnResponse::publish` exists so a stage can publish signals \"for later\nstages of the same turn to read\", and `admissible`\n(`crates/stella-runtime/src/wrapper/mod.rs`) checks the value's *kind*. What it\ncannot check — because the vocabulary does not support the question — is\nwhether the publishing stage is one that publishes that signal at all.\n\n`StageName::Research.publishes()` is `&[]`\n(`crates/stella-plugin/src/wrapper.rs`), and every entry in `Signal` belongs to\ntriage, execute, witness or verify. So `plugins/stella-research` publishes\nnothing, and it is not a shortcut: there is no signal it could publish that\nwould be true. \"How many groundings did research find\" and \"did research find\nthe symbol the goal names\" are exactly the facts a later stage would branch on,\nand neither is expressible.\n\nThis is the `doc:pipeline-as-plugins` §A8 tail (\"Signal is 5 values and only\nTriage publishes any\" — it is 15 now, and the stages that publish are still\nfour), pointed at the stage Track B extracted first.\n\n## The second half: a published value has nowhere to go\n\n`BeforeTurnResponse::publish`'s own doc calls this out as a declared gap:\n`Wrapper::resolve` takes one up-front `SignalValues` snapshot, so a value a\nstage publishes mid-turn cannot reach the condition that reads it (#3491). Both\nhalves have to close for a publication to mean anything — a signal a research\nstage may publish is useless while nothing can read it, and vice versa.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- Either `Signal` grows the research-published facts (each transcribing a live\n  branch, per the rule the enum's doc comment sets), and\n  `StageName::Research.publishes()` names them; or the impossibility is written\n  down where a plugin author meets it.\n- `plugins/stella-research` publishes them, and\n  `crates/stella-runtime/tests/research_plugin_conformance.rs` stops asserting\n  `response.publish.is_empty()`.\n- #3491 closes alongside, or the new signals are documented as unreadable until\n  it does.\n\nRefs #3380, #3491.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3542[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"A research stage has no signal it may honestly publish, so a before_turn contribution cannot tell a later stage what it found"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
