    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`stella-plugin` and `stella-runtime` have no `area:*` label, and the backlog can no longer absorb that.\n\nThe triage sweep of 2026-08-17 processed 55 open issues. **Twenty-six of them land in `crates/stella-plugin/` or `crates/stella-runtime/`** — the manifest grammar, the wrapper socket, the verdict path, the consent transaction, the plugin roster. Every one had to be routed to `area:core` under the AGENTS.md fallback rule, which is now actively misleading: `area:core` is documented as `stella-core`, the crate those two are specifically *not* allowed to live in (invariant #1 forbids `stella-core` depending on `stella-plugin` at all).\n\nSo a filter on `area:core` now returns two disjoint populations, and a filter that would find the plugin platform's 26 issues does not exist.\n\n## Why this is not just a missing label\n\n`stella-plugin` was a leaf crate with a handful of issues when the fallback was written. It is now the substrate of an entire epic tree (#3246, #3274) with two P0 security defects (#3509, #3512) and three P0/P1 verification-integrity defects (#3510, #3513, #3515) in it. The routing table in AGENTS.md § \"Workspace layout\" does not list either crate, so a contributor deciding where a change goes gets no answer.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n1. A label `area:plugin` exists, covering `crates/stella-plugin/` and `crates/stella-runtime/` — or two labels if the wrapper socket's presence in `stella-runtime` argues for splitting them. Decide which; do not create both by default.\n2. The 26 issues below are relabelled, and `area:core` removed from the ones where it was only the fallback (keep it where the issue genuinely touches `stella-core` too — e.g. #3486, #3487, #3522 name engine-side seams):\n\n   #3380 #3381 #3408 #3472 #3481 #3483 #3484 #3486 #3487 #3491 #3492 #3494 #3496 #3497 #3498 #3499 #3500 #3501 #3509 #3510 #3512 #3513 #3514 #3515 #3518 #3520 #3521 #3522 #3523 #3524 #3529\n\n3. AGENTS.md § \"Workspace layout — where a change goes\" gains rows for `stella-plugin` and `stella-runtime` pointing at the new label. Both crates already have READMEs to link.\n4. `.claude/commands/backlog-triage.md`'s crate→label table gains the rows, and its \"six crates have no label of their own\" sentence is corrected — it currently names `stella-home`, `stella-diag`, `stella-diff`, `stella-engine`, `stella-runtime`, `stella-parity`, and would be down to five (or four).\n\n## Remaining unlabelled crates, for the same decision\n\n`stella-home`, `stella-diag`, `stella-diff`, `stella-engine`, `stella-parity` carry few or no open issues today and do **not** need labels on this evidence. Named here so the next sweep does not re-derive the list. Do not create labels speculatively — the argument above is a volume argument, and it applies to `stella-plugin` alone.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3531[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Taxonomy: stella-plugin has 26 open issues and no area label, so they all route to area:core — which invariant #1 forbids them depending on"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
