    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`crates/stella-tui/src/envelope.rs` is **1496 lines** after commit `df89681`\n(#3472's first slice, which added 11). The file is *not* in\n`scripts/file-size-baseline.txt`, so it is judged against the flat 1500-line\nlimit: the next PR that adds five lines of type or doc to the deck's wire\ncontract fails `make gate`, and the tempting fix — a new baseline entry — is\nthe expedient CLAUDE.md forbids and the one `--update` now refuses outright\n(#3441).\n\nIt is also the file every envelope-contract change has to touch, so the\npressure is continuous rather than incidental. Two changes already queued\nagainst it: a contributor/provenance field on `RoleWiringRow` (#3492) and\nwhatever the plugin host needs to describe a contributed row.\n\n## Repro\n\n```\nwc -l crates/stella-tui/src/envelope.rs      # 1496\n./scripts/check-file-size.sh                 # OK today; fails at 1501\n```\n\n## Shape of the fix\n\nThe file already carries submodules under `crates/stella-tui/src/envelope/`\n(`mcp.rs`, `steering.rs`, `roles.rs`), so the pattern is established and\nneeds no rename of `envelope.rs` itself: move a cohesive cluster of types out\nand re-export it, exactly as `mcp.rs` does. Candidate clusters, largest first\n— measure before choosing:\n\n- the engine-config cluster (`EngineRole`, `EngineAgentState`,\n  `RoleWiringRow`, `EngineConfigState`) → `envelope/engine_config.rs`, which\n  is also where #3492's new field would land;\n- the skills cluster (`SkillRow`, `SkillScope`, `SkillOp`, `SkillsView`,\n  `SkillSearchHit`);\n- the tool-policy cluster (`ToolRow`, `ToolScope`, `ToolPolicyState`,\n  `ToolDenial`).\n\nRe-export from `envelope.rs` so `stella_tui::envelope::…` and the crate-root\n`pub use envelope::{…}` list in `src/lib.rs` are unchanged — this must be a\npure move, with no import churn in `views/`, `deck_ui/` or `stella-cli`.\n\n## Done when\n\n- `envelope.rs` is comfortably under 1500 (target ≤ 1200 so the next contract\n  change has room), no file in the crate is over it, and **no entry is added\n  to `scripts/file-size-baseline.txt`**.\n- `cargo test -p stella-tui` and `cargo clippy -p stella-tui --all-targets --\n  -D warnings` are green; the move changes no behaviour, so a witness test is\n  not expected — say so in the PR template.\n- `./scripts/check-god-files.sh` still passes (the crate's README and\n  AGENTS.md name its god files; a split must not strand those lists).\n\nRefs #3472, #3492"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3493[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"crates/stella-tui/src/envelope.rs is 4 lines from the 1500-line ceiling and is not grandfathered"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
