    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## What is happening\n\nThe `Dependabot Updates` cargo job fails partway through, on `serde` specifically:\n\n```\nupdater | ERROR <job_1526904502> Error processing serde (RuntimeError)\n          ERROR <job_1526904502> Failed to update serde!\n          ERROR .../dependabot/cargo/file_updater/lockfile_updater.rb:127:in\n                'Dependabot::Cargo::FileUpdater::LockfileUpdater#validate_dependency_update'\n```\n\nExample run: https://github.com/macanderson/stella/actions/runs/31946407960 (2026-08-16)\n\nIt is **partial, not total** — on 2026-08-16 two of the four Dependabot jobs succeeded and two failed, and the same mix appears on 2026-08-13 (three failures) and 2026-08-09. So dependency updates are half-working rather than dead, which is exactly the state that goes unnoticed: PRs do appear, so nobody checks whether some are missing.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n`Cargo.lock` is tracked and `install.sh` builds `--locked` (AGENTS.md § Gotchas), so lockfile-affecting updates are load-bearing here rather than cosmetic. A dependency whose update silently never gets proposed is a dependency that quietly ages — and `cargo deny`'s `advisories`/`yanked` gates are the thing that eventually turns that into a red gate for whoever is unlucky, rather than a routine bump.\n\n## What is NOT the cause\n\nNot a repository code defect: the failure is inside Dependabot's own Ruby cargo `LockfileUpdater`, running on Dependabot's infrastructure. Nothing in this repo's CI configuration is executing at that point.\n\n## Suggested investigation\n\n1. Determine why `serde` in particular trips `validate_dependency_update`. This workspace pins `serde` through `[workspace.dependencies]` and also carries `serde_core` as a transitive — a split-crate arrangement is a plausible trigger for a validator that expects one version to resolve.\n2. Check whether the exact-pinned registry crates (`contextgraph-*`, pinned with `=` requirements per AGENTS.md) interact badly with the group update rules in `.github/dependabot.yml` — the failing job is the grouped `cargo` update (`dependency-groups: [{name: cargo, rules: {update-types: [minor, patch]}}]`).\n3. If it is an upstream bug, an `ignore` entry for `serde` would unblock the rest of the group — but that is a decision to stop tracking `serde` updates automatically, so it needs to be deliberate and commented, not a silent workaround.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- The `Dependabot Updates` cargo job completes without a `RuntimeError`, or\n- The cause is confirmed upstream and linked here, with whatever scoped `ignore`/config change is needed carrying a comment saying why.\n- Either way: a statement of which dependencies are, and are not, being tracked automatically — since the current state is \"some are, silently\".\n\nFound while monitoring `main` CI on 2026-08-17. Not blocking any required check.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3459[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Dependabot's cargo lockfile updater fails on serde, so part of every grouped update is silently not proposed"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
