    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## The problem\n\n#3358 (PR #3435) put skills' and frames' evictions into `SteeringSet::dropped`, so the ledger is now complete across the record, skill and memory sources. The **human-facing** half is not: `report_record_drops` (`crates/stella-cli/src/memory/recall.rs`) filters `set.dropped` to `SteeringSource::Record` and prints only those, through the single producer `record_drop_message`. A skill that loses its seat every turn, or a frame the recall host's merge evicts, is now queryable but still says nothing to the person watching the run — which is the #2709 observability gap in its other half.\n\nTwo smaller silences noticed alongside, both in `recalled_frames_anchored` (same file) and both distinct from the host-merge drops #3358 wired:\n\n- Frames filtered out by the citation-label rule (`project_recalled_frame` returns `None`) vanish uncounted. The provider spent tokens fetching them.\n- Frames dropped by quarantine (`is_suppressed_local_frame`) also vanish. This one is deliberate suppression rather than a budget eviction, so it may want a different vocabulary than `DroppedCandidate` — decide, don't default.\n\n## What done looks like\n\n- One drop line per evicted candidate regardless of source, following `record_drop_message`'s shape rather than adding a second format (the constraint #3358 was held to). Each source needs its own remedy sentence: \"raise `skills.max_skills`\", \"raise `context.retrieval.max_tokens`\", not the record channel's precedence advice.\n- The section-budget skill omission needs care: it appears in both `selected` and `dropped` by design (see the `GatheredSteering::source_drops` doc), so a naive loop over `set.dropped` would tell a user a skill was dropped that is in fact in their prompt. Either the line says what actually happened (\"rendered without body/omitted from the section\") or that class is excluded until #3243 Phase 4 collapses the budgets.\n- A decision, recorded in code, on the two recall-side filters above: reported, or deliberately not, with the reason.\n\n## Verify\n\nExtend `crates/stella-cli/src/memory/tests/steering_selection.rs`, which already has the injectable-sink pattern (`recalled_frames_anchored(goal, anchors, |message| …)`) — assert the message text for a skill drop and a frame drop, as `memory/tests/record_channel.rs` does for records.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The golden block test (`crates/stella-cli/src/memory/tests/golden_block.rs`) pins the volatile block byte-for-byte; a diagnostic must not reach the prompt.\n- `report_record_drops` is called from three sites (`recall_block_reported`, `pipeline_recall_block`, `signal_recall_block`); widening it widens all three, including the mid-turn re-query, which fires per drifted step — check the volume before making it unconditional.\n\nRefs #3358, #3349, #2709, #3243\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3437[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"steering: the drop report is on the ledger for all three sources but on stderr for only one"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
