    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`deck-fit.yml`'s deck **enumeration** has no automated regression test. #3376 was\nexactly an enumeration bug — a recursive trigger paired with a non-recursive glob —\nand #3403 fixed it, but the fix's witness was run by hand against a throwaway fixture\ntree and then deleted. Nothing in CI or `make gate` would catch the same class of\nmistake being reintroduced: the enumeration silently covering fewer files than the\ntrigger implies.\n\nThis is the shape both #2425 and #3376 already are, twice: a check that is green\nwhile measuring less than a reader believes. The third occurrence should be caught by\na test rather than by someone noticing.\n\n## Why it was not done in #3403\n\nThe measurement loop lives inline in the workflow's `run:` block, so there is no\naddressable unit to test. Testing it means first extracting it — e.g. to\n`scripts/deck-fit-all.sh <root>` with the workflow reduced to one call — which is a\nlarger, separately reviewable change than the bug fix warranted.\n\nA committed always-failing fixture deck is *not* the answer: anything under\n`website/public/presentations/` is measured by construction, so it would red-line the\nreal job.\n\n## Files\n\n- `.github/workflows/deck-fit.yml` — the `every slide fits the canvas at every\n  viewport` step holds the enumeration and the pass/skip/fail accounting.\n- `scripts/deck-fit.mjs` — exit statuses 0/1/2/3 documented in its header; the\n  script itself needs no change.\n\n## Suggested shape\n\n1. Extract the loop to `scripts/deck-fit-all.sh`, taking the tree root as `$1` and\n   defaulting to `website/public/presentations`; the workflow step becomes one call.\n2. Add a hermetic test (a shell test in the style of `make impacted-test`, needing no\n   browser) that points the script at a temporary fixture tree **outside** the\n   presentations directory, with `node` replaced by a stub whose exit status is\n   derived from the filename. Assert:\n   - a deck in a subdirectory is enumerated (the #3376 regression);\n   - a top-level deck is still enumerated;\n   - exit status 3 counts as a skip, is printed with its path, and does not fail;\n   - a failing deck does not abort the loop early (the step runs under `bash -e`);\n   - an empty tree still exits 1.\n3. Keep it out of `make gate` only if it needs a browser — the stub form does not,\n   so it can join the gate.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- The enumeration is callable outside the workflow and covered by a test that fails\n  if the walk stops being recursive, if a skip becomes silent, or if a failing deck\n  aborts the loop.\n- The test needs no browser and no network.\n- `deck-fit.yml` still measures exactly what it measures today (verify: investor-deck\n  measured, `turn-loop/index.html` skipped by name, job green).\n\nRefs #3376, #3403, #2425.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3404[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"deck-fit's deck enumeration has no regression test: extract the loop and cover it"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nOn the `cloud run` path with a gate armed, each Batch job's whole S3 prefix is\ndownloaded **twice**, into two full byte copies:\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/gate_watch.py:85-89` — at gate settlement the watcher\n  pulls `runs/<run-id>/<job-id>/` into `dest/<label>/`;\n- `arenabench/arenabench/cloud_executor.py:518` — the fetch tail then pulls\n  `runs/<run-id>/` into `dest/`, producing `dest/<job-uuid>/...`.\n\nNeither writer knows about the other. `_fetch_prefix` is name-blind: it is\nhanded the run-level prefix and derives its destination purely from the S3\nkey, so it cannot reuse the label directory (`cloud_executor.py:532-536`).\n\nThe *assembly* consequence — one trial filed as two cells, the `x2` twin — is\nfixed in #3324 by recognising the two roots as one job through the submission\nsidecar's id/label pairing. The waste is not: a run still pays double egress\nand double disk for every trial's artifacts.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nA gated `cloud run --artifacts` downloads each job's artifacts once. The\ncheapest shape found while fixing #3324: pass the `{job_id: label}` map into\n`fetch_results`' artifact branch (or give `_fetch_prefix` a per-segment rename\ncallback) so both writers land on `dest/<label>/`. Whichever root wins, the\nchoice must stay stable for already-fetched runs — the #3324 dedup keys on the\nsidecar, not on a root name, so it survives either answer, but `bench` readers\nthat glob a run directory should be checked.\n\nA test asserting the fake S3 client saw each key once (the recorded-call fakes\nin `arenabench/tests/cloud_fakes.py` already support this) is the witness.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The trial glob `*/ws/matches/*/jobs/*/*` (`assemble.py:102`) is shared with\n  `bench.trace_triage.run_trace`; do not change the depth of the tree without\n  changing both.\n- Fetch layout changes are observable to anything reading\n  `~/arenabench-results/<run>/`. Say so in the PR.\n\nRefs #3324.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3400[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: a gated cloud run downloads every trial's artifacts twice"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`make brand-case` fails on `main` at `730f2286c`, and its whole output is one\nline:\n\n```\ncheck-brand-case: docs prose spells the wordmark lowercase\n```\n\nTwo separate defects, and the second is the one that will keep costing time.\n\n**1. The gate is red on `main`.** Confirmed by deleting an in-flight new doc and\nre-running: the failure is inherited, not introduced. Since a red gate step\nmasks every step after it in `GATE_STEPS`, anyone running the full gate on a\ndocs-touching branch stops here and never reaches the steps below it.\n\n**2. The failure names nothing.** It does not print the file, the line, or the\noffending text. A contributor who did not write the offending prose cannot tell\nwhether the failure is theirs, and a contributor who did cannot find it without\nre-implementing the script's matcher by hand. Compare `check-doc-links`, which\nprints every unresolved citation and the document it sits in, or\n`check-file-size`, which names the file and both numbers.\n\n## Files\n\n- `scripts/check-brand-case.sh` — the guard.\n- `Makefile` — `brand-case` in `GATE_STEPS`.\n\n## Verify\n\n```\nsh scripts/check-brand-case.sh   # currently exits non-zero, prints one line\n```\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- Whatever prose is currently lowercase is fixed, and `make brand-case` is green\n  on `main`.\n- The guard prints `path:line` plus the matched text for every violation, so a\n  future failure is actionable from its output alone. This half matters more\n  than the first: without it, the next red is as slow to diagnose as this one.\n- A test or fixture pinning the reporting shape, so a later refactor cannot\n  silently return the guard to a bare verdict line.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not fold this into an unrelated PR. It is a repair of a shared cell on\n  `main` and should land on its own from a fresh `main`, per the AGENTS.md\n  guidance on inherited gate drift.\n- The guard deliberately exempts code paths, filenames and command names\n  (`stella run`, `crates/stella-core/...`). Whatever fix lands must not start\n  flagging those.\n\nNoticed while landing `doc:turn-loop-wrappers` (#3379/#3380/#3381), which does\nnot touch it.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3382[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"gate: brand-case is red on main and its failure names no file, line, or matched text"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
