    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`make shellcheck` (Makefile ~line 296) and ci.yml's shellcheck step (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, the `run: shellcheck …` line in the gate job) each spell out the same argument list by hand. `scripts/check-gate-parity.sh` guards which *steps* the gate lists, not what arguments a step's two copies pass — so the lists can drift silently.\n\nThey already did: #3353 taught the Makefile target the `scripts/lib/*.sh` glob (needed so shellcheck follows the sourced `help-header.sh` instead of tripping SC1091), but ci.yml kept the old list. Result: `make shellcheck` green locally, the CI step red on every PR, masked behind the stella-parity failure #3371 fixed until #3372 repaired the ci.yml copy. Two PRs and several red CI rounds to find one drifted glob.\n\n## Fix shape (pick one)\n\n1. **Single source:** have ci.yml run `make shellcheck` (shellcheck ships preinstalled on ubuntu-latest; make is available) so there is one argument list. Simplest and matches how the rest of the gate steps are already make targets in spirit.\n2. Or extract the file list into a small script (`scripts/shellcheck-targets.sh` or similar) both callers invoke.\n3. Or extend `check-gate-parity.sh` to diff the two invocations.\n\nOption 1 is probably right; the ci.yml comment near the step (added in #3372) already pins the two lists together prose-wise, which is exactly the arrangement that failed before.\n\n## Verify\n\nChange the Makefile target's file list without touching ci.yml; the guard (or shared entry point) must go red — today nothing does.\n\n## Constraints\n- The gate job runs shellcheck before any toolchain install on purpose (toolchain-free rung); keep it that way.\n- Refs #3353 (introduced the drift), #3372 (repaired this instance), #1439 (the gate/ci split rationale).\n\nRefs #3372"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3375[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"gate-parity: ci.yml's shellcheck invocation is a hand-copied argument list nothing keeps in sync with the Makefile"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
