    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`Settings::load` reads `STELLA_MANAGED_SETTINGS` (`crates/stella-cli/src/settings/managed.rs:44`) and other env vars. The binary-wide convention is that any test whose code path reads the environment holds `crate::test_env::lock()` and restores via `EnvRestore` — e.g. `managed_authority_rejects_unknown_keys_through_settings_load` (`crates/stella-cli/src/settings/authority.rs`), which sets `STELLA_MANAGED_SETTINGS` to a fixture containing a deliberate typo (`project_promtps`).\n\nBut roughly 25 tests call `Settings::load` (or save/roundtrip helpers that call it) WITHOUT taking the lock. When the test scheduler interleaves one of them with a lock-holding test that has just set `STELLA_MANAGED_SETTINGS`, the lockless test loads the other test's managed fixture and fails on an error that has nothing to do with it.\n\n## Observed failure (2026-08-16, filtered run `cargo test -p stella-cli --bin stella settings`)\n\n```\nsettings::tests::enable_recap_survives_the_scope_merge panicked:\nsettings load: \"invalid settings file .../T/.tmpruMXbc/managed.json: unknown field `project_promtps`, ...\"\n```\n\nThe typo fixture belongs to `managed_authority_rejects_unknown_keys_through_settings_load`; `enable_recap_survives_the_scope_merge` (`crates/stella-cli/src/settings/tests.rs` ~1080) never touches managed settings. The full-suite run usually passes because scheduling rarely interleaves them; filtered runs (`... settings`) hit it readily.\n\n## Affected (lockless `Settings::load` callers)\n\nIn `crates/stella-cli/src/settings/tests.rs`: `missing_files_merge_to_empty_settings`, `the_edit_reader_returns_one_files_engine_block_not_the_merge`, `later_scopes_overlay_earlier_ones_field_by_field`, `mcp_registry_url_defaults_and_takes_the_last_scope`, `hooks_concatenate_across_scopes_instead_of_replacing`, `settings_without_hooks_stay_hook_free`, `agent_engine_config_*` (3), `ui_theme_save_preserves_other_keys_and_roundtrips`, `every_tool_is_on_with_no_settings_at_all`, `trace_capture_defaults_off_and_survives_the_scope_merge`, `ignore_gitignore_defaults_on_and_an_off_survives_the_scope_merge`, `a_tools_entry_switches_a_tool_off_and_the_project_scope_wins_per_key`, `a_group_key_switches_off_the_whole_family`, `mcp_and_custom_tool_names_are_addressable_from_settings`, `enable_recap_survives_the_scope_merge`, `enable_recap_defaults_off_when_no_scope_sets_it`, `create_worktrees_survives_the_scope_merge`, and several parse-error tests; plus `every_merged_settings_field_survives_the_scope_merge` in `settings/completeness.rs`. (List from a crude sweep — re-derive with an rg pass over `#[test]` bodies containing `Settings::load` but not `test_env::lock`; some may go through helpers that never read env.)\n\n## Fix shape\n\nAdd `let _env = crate::test_env::lock();` (shared/read lock is enough — these tests only need the env NOT to change under them) at the top of each affected test. No `EnvRestore` needed for tests that set nothing. Alternatively, a `load_with_clean_env` test helper that takes the lock internally would prevent recurrence.\n\n## Verify\n\n`for i in 1..10: cargo test -p stella-cli --bin stella settings` — currently flakes within a few iterations; must pass all.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Pre-existing; unrelated to PR #3348, which is where it was observed.\n- `set_var`/`get_var` racing is UB on POSIX — this is a correctness fix, not just flake hygiene.\n\n## Done\n\nAll `Settings::load`-calling tests hold the env lock; the filtered loop above is stable."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3369[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"settings tests: ~25 tests call Settings::load without test_env::lock(), racing STELLA_MANAGED_SETTINGS setters"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
