    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nThe release version-sync automation bumps every workspace crate's `Cargo.toml` but does not always refresh the matching `[[package]]` entry in `Cargo.lock`. When it misses one, the required CI step **\"Cargo.lock is in sync with the manifests\"** fails on `main`, and because it is a required check, *every* PR opened afterwards inherits a red gate until someone notices.\n\nThis happened on 2026-08-16: the 0.9.50 sync (#3316, #3323) left `crates/stella-plugin` at `version = \"0.9.49\"` in `Cargo.lock` while its manifest read `0.9.50`. `main` was red from `543f5d486` through `074124b9c` and was unblocked by the one-line #3333.\n\n`stella-plugin` is a **newly added crate** (the #3245 slice A work). That is the suspicious part: the older crates were all resynced correctly in the same commit, so the likely defect is that the sync step enumerates a stale crate list — or regenerates the lock before the new member is visible — rather than simply running `cargo metadata` after the bump.\n\n## Why it recurs\n\nNothing in the release path asserts the invariant the CI step checks, so the failure is only ever discovered *after* the sync commit is already on `main`. The next crate added to the workspace hits it again.\n\n## Files\n\n- `.github/workflows/` — the release / version-sync workflow that produces the `chore(release): sync versions to X` PRs (see #3316, #3323 for the shape of the commit).\n- Whatever script that workflow calls to rewrite the versions (search for the `sync versions` commit-message template).\n- `Cargo.lock` — the artifact that goes stale.\n- The CI step that catches it lives in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, named \"Cargo.lock is in sync with the manifests\", and runs `cargo metadata --locked --format-version 1`.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n1. `git checkout 074124b9c` (or any commit between `543f5d486` and `074124b9c`).\n2. `cargo metadata --locked --format-version 1 > /dev/null` — fails, naming `stella-plugin`.\n3. `cargo metadata --format-version 1 > /dev/null && git diff Cargo.lock` — shows the single version line the sync should have written.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- The version-sync step regenerates `Cargo.lock` after rewriting the manifests (running `cargo metadata`/`cargo check --workspace --locked=false` and committing the result), so the sync PR is self-consistent by construction rather than by luck.\n- Adding a new workspace member and running the sync produces a lockfile that passes `cargo metadata --locked` — ideally proven by a test or a dry-run in the release workflow, since the current failure mode is invisible until it is already on `main`.\n- The sync workflow fails loudly if the lockfile it produces would not pass the CI check, rather than opening a PR that reds `main` on merge.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- `Cargo.lock` is tracked and `install.sh` builds with `--locked` (AGENTS.md § Gotchas), so it must stay committed and reproducible.\n- Do not fold this into an unrelated PR; #3333 is the one-line unblock and this is the durable fix.\n\nUnblocked by #3333.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3336[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"release version-sync leaves Cargo.lock stale for newly added crates, redding main"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
