    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n#3303's fix stamped the **silent custom-tool** success (exit 0, empty stdout) with an input-derived `sha256/8` in `crates/stella-tools/src/custom.rs::run_custom`, so distinct inputs no longer render byte-identical empty outputs. That was fix (a) of #3303 — harness-side, custom tools only. Two populations of the #3176 stagnation-hazard class remain, and only the detector-side fix (#3303's fix b, originally PR #3187's deliberately-untaken fix 2) can reach them:\n\n1. **MCP tools.** Third-party server outputs are relayed verbatim (`stella-mcp` → the registry decorator chain); Stella cannot stamp them. A server whose success responses are constant (an ack string, an empty result) converts a legitimate work loop into a stagnation kill exactly as the custom-tool empty-stdout case did.\n2. **Constant non-empty custom-tool stdout.** A script that prints the same bytes on every success (`echo done`) is the same hazard one byte away; the #3303 stamp fires only on *empty* stdout, deliberately, to keep the developer-API change minimal.\n\n## The fix under consideration\n\nDetector-side: weaken or exempt the output-keyed stagnation rung in `crates/stella-core/src/loop_detect.rs` (\"Consecutive calls to the SAME tool that all produced byte-identical output — whatever their arguments\") when the *arguments* differ across the run.\n\n**This trades a false positive for a false negative** — the exact blindness #3292 documents from the other direction — so any change here must be decided **jointly with #3292**, or the two fixes will fight. That joint design call is the actual work of this issue; the code change is small once decided.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- `stella-core` is I/O-free (AGENTS.md invariant #2): any detector change is pure logic over owned data, with property tests (`loop_detect` already has them).\n- Deterministic only — no timings in `ToolOutput` (#2706).\n- `loop_detect.rs` is not a god file; no baseline involved.\n\n## Verify / definition of done\n\nSynthesized `loop_detect` records: N consecutive calls to one tool with **differing arguments** and byte-identical outputs must no longer trip the rung (or must trip it later / under a stricter joint condition per the #3292 decision); N calls with **identical** arguments and identical outputs must still trip it. Property tests updated alongside.\n\nRefs #3303, #3292, #3176, #3187, #2706.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3328[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"loop_detect: output-keyed stagnation rung still kills legitimate loops over unstampable constant-output tools (MCP, constant-stdout scripts) — the detector-side half of #3303, decide jointly with #3292"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
