    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nAGENTS.md invariant #8 claims, of the provider-parity matrix:\n\n> Each provider id declares a posture on **every** axis and, for a controllable/opt-in/implicit/fallback posture, names the **witness test** proving it on the wire. Tests enforce each matrix from both sides: `stella-cli`'s config tests fail if a seeded provider lacks a row on any axis, and `stella-model`'s parity tests fail if a row's witness test no longer exists.\n\nThat is untrue for **`StreamFallbackPosture`** (#2686), and partly untrue for `OutputBudgetPosture`. The axis is declared and documented but carries **none** of the enforcement the other four carry, so nothing fails when it rots.\n\nVerified on `origin/main` (`crates/stella-model/src/provider_parity.rs`, `mod tests`):\n\n| Enforcement | cache | reasoning | overflow | output-budget | **stream-fallback** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `every_*_witness_test_exists_in_the_adapter_sources` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ **absent** |\n| `*_provider_ids_are_unique` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ **absent** |\n| covered by `all_axes_cover_the_same_provider_ids` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ⚠️ proxy only | ❌ **absent** |\n| `stella-cli` `every_seeded_provider_declares_*` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ **absent** |\n\n- The `stella-model` test module has `every_witness_test_exists_in_the_adapter_sources` (cache), `every_reasoning_witness_test_exists_in_the_adapter_sources`, `every_overflow_witness_test_exists_in_the_adapter_sources`, and `every_output_budget_witness_test_exists_in_the_adapter_sources` — and no stream-fallback equivalent.\n- `all_axes_cover_the_same_provider_ids` builds sets from `CACHE_POSTURE`, `REASONING_POSTURE`, and `OVERFLOW_POSTURE` only. `OUTPUT_BUDGET_POSTURE` gets a narrower proxy (`the_output_budget_axis_covers_every_provider_the_overflow_axis_does`); `STREAM_FALLBACK_POSTURE` gets nothing.\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/config/tests.rs` declares completeness tests for a cache, reasoning, overflow, and output-budget posture — none for stream-fallback.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThree failure modes are currently silent:\n\n1. **A new provider ships without a `StreamFallbackPosture` row.** Every other axis fails the `stella-cli` config test; this one does not, so the provider quietly has no declared streaming-recovery posture — the exact \"matrix hole\" shape invariant #8 exists to prevent, and the shape that let OpenRouter run with zero prompt caching for months.\n2. **A stream-fallback witness is renamed or deleted.** The row keeps naming a test that no longer exists, i.e. a declared proof that proves nothing. Every other axis catches this at test time.\n3. **Duplicate provider ids in `STREAM_FALLBACK_POSTURE`** go unnoticed; the lookup returns the first row and the second is dead.\n\n**This is latent today, not broken.** As of `origin/main`, all five matrices carry the same 10 provider ids (`anthropic, bedrock, deepseek, gemini, local, openai, openrouter, vertex, xai, zai`), and both declared stream-fallback witnesses exist:\n- `an_empty_stream_falls_back_to_a_non_streaming_request` — `crates/stella-model/src/zai/tests/stream_fallback.rs:137`\n- `a_stream_hung_before_its_first_byte_falls_back_to_a_non_streaming_request` — `crates/stella-model/src/zai/tests/stream_fallback.rs:96`\n\nSo this is a guard to add before the next provider or rename lands, not a live defect to chase.\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-model/src/provider_parity.rs` — the `mod tests` block (~L727-1010) holds every existing per-axis test; copy the `output_budget` trio, which is the newest and closest in shape.\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/config/tests.rs` — `every_seeded_provider_declares_an_output_budget_posture` (~L104) is the template for the missing CLI-side completeness test. **Note the file-size ratchet**: this file is near its baseline ceiling, and PR #3309 previously had to move these tests to a `config/tests/parity.rs` submodule for exactly this reason. Check `scripts/file-size-baseline.txt` before adding lines, and prefer a submodule split over growing the file (AGENTS.md § \"God files\").\n- `AGENTS.md` invariant #8 — the prose that currently over-claims.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n1. `every_stream_fallback_witness_test_exists_in_the_adapter_sources` in `provider_parity.rs`, skipping the non-witnessed posture arms exactly as the overflow/output-budget versions skip theirs.\n2. `stream_fallback_provider_ids_are_unique`.\n3. `all_axes_cover_the_same_provider_ids` extended to assert `cache == stream_fallback` **and** `cache == output_budget`, retiring the narrower output-budget proxy test if it becomes redundant.\n4. `every_seeded_provider_declares_a_stream_fallback_posture` on the `stella-cli` side.\n5. Invariant #8's enforcement sentence is true as written for all five axes (adjust prose or code until it is).\n\n## Witness\n\nEach new test must be shown to fail before it passes — the flip is cheap here and should be demonstrated, not asserted:\n\n- Witness-existence test: temporarily rename `an_empty_stream_falls_back_to_a_non_streaming_request` in `zai/tests/stream_fallback.rs`; the new test must fail naming the rotted row, and pass again on revert.\n- Uniqueness / coverage tests: temporarily duplicate or delete a `STREAM_FALLBACK_POSTURE` row and confirm the corresponding test fails.\n- CLI completeness test: temporarily drop the `xai` stream-fallback row and confirm the config test names it.\n\nRecord the observed failure output in the PR description (per CLAUDE.md, \"correctness is demonstrated or it is not claimed\"). This is a test-only change, so no behavior witness is required beyond these flips.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound while triaging PR #3309, which was closed as superseded by #3293 (both implemented OpenRouter 402 resilience; #3293's engine-level `OutputBudgetPosture` + `driver/output_budget_recovery.rs` shipped instead of #3309's adapter-level one-shot resend). #3309 had noticed and fixed this same enforcement gap in passing; that fix died with the PR, so it is filed here rather than left behind.\n\nRelated: #2686 (the axis itself), #2746 (extending the fallback to the other dialects — that PR will add rows this guard should be protecting).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3322[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"provider parity: the StreamFallbackPosture axis carries none of the enforcement the other four axes carry"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
