    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## The blind spot\n\n`loop_detect` has four detectors and every one of them keys on something being **identical**: exact repeat and short cycle key on identical *inputs*, stagnation keys on identical *outputs*, interleaved repeat keys on an identical (input, output) pair recurring. A model that grinds unproductively while varying both is invisible to all four.\n\n## The trace\n\n`~/.arenabench/matches/5a38720c145f/jobs/5a38720c145f-stella-glm-5-2-via-openrouter-bare-loop/extract-moves-from-video__3AqwMdY/agent/stella-events.jsonl`\n\nCensus of that trial:\n\n- 62 `tool_start` events, **all 62 are `bash`** — no other tool called at any point\n- 62 distinct tool inputs (nothing repeats, so detectors 1, 2 and 4 never arm)\n- **62 distinct outputs** (so detector 3, stagnation, never arms either)\n- the turn ran to its step ceiling and solved nothing\n\nSo this is not a tuning problem with an existing detector. It is a class none of them covers: *varied inputs producing varied outputs that nonetheless carry no new information*.\n\n## Why this is not a one-line fix\n\n\"Unproductive\" needs a definition the engine can compute without a model call, and a false positive here **aborts work that was going fine** — strictly worse than the grind it prevents. Candidate signals, none yet validated:\n\n- **novelty collapse** — the fraction of output lines already seen earlier in the window. Grinding tends to re-derive the same content with cosmetic variation (same error, same listing, same failing assertion) so byte-difference is high while information-difference is near zero.\n- **workspace immobility** — no file mutated over N steps. Cheaper and sharper, but after the 12-tool purge every mutation goes through `bash`, so it has to be inferred rather than observed from the tool name.\n- **plan immobility** — the model's stated next action not changing across steps.\n\nAny of these needs a labelled study before it can ship: take the traces we have, hand-label the windows that were genuinely stuck versus genuinely working, and show the candidate metric separates them with a threshold that has no false positives on the working population. That study is the actual work item here — not the detector.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n1. A labelled corpus of trace windows (stuck / working) drawn from `~/.arenabench/matches/**/agent/stella-events.jsonl`, committed as fixtures.\n2. A pure detector in `crates/stella-core/src/loop_detect.rs` matching the existing four in shape (plain synchronous function over owned data, property-tested).\n3. Evidence in the PR that it fires on the stuck population and **never** on the working one — the false-positive side is the one that matters.\n4. The `extract-moves-from-video` trace above as a named witness fixture.\n\n## Related\n\n- The task-deadline signal now shipped (`crates/stella-core/src/driver/deadline_notice.rs`) mitigates a *different* half of the same loss — it tells the model to submit what it has as the wall approaches. It does not fire here: that trial had **0 of 62** budget ticks with a deadline armed, so a grind with no deadline configured is still unbounded by anything but the step ceiling. See #2957.\n- #1851 (the stagnation detector, which closed the previous blind spot in this family).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3292[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"loop detection is blind to varied-input, varied-output grinding — 62 bash calls, 62 distinct outputs, no detector fires"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
