    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nFive tests in `arenabench/tests/test_sut.py` (`TestCheckoutDiscovery::test_the_launch_wires_the_adapter_from_that_same_checkout`, `TestTwoSeatsRaceTwoBuilds::test_two_seats_launch_two_binaries_and_record_them`, and all three of `TestAPinIsObservedOnce`) fail identically on `main` and on every branch, on any host whose `/usr/bin/python3` is the stock macOS 3.9:\n\n```\narenabench.adapter.AdapterUnavailableError: /usr/bin/python3 cannot build a\nStella seat: `import arenabench.harbor_agent` failed with\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tomllib'.\n```\n\n`tomllib` arrived in Python 3.11, so the adapter preflight is doing its job — the defect is that these *tests* reach the real preflight against the real system interpreter instead of a faked one, making the local suite red for a reason that has nothing to do with the code under test. Verified 2026-08-14: same five failures on `main` (a4b87649a) and on `worktree-arenabench-issue-batch`; the other 630+ tests pass.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nA permanently-red slice of the suite trains everyone to read failures as environmental — which is exactly how a real regression in `sut.py` would be walked past. It also breaks `pytest tests` as a pre-push confidence signal on macOS, the primary dev platform.\n\n## Where\n\n- `arenabench/tests/test_sut.py` — the five tests above\n- `arenabench/arenabench/adapter.py` — the preflight they hit (the `cannot build a Stella seat` error)\n- Other tests in the same file already avoid this, so a faking pattern exists in-file to copy.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nThe five tests either fake the adapter preflight (preferred — match the file's existing fakes) or skip with a named reason when the probed interpreter lacks the adapter deps (weaker; a skip hides the seam). `python3 -m pytest tests/test_sut.py` is green on a stock macOS host with no `uv sync` performed.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The preflight's fail-closed behavior at *launch* is correct and load-bearing (#2098 family) — only the tests' reach into the real interpreter is at issue.\n- Repro: any macOS host, `cd arenabench && python3 -m pytest tests/test_sut.py -q`."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3282[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: five test_sut.py tests fail on any stock macOS host — the suite probes the real /usr/bin/python3, which lacks tomllib"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
