    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`.stella/rules/ctx.stella.dependency-license-allowlist.toml` is an **active** published context record whose rationale comment (lines ~15–21) justifies omitting `guard_tool` by reasoning about `edit_file`/`apply_edits`/`write_file` coverage — tool names that no longer exist after the purge. The rule itself (never widen `deny.toml` without a licensing decision) still stands and its path-only guard still works; only the stated *reason* is void.\n\n## Fix\n\nSupersede the record through the proper lifecycle (`stella context` tooling; `promotions.jsonl` is a hash-chained ledger verified by `stella context validate` in CI — no hand edits). The revised rationale should be crate-agnostic, e.g.: the guard matches on path, so every path-naming tool — MCP or workspace custom — is covered; a shell-shaped tool carries no path and is deliberately out of scope.\n\nPrecedent: `ctx.macanderson.stella.verify-done-shadow-worktree` was retired via ledger seq 2 on PR #3244.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nThe superseding record is active with a truthful rationale, the old revision is superseded on the ledger, and `stella context validate` is green.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3269[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"context: the dependency-license-allowlist record's guard-tool rationale names deleted tools — supersede through the ledger"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
