    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## The problem\n\nOn 2026-08-14 `main` went red at `868ad77e0`: `stella-core` failed to compile, taking down `cargo clippy -D warnings` and `cargo test` for the whole workspace (run [31775648996](https://github.com/macanderson/stella/actions/runs/31775648996)). Neither contributing PR was faulty, and both were green on their own branch.\n\nThe mechanism, entirely inside `crates/stella-core/src/driver/restore.rs`:\n\n- **#3244** (12-tool purge) replaced the `MapTools` test executor with the tool-less `SkillTools`, and deleted the `Arc`/`Mutex`/`HashMap` imports it needed, plus the now-unused `ToolCall`/`ToolOutput` imports and the `RESTORE_CALL_ID` constant.\n- **#3253** (overflow-summarizer headroom) added two new witnesses to the same test module that construct `MapTools { files: .., active: .. }`.\n\nNeither branch's diff contains the other's lines, so git merged both with no conflict to report, and the composed file references a struct and three imports that no longer exist.\n\nFixed by #3265. This issue is about the guard, not the fix.\n\n## Why no guard caught it\n\n`scripts/check-deleted-tests.sh` (CI, `pull_request` only) exists for exactly this class — a PR silently removing something another PR is concurrently depending on — but it compares **`#[test]` / `#[tokio::test]` function names** across the base tree and the merge result. What went missing here was a *test helper*: a `struct`, its `impl`, and its `use` statements. No test function disappeared, so the guard was silent and correct by its own contract.\n\nThe generalization is uncomfortable: **any item a concurrently-added test depends on can be deleted by a clean merge**, and the only thing that catches it is compiling the merge result. CI does compile the merge result — but on `pull_request`, against a base that did not yet contain the other PR. Both PRs passed that check honestly, before the other landed.\n\nRelated but not the same: #2495 (a clean merge silently reverting a measurement-tuned constant). Same family — \"textually clean, semantically broken\" — different payload.\n\n## What \"done\" looks like\n\nDecide and implement one of these, or argue in the issue for a third:\n\n1. **Merge queue.** The only option that actually compiles the composition before it lands. Also the heaviest; check whether the repo's branch protection and Actions budget can carry it. Note `enforce_admins` is off and auto-merge is on, so today an admin merge can land a pair that was never built together.\n2. **Post-merge fast alarm on `main`.** A cheap `cargo check --workspace --all-targets` job triggered on push to `main`, distinct from the full gate, whose only job is to shout within ~2 minutes rather than ~20. Does not prevent the break; shortens the red window, which is most of the cost — a red `main` reds every open PR.\n3. **Widen `check-deleted-tests.sh` to deleted test-scope items.** Extend the comparison from `#[test]` fn names to items inside `#[cfg(test)]` modules (`struct`/`fn`/`impl`/`use`) and require a PR that removes one to name it, the same way a deleted test must be named. Cheapest of the three; catches this exact shape and nothing broader.\n\nWhichever is chosen, the definition of done is: **a PR that deletes a `#[cfg(test)]` helper, merged alongside a PR that adds a use of it, cannot leave `main` uncompilable without something failing first.**\n\n## Verify\n\nThe repro is a real pair, so it can be replayed:\n\n```sh\ngit checkout 868ad77e0\ncargo clippy -p stella-core --all-targets   # 2 errors: unused imports, dead RESTORE_CALL_ID\ncargo test -p stella-core --lib             # 10 errors: MapTools / Arc / Mutex / HashMap not in scope\n```\n\nBase commits: `54233fd68` (#3244) and `62707541d` (#3253); neither is red alone.\n\n## Constraints already discovered\n\n- `check-deleted-tests.sh` runs in CI on `pull_request` only, deliberately — locally there is no second tree to compare (AGENTS.md § the witness-test contract).\n- Adding a workflow: `ci.yml` ignores `docs/**` and `*.md`; a new job that must run on every push needs its own trigger, and the repo has precedent for a separate file per disjoint path set (`wire-schema.yml`, `deck-fit.yml`).\n- A new `make gate` step must be added to `GATE_STEPS` in the `Makefile` **and** to AGENTS.md's and CONTRIBUTING.md's lists, or `gate-parity` fails.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3267[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"gate: a clean merge can delete a test helper another PR is concurrently using, and nothing catches it until main is red"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
