    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nThe **CodeQL** workflow's latest run on `main` is a **failure**, dated **2026-07-17** (run `44895f906`). Nothing has run it successfully since. A security scanner that has been red for roughly a month is, in practice, a scanner that is not running — and nothing surfaces that, because CodeQL is not part of the required gate.\n\nIts logs have already expired, so the failure cause is not recoverable from the run itself:\n\n```\ngh run view 29559563152 --log-failed   # returns nothing; retention window passed\n```\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThis repository takes supply-chain and security posture seriously enough to gate on `cargo deny` (advisories, bans, sources, licenses) and to run `dependency-review` on every PR. CodeQL is the static-analysis half of that posture, and it has been silently absent. The failure mode is the same one AGENTS.md describes for under-reported gate steps: a reader sees a configured scanner and believes it is working.\n\n## Verify\n\n```sh\ngh run list --repo macanderson/stella --workflow CodeQL --limit 5 \\\n  --json conclusion,createdAt,headSha\n```\n\n## Definition of done\n\n1. CodeQL is re-run on current `main` and the failure reproduced (or shown to be gone).\n2. If it still fails, the cause is fixed — most likely an autobuild failure on a Rust workspace this size, in which case the fix is an explicit build step or restricting the analysed languages.\n3. A green CodeQL run exists on `main`.\n4. A decision is recorded on whether CodeQL should block merges or stay advisory — and if advisory, something must make a sustained red **visible**, since a month of silence is the defect this issue documents.\n\n## Context\n\nFound while auditing the latest run of every workflow on `main` (2026-08-14). The required gate — `ci`, `docs-guards`, `wire-schema`, `deck-fit`, `containment-posture` — is green; four non-gate workflows were red, of which this is the oldest. The others: #3009 (nightly-bench), the `live-smoke` issue filed alongside this one, and `Dependabot Updates`, fixed by #3258.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3260[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"CodeQL has been failing on main since 2026-07-17 and nothing surfaces it — the scanner is configured but not running"[m
