    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`live-smoke`'s latest run on `main` is a **failure**, and has been since 2026-08-10 (head `b77d0f17b`, run 08-10T08:23Z). One of sixteen provider smokes fails:\n\n```\nthread 'anthropic_smoke' (4568) panicked at crates/stella-model/tests/live_smoke.rs:632:19:\nanthropic live smoke did not return a parseable 200 — could be a genuine wire-shape\nregression OR an [expired key / quota]\ntest anthropic_smoke ... FAILED\ntest result: FAILED. 15 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out\n```\n\nThe other 15 provider smokes pass, which is what makes this worth a look rather than a shrug: whatever is wrong is specific to the Anthropic adapter or its credential, not to the harness.\n\n## Why it is not self-diagnosing\n\nThe panic message itself names the ambiguity — it **cannot distinguish** a genuine wire-shape regression in `crates/stella-model/src/anthropic.rs` from an expired/quota-limited `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` secret. That is the first thing to settle, and it cannot be settled from the log alone. This is the \"evidence consistent with both answers is not evidence\" case from CLAUDE.md.\n\n## Verify / reproduce\n\n```sh\n# with a known-good ANTHROPIC_API_KEY exported\ncargo test -p stella-model --test live_smoke anthropic_smoke -- --nocapture\n```\n\nThen read the actual response body at `crates/stella-model/tests/live_smoke.rs:632` — the assertion should be made to print the status code and body prefix so the next failure distinguishes the two causes without a human re-running it.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n1. The cause is named: expired credential, quota, or a real wire-shape change.\n2. If it is a credential, the repository secret is rotated and the run is green.\n3. If it is a wire-shape regression, the adapter is fixed with a witness test.\n4. **Either way**, the assertion at `live_smoke.rs:632` is widened to print status + body prefix on failure, so this test never again reports a diagnosis it cannot support.\n\n## Context\n\n`live-smoke` is opt-in and spends real money, so it is not in the required gate — which is why a 4-day-old red went unnoticed. Found while auditing the latest run of every workflow on `main`; the required gate is green.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3259[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"live-smoke: anthropic_smoke has failed on main since 2026-08-10, and the assertion cannot say whether it is a wire regression or an expired key"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
