    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nThe two halves of record retirement disagree about where an archived revision lives, so following the documented retirement flow leaves `stella context validate` — which CI runs on every PR (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, step \"stella context validate\") — permanently red.\n\n- `stella ingest --refresh <file>` retires a claim the source no longer asserts by appending the hash-chained `Retired` ledger event **and rewriting the record file in place** with `status = \"archived\"`, re-stamped (`crates/stella-cli/src/ingest_cmd/refresh.rs::retire`, `record_retirement`). The file stays in `.stella/rules/`; its own test `an_archived_record_is_not_retired_twice` relies on it staying there.\n- `stella context validate` counts **every loaded record whose disposition is not selected** as blocking (`crates/stella-cli/src/context_cmd/validate.rs::print_blocked`: `!entry.disposition.is_selected()`), and an archived record loads with disposition reason \"its status is archived\". So the freshly archived file makes validate exit non-zero with \"1 record(s) must not steer anything until this is resolved\" — forever, since the file never changes again.\n\nObserved on 2026-08-14 while retiring `ctx.macanderson.stella.verify-done-shadow-worktree` for PR #3244 (the #3238 follow-up): with the archived revision in place validate reported both the refuted probe and \"Not steering … its status is archived\" and exited 1; deleting the file from `.stella/rules/` (ledger event kept) made validate exit 0. That deletion is the workaround PR #3244 shipped.\n\n## Repro\n\n1. Take any published record in `.stella/rules/<lineage>.toml`.\n2. Set `status = \"archived\"`, `supersedes_record_id` to its own `record_id`, re-stamp (what `refresh.rs::retire` does), and append the `Retired` ledger event.\n3. `cargo run -p stella-cli -- context validate` → exit 1, \"must not steer anything until this is resolved\".\n\n## What \"done\" looks like\n\nDecide which side is right and make the two agree, with a witness test that a completed retirement leaves validate green:\n\n- **Option A** — validate treats `status = \"archived\"` as a *resolved* disposition (reported informationally, not counted in `print_blocked`). Archived files stay in place as the audit trail refresh intends.\n- **Option B** — retirement moves the archived revision out of the loader's directories (e.g. `.stella/rules/archive/`) or deletes it, and the refresh tests/spec are updated to match; validate stays strict.\n\nConstraints discovered: validate's exit contract is deliberately \"any loaded record not steering fails\" because a refuted claim carries no finding (see the comment on `print_blocked`); whatever changes must keep the refuted-active case failing. The ledger side is fine — `parse_and_verify` accepts the `Retired` event and the fold revokes grants correctly.\n\nRefs #2728 (retirement/supersession ledger vocabulary), #3238 (the retirement that surfaced this), #3244 (the PR carrying the workaround)."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3254[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"`context validate` exits non-zero on an archived record left in `.stella/rules/`, but `ingest --refresh` archives in place — retirement cannot end green"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
