    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nAll three known dispatch sites now carry both halves of the starvation\nmachinery (`crates/stella-core/src/starvation.rs`): `metered_raw_call`\n(`crates/stella-pipeline/src/pipeline/raw_usage.rs`, #2128),\n`complete_standalone` (`crates/stella-cli/src/accounted_call.rs`, #2174 /\n#2444), and the overflow summarizer (`crates/stella-core/src/driver/restore.rs`,\n#2503). But each carries its own copy of the *pattern* — pad the contract with\n`with_reasoning_headroom`, retry once at `starved_retry_cap` — and nothing\nmechanical prevents a **fourth** call site from being written tomorrow with a\nbare `max_output_tokens` and no retry. That is exactly how sites two and three\nhappened: each was written before the machinery existed at its layer, and each\nwas found by a production failure rather than a test.\n\n#2503 flagged this explicitly: \"What must not happen is a fourth bare cap\nappearing later with nothing to stop it — consider whether `run_accounted_call`\nis the right place for the retry, since it is the seam all three sites already\nshare.\"\n\n## Why #2503's fix did not resolve this\n\nThe #2503 PR deliberately kept the retry local to the summarizer, mirroring the\ntwo existing chokepoints, because moving it into `run_accounted_call`\n(`crates/stella-core/src/accounted_call.rs`) is a behavior change for every\ncaller and both existing chokepoints already own their retries with\nrole-specific cost accounting (`superseded_cost` reporting differs per site).\nCentralizing would also need care with the receipt seam: a retry inside\n`run_accounted_call` would re-emit the same `ReceiptContext` internally, and\neach site currently decides its own receipt/cost semantics.\n\n## What to decide\n\nTwo candidate shapes; the maintainer should pick one (or reject both with a\nreason):\n\n1. **Move the starved-retry into `run_accounted_call`.** The seam all sites\n   share. A retry there fires only when `starved_of_output(&result)` and\n   `starved_retry_cap(request.max_output_tokens)` says more room could help —\n   both pure predicates from `starvation.rs`. Existing per-site retries would\n   be deleted (they become unreachable: the inner retry recovers first). Cost\n   reporting must then surface both attempts' spend through the single returned\n   `CompletionResult` or a widened return type — the part that makes this a\n   real design decision rather than a mechanical move. `StepUsage` per attempt\n   already happens naturally since the retry re-dispatches internally.\n2. **A guard instead of a mechanism.** A gate script (the\n   `check-typed-errors.py` shape) that finds `max_output_tokens: Some(` /\n   `CompletionRequest {` construction sites outside the three blessed modules\n   and fails when a new one appears without either `with_reasoning_headroom` or\n   an allowlist entry citing a reason. Cruder, but zero behavior change.\n\n## Verify\n\n- Option 1: the three sites' existing starvation witnesses\n  (`a_call_starved_by_its_own_reasoning_is_retried_with_room` in\n  `crates/stella-cli/src/accounted_call.rs`, the #2128 tests in\n  `crates/stella-pipeline`, and\n  `a_starved_summarizer_is_retried_with_room_and_never_latches` in\n  `crates/stella-core/src/driver/restore.rs`) must keep passing with the\n  per-site retry code deleted.\n- Option 2: a new gate step, wired into `GATE_STEPS` in the `Makefile` (which\n  updates AGENTS.md/CONTRIBUTING.md via the `gate-parity` contract) — plus a\n  witness that a synthetic bare-cap site fails it.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- `starvation.rs` stays the single home of the constants (two copies is how\n  #2128's fix missed `complete_standalone`, per its module doc).\n- `run_accounted_call` is library code in `stella-core` — typed errors,\n  no panics (invariant 5); budget aborts stay at safe boundaries\n  (invariant 6).\n\nRefs #2503, #2444, #2174, #2128."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3250[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Nothing stops a fourth bare-cap dispatch site — decide the structural guard for reasoning starvation"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
