    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Outcome\n\n`search` is the **one way an agent finds things** in a workspace, and the answer it returns is honest: it ranks by what the query means, it says plainly what it can and cannot do on the host it is running on, it can see every kind of workspace truth, and the budget it advertises is the budget it spends.\n\n`search` is one of the tools that stays in the core surface, so its quality is load-bearing — on a host with no embedder configured (the normal case on a bench container) the fallback rungs are the *only* rungs, and they are what the benchmark actually measures.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n1. **Ranking is honest on the no-embedder path.** Prose queries rank by relevance, not by substring coincidence or per-file symbol count.\n2. **The schema tells the truth about the host.** The description does not promise meaning-matching that an embedder-less host cannot deliver.\n3. **Nothing in the workspace is beyond it.** Config, context records, and other non-code truth are reachable on some rung.\n4. **The budget bounds the rendered answer**, not an estimate of it.\n5. **The relevance constants are measured**, not provisional.\n6. **The enrichment facets say what they are** — a name-based lookup is labelled as one and does not silently conflate same-named symbols.\n7. **Caching never serves a stale cross-file fact.**\n\n## Children\n\n- #3063 — spec: search, one way to find things, with budget-driven graph enrichment and a tunable depth\n- #3138 — the name rung mis-ranks prose queries (no stemming, symbol-count bias)\n- #3139 — the schema description promises meaning-matching an embedder-less host cannot deliver\n- #3140 — the character budget bounds an estimate, not the rendered answer\n- #3142 — the callers facet conflates same-named symbols across files and languages\n- #3162 — context records and other TOML are unsearchable on every rung\n- #3184 — index C++ with a dedicated tree-sitter-cpp grammar\n- #3196 — gather cache: cross-file facets can serve one generation stale\n- #3198 — context cache: the domain-grouped, cross-session, git-authority half of #3163\n- #3096 — calibrate the search relevance constants from measurement\n- #3097 — the three #3089 retrieval witnesses: chunk search is unproven end to end\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3248[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Epic: search is the one way to find things, and it ranks honestly"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
