    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nThe sub-agent primitive was designed for cheap delegation, and one production\nsurface never got the routing. `stella-core`'s own docs say a child \"is very\noften served by a *different* model than its parent — a cheap searcher, a\ncross-family verifier\" (`crates/stella-core/src/subagent.rs`, the\n`SubAgentHost` doc), and the seam exists: `SubAgentHost::new(provider)` takes\nany provider, and `SubAgentSpec.effort` overrides the child's reasoning\neffort per spawn.\n\nBut the `task` tool's session dispatcher pins none of it:\n`crates/stella-cli/src/subagent.rs::install_for_session` builds the\ndispatcher over `Arc::from(crate::agent::build_provider(cfg)?)` — the session\ndefault — with `crate::agent::engine_config_for(cfg)`, and the `task` tool's\nspec (`crates/stella-tools/src/subagent.rs::execute`) leaves\n`effort: None`, which `run_child_turn` resolves to the parent's effort\n(`crates/stella-core/src/subagent.rs`, the `effort: spec.effort.or(self.config.effort)`\nline). So every interactive/one-shot research child runs the full worker\nmodel at the parent's effort tier — a session on an expensive model at\n`xhigh` pays worker prices for grep-and-read work.\n\nThe contrast that shows this is a gap and not a design choice: the\n*pipeline's* research children are role-routed. `pipeline/research_stage.rs`\nresolves `ModelCallRole::Research` through the roster and hands the resolved\nprovider to `SubAgentHost::new` — a researcher pin reaches those children.\nThe `task` tool's children are the only sub-agent population with no routing\nseam at all.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe `task` tool's whole premise is context economy (its report caps at 8k\nchars precisely so delegation is cheaper than doing the reads inline). The\ntoken side is managed; the price side is not. Delegation multiplies model\ncalls (up to 16 steps per child, siblings concurrent), so an unroutable child\npopulation multiplies cost at exactly the surface built to reduce it.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\n- Add a worker-adjacent routing input for task-tool children — e.g. an\n  `agents.researcher.*` pin (the roster vocabulary already exists) or a\n  `context.subagent_model` setting — resolved once in `install_for_session`.\n- Resolution failure degrades softly to the session default with a notice,\n  exactly like `pin_role` in `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/engine.rs` (a\n  missing credential must not make delegation unavailable).\n- Default behavior with no config stays byte-identical: session default\n  provider, inherited effort.\n- Consider whether the child's default effort should drop a tier when the\n  parent runs `xhigh`/`max` — a maintainer call; if declined, say why in the\n  resolving code's doc.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A configured pin routes `task`-tool children to that model (and optionally\n  effort); witness: a test on `install_for_session` (or the dispatcher it\n  builds) that the child engine is constructed over the configured ref, and\n  that no config yields the session default — the second half must pass on\n  today's code, the first half must fail.\n- `StepUsage` from routed children carries the routed model so `stella stats`\n  prices them correctly (it already carries the serving provider's model —\n  verify, don't assume).\n- Settings docs updated where the key lands.\n\n## Constraints and prior art\n\n- Invariant 8 (provider parity is declared): a routed child provider is an\n  existing adapter with parity rows — no new axis needed.\n- Budget accounting is already correct for any provider (the carve/settle\n  path in `crates/stella-cli/src/subagent.rs` meters whatever runs).\n- Related, not duplicate: #2632 measures whether delegation helps the bare\n  loop at all; this issue is about what delegation costs when it runs.\n\nFound during a token-efficiency audit (the one that fixed #2476).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3240[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"sub-agents: the task tool has no model routing — every child rides the session-default worker at inherited effort"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
