    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`crates/stella-media` is orphaned by the tool purge: its only consuming surface was the generate_image / generate_video / poll_video / generate_svg tools in stella-tools, which are deleted. Nothing in the workspace links it except possibly stale references; its README and module docs describe the deleted tools as its consumers.\n\n## Decision needed\n\nKeep the crate as a library awaiting a future surface (MCP server? a media-capable custom tool host?) or delete it from the workspace. If deleted: remove the workspace member, its `[workspace.dependencies]` entries with no other consumer, and sweep `AGENTS.md`'s crate routing table and any remaining docs rows. If kept: rewrite its README boundary section to name its actual (currently absent) consumer honestly and file the wiring issue.\n\n## Related orphans from the same purge (bundle or split as appropriate)\n\n- `crates/stella-graph`: `importer_paths` (impacted-scope selection), the storage-map extraction plane (built for the deleted schema gate), and the chunk-vector plane lost their tool consumers. CLI mount (`stella search`, `stella init`) and CGP recall remain. The dead public API needs a keep/remove decision.\n- `crates/stella-tui` ISSUES tab (`src/views/issues.rs`, `IssueRow`): no built-in feeder remains (tracker backends died with stella-tools). Keep (MCP-fed future) or delete the tab.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nEach named surface either has a consumer again, is deleted, or its README/docs state its real status with a tracking issue for the wiring.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3236[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"workspace: stella-media, stella-graph dead surfaces, and the TUI ISSUES tab lost their consumers — keep or delete"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
