    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Deferred out of #3102 by the maintainer's own text (\"that trade deserves its own issue and its own argument\"), filed so the deferral is tracked rather than lost.\n\n## Problem\n\n`crates/stella-graph/src/workspace_ignore.rs:63` returns no rules at all when `root/.git` is absent, so a directory that carries its own `.gitignore` but is not a git repository — an extracted tarball, a bench container's `/app` — has its own ignore declaration ignored and is walked with only the hardcoded deny-list filtering it.\n\nThe `.git` gate itself is **not** the bug and must not be removed: the doc comment and the test `a_non_repository_ignores_nothing_even_inside_a_repository` pin it deliberately. Without the gate, a scratch directory under a `$HOME` dotfiles repo whose `.gitignore` says `*` would inherit rules nobody wrote for it and the caller would go silently blind. Removing the gate is a regression, not a fix.\n\n## The narrow gap to close\n\nHonour the workspace's **own** `.gitignore` (the file at `root/.gitignore`) when `root/.git` is absent, **without** inheriting any ancestor's rules. The module's stated position is that \"the resolution is `git`'s own, not a reimplementation\" — it shells out to `git check-ignore`/equivalent rather than re-implementing pattern semantics, because a subtly-wrong second ignore engine fails silently. Whatever design closes the gap has to either keep that property (e.g. `git -c core.excludesFile= check-ignore --no-index`-style invocation rooted at the workspace, if one exists that works without a repository) or make the argument for a bounded exception explicitly in the module docs.\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-graph/src/workspace_ignore.rs` (the gate at ~line 63, the module doc stating the no-reimplementation position, and its tests)\n- `crates/stella-graph/src/walk.rs` (the consumer, `walk_indexable`)\n- Related history: #2360 extended real-gitignore consultation to `walk_indexable`.\n\n## Repro / verify\n\n1. `mkdir /tmp/ws && cd /tmp/ws` (no `git init`).\n2. Write `.gitignore` containing `generated/`, and put a large parseable file under `generated/`.\n3. `stella init` — today `generated/` is indexed; done means it is excluded, while a workspace with no `.gitignore` at all keeps today's behavior, and the existing ancestor-inheritance tests stay green unchanged.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nA witness test in `workspace_ignore.rs` (or `walk.rs`) proving a root-level `.gitignore` is honoured in a non-repository workspace AND that an ancestor repository's rules are still not inherited — both sides, since the second property is the reason the gate exists."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3204[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"workspace_ignore: a workspace with its own .gitignore but no .git is walked unfiltered"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
