    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nAfter #3110's fix, a successful mutation renders its diff inline under the\n`tool_result` entry — but the `file_change` event still renders as its own\ncompact-JSON transcript row (`arenabench/arenabench/transcript.py::_entries_for`,\nthe `kind in (\"file_change\", \"commit\", \"task_update\", \"loop_detected\")` arm):\n2000 capped characters of `json.dumps` whose `diff` field is the same bytes,\nJSON-escaped, directly above the readable render. The transcript now shows every\nmutation's diff twice, once as noise.\n\nThat PR left the row byte-identical on purpose: the JSON dump is currently the\nonly place a diff survives when the correlation cannot be made — a mutating\n`file_change` produced by a tool outside the deck's `is_file_mutation` four\n(`write_file`/`edit_file`/`apply_edits`/`delete_file`), or a stream whose\n`tool_start` never arrived. Reshaping it is a presentation decision with an\ninformation-loss edge, not a mechanical dedupe.\n\n## What \"done\" looks like\n\n- Decide the row's shape and implement it. The parity reference: the deck\n  renders **no** `file_change` transcript row at all — `crates/stella-tui/src/model.rs`\n  routes the event to the Files panel and the inline diff. A reasonable arena\n  shape: a quiet structured row (title `file change · modified <path>`, meta\n  `{path, kind, added, removed}`, no raw diff bytes in the body) for a mutation\n  whose diff was claimed by a result entry, keeping the diff visible (as a\n  proper diff body, not escaped JSON) when nothing claimed it.\n- The correlation contract in `arenabench/tests/test_transcript_diff.py` keeps\n  passing untouched; a new test pins whichever row shape is chosen.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/transcript.py` — `_entries_for`, the `file_change`\n  recording arm (added by #3110's PR) and the compact-row arm below it.\n- `arenabench/ui/components/arena/transcript-page.tsx` — `file_change` currently\n  falls through to the default plain-body arm; a structured row wants its own arm.\n\n## Verify\n\n`cd arenabench && uv run --with pytest --no-project pytest -q tests/test_transcript_diff.py`\nand the fixture pattern in that file (write a `stella-events.jsonl` with\n`tool_start` → `file_change` → `tool_result`).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3200[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench transcript: the file_change row repeats a diff the result row now renders"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
