    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`crates/stella-graph/README.md` has drifted from the tree, in three spots. Stale prose is treated as a bug in review (AGENTS.md § Code style), and two shipped changes (#3095 markdown indexing, #3103 markdown link edges + setext) widened the gap.\n\n1. **Key concepts** opens with \"Ten `Language` variants — Rust, Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Tsx, Sql, Go, Java, C, Php\". There are eleven: `Language::Markdown` (`crates/stella-graph/src/lang.rs`) has existed since #3095, is grammarless (line scan in `src/markdown.rs`), and now also produces import edges (#3103). The \"nine grammar crates\" framing needs a sentence for the grammarless eleventh, and `md`/`markdown` belongs in the extension list.\n2. **Layout table** omits files it should route readers to: `src/markdown.rs` (sections + link extraction), `src/rust_resolve.rs` (#443 module-tree resolution), `src/vectors.rs` + `src/vectors/` (the semantic index), `src/workspace_ignore.rs`, and the `src/store/` submodule dir. Compare `ls crates/stella-graph/src` against the table.\n3. **God files section** says \"`src/parse.rs` is approaching it at 1474 lines today\" — it is 1494 as of #3103's PR, six lines under the 1500 ratchet. Either update the number or (better) drop it and keep only the warning, since a count in prose goes stale by design — the same reasoning AGENTS.md applies to baseline ceilings.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nOne docs PR updating `crates/stella-graph/README.md`: eleven languages with Markdown's grammarless status stated, a Layout row for each missing file, and the parse.rs sentence made count-free or current. No code changes. Verify with `ls crates/stella-graph/src` vs the table, and `rg -n 'Ten .Language. variants|1474' crates/stella-graph/README.md` returning nothing."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3199[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"stella-graph README drift: language list says ten (Markdown is eleventh), Layout table omits five files, parse.rs line count stale"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
