    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n#3163 was closed by the smallest coherent slice: a session-lifetime, in-process, per-file gathered-context cache inside the `search` tool (`crates/stella-tools/src/search/cache.rs`), keyed by `(path, sha256(file bytes))`, bounded at 256 LRU entries. The issue's fuller proposal remains unbuilt and this is its tracking handoff:\n\n- **Cross-session persistence**: the issue targets re-gathers \"across the sessions of a team working the same tree\" — that needs a store under `.stella/private/` (`stella-context`/`stella-store` territory), consumed by the tool through a port (invariant 1), not the in-process map that dies with the session.\n- **Domain grouping**: `.stella/domains.toml` (written by `stella init`) as the grouping key, and the unit a warm pass could pre-gather.\n- **Git as invalidation authority for persisted entries**: a persisted entry outlives the process, so \"same bytes\" needs an identity that is cheap to check at load — the issue sketches last-change commit shas per file with a batched `git ls-tree`/diff walk per generation, and an explicit dirty-file bypass. (In-process, the content hash made the dirty case a non-issue; on disk it returns.)\n- **Disclosure**: the issue asks that an answer assembled from cache say so if that ever affects fidelity; the in-process slice never affects source-derived fidelity (source is re-read fresh) but a persisted cache may need the disclosure line.\n\n## Where the seam is today\n\n- `crates/stella-tools/src/search/enrich.rs::gathered_neighborhood` — the single gather point; a persistent tier slots in behind the same function.\n- `crates/stella-tools/src/search/cache.rs` — the identity choice and its rationale, plus the precision boundary (#3196 tracks the cross-file staleness half).\n- `crates/stella-tools/src/search.rs::report_with` — where the cache is threaded and locked.\n\n## Constraints discovered\n\n- The heavy per-call costs in `search` are the embedding round trips and the `index_all` catch-up pass, both out of scope for the gather cache — a persisted gather cache saves SQLite reads, so measure before building (the issue's own metric: graph reads per call, wall clock).\n- Invariant 7 (byte-stable answers): a cache hit must render byte-identically to the miss that populated it — the golden test shape exists in `crates/stella-tools/src/search/cache.rs::tests`.\n- Invariant 2: keep the decision logic pure; I/O stays behind the port.\n\n## Done\n\nEither the persisted, domain-grouped tier exists behind the `gathered_neighborhood` seam with the measurements justifying it, or a written decision on #3163's thread that the session-lifetime cache is where this stops.\n\nRefs #3163, #3196, #3154, #3162."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3198[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"search context cache: the domain-grouped, cross-session, git-authority half of #3163"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
