    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench cloud fetch` (assembly path) printed for run `fivetools2`:\n\n> !! 10 distinct provenance records across the run's trials — the slices did not all measure the same apparatus. Read them before quoting a number.\n\nChecked directly: all 11 `provenance.json` files under the fetched tree agree exactly on `sut_commit`, `sut_sha256`, `tool_set_seats`, `arenabench_version`, and `harbor_version` — one signature, 11 records. The apparatus WAS uniform; the warning cried wolf.\n\nA cloud run slices one match into one (task, seat) trial per Batch container (`cloud.py`), so every slice necessarily writes its own provenance record with per-slice fields (match id, timestamps, lineage). Counting record instances — or comparing whole records including per-slice fields — makes this warning fire on every sliced cloud run, which trains operators to ignore it. The warning matters precisely for the case it was written for (mixed SUT pins, e.g. a re-run half-cached on an older binary), and it cannot be heard over false positives.\n\n## Repro\n\n`arenabench cloud fetch fivetools2 --artifacts --out /tmp/x` (bucket `arenabench-artifacts-578673726240`), or any `cloud run` of a multi-task match, then compare the printed warning against:\n\n```python\nimport json, glob, collections\nsigs = collections.Counter()\nfor p in glob.glob('/tmp/x/**/provenance.json', recursive=True):\n    d = json.load(open(p))\n    sigs[(d.get('sut_commit'), d.get('sut_sha256'), json.dumps(d.get('tool_set_seats'), sort_keys=True), d.get('arenabench_version'), d.get('harbor_version'))] += 1\nprint(sigs)  # one signature => the warning was wrong\n```\n\n## Definition of done\n\nThe assembler compares provenance on the apparatus fields (SUT identity per seat, tool_set_seats, versions, engine posture) rather than record identity/count; a sliced run with one signature assembles silently, and the warning names the differing FIELDS when it does fire. A test covers both directions: N identical-signature slices → no warning; two slices differing in `sut_commit` → warning naming `sut_commit`.\n\n## Context\n\nFound while assembling the first valid five-tool arm run (#3121 fixed by runner-image rebuild; see #3032 for the programme this run serves). Files: `arenabench/arenabench/assemble.py` (warning site), `arenabench/arenabench/provenance.py` (record shape), `arenabench/arenabench/cloud.py` (slicing)."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3165[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"assemble: 'N distinct provenance records — not the same apparatus' fires on a sliced cloud run whose records are identical on every load-bearing field"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
