    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nPR #3155 (issue #3149) gave `agent.tool.result` the closed `tool: ToolName` field, retained by the bridge per in-flight `call_id`. `agent.tool.speculation_discarded` still carries only `seq` — yet at the exact point it drains the retention entry, the bridge is holding that call's `ToolName`, and the event itself carries `name` and a `reason` token. A reader asking \"which tool is speculation mispredicting on?\" (the record's own documented purpose: \"a high rate means speculation is mispredicting\") cannot answer from the diag plane.\n\n## Fix shape\n\nIn `crates/stella-cli/src/diag_bridge.rs`, the `AgentEvent::SpeculationDiscarded` arm already calls `self.take_in_flight(call_id)` and discards the return. Use it:\n\n- `.with(\"tool\", tool)` — the same closed `ToolName` mechanism `agent.tool.call`/`agent.tool.result` use (no `String` may reach a record; `log_enum!` values are the allowed shape).\n- Optionally also a closed vocabulary for `reason` (`\"attempt_failed\"` / `\"harvest_mismatch\"` — the event doc in `crates/stella-protocol/src/event.rs` says these are stable tokens, but map them through a `log_enum!` rather than passing the string).\n\nThen regenerate the reference: `make diag-reference` (`scripts/diagnostic-codes.py write`) and update the prose under `agent.tool.speculation_discarded` in `docs/reference/diagnostics.md`.\n\n## Verify\n\n- Witness: a `SpeculationDiscarded` for an observed `ToolStart` produces an `agent.tool.speculation_discarded` record containing `\"tool\":\"<name>\"` (fails today: the record has only `seq`). Test idiom: `diag_bridge.rs` `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`, `Dx::capturing()` — see `a_failed_tool_result_names_its_tool_without_a_join`.\n- Gates: `cargo clippy -p stella-cli --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p stella-cli diag_bridge`, `bash scripts/check-diagnostic-codes.sh`.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- `diag_bridge.rs` is not a god file (verified against `scripts/file-size-baseline.txt` as of #3155) but check again before adding.\n- Do not put the raw `name` string on the record; `ToolName::classify` collapse (MCP → `other`) is the declared posture (#3149).\n\nDone when the discard record names its tool (closed vocabulary), the reference page matches, and the witness flips.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3156[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"diag: agent.tool.speculation_discarded names no tool, though the bridge holds its ToolName at the drain point"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
