    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`crates/stella-protocol/src/context_event.rs` is 524 lines of published wire\ncontract that nothing in the workspace constructs or reads. The module doc says\nso itself (line 20):\n\n> **Status: schema landed, channel not yet wired.** Nothing in this workspace\n> constructs or reads a `LifecycleEventEnvelope` today — the types and their\n> golden JCS vectors exist so the wire shape (and therefore the `record_hash`\n> preimages built from it) is pinned before the first emitter lands.\n\nVerified: zero references to `LifecycleEventEnvelope`, `LifecycleEvent`, or\n`context_event::` anywhere outside the defining crate.\n\nThe decision to land the schema ahead of the emitter is defensible and the\nrationale in the module doc is good. What is missing is the tracking issue.\nAGENTS.md § \"Nothing left behind\" is explicit:\n\n> If your change ships scaffolding that something else must later wire up, file\n> the issue for that wiring in the same breath as the PR — unwired code with no\n> tracking issue is exactly the failure mode this rule exists to prevent.\n\nThe file names no issue number, and no open issue covers the wiring (#469,\n\"Epic: adaptive context lifecycle\", is closed). `check-left-behind` does not\ncatch this: the guard looks for bare `TODO`/`FIXME`/`XXX`/`HACK` markers, and\nthis module carries none — the prose is careful enough that it reads as a\ndecision rather than a deferral, which is precisely why it slipped the net.\n\nThis issue exists so the wiring is tracked. It is **not** an argument for\ndeleting the module.\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-protocol/src/context_event.rs` — the types, the\n  `LifecycleEventEnvelope` versioned envelope, `LifecycleEvent::Unknown`\n  fallback, and the golden JCS vectors.\n- `docs/spec/adaptive-context/` — the spec the module implements.\n- `doc:adr/0006-contextframe-vs-compiledcontextframe` — the cited ADR for\n  `CompiledContextFrameBuilt`.\n\n## Verify the gap\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"LifecycleEventEnvelope|LifecycleEvent|context_event::\" --glob '*.rs' \\\n  crates/ --glob '!crates/stella-protocol/**'\n# expected today: no matches\n```\n\n## Definition of done\n\nEither of these closes it — the point is that a human decides, on the record:\n\n1. **Wire the first emitter.** A producer constructs `LifecycleEventEnvelope`\n   for at least one `LifecycleEvent` variant, a consumer reads it, and a\n   witness test fails without the emitter and passes with it. The golden JCS\n   vectors already pin the wire shape, so the witness is about the channel, not\n   the bytes.\n2. **Or record the deferral where a guard can see it.** Keep the module, and\n   reference this issue number from the module doc so the unwired status is\n   discoverable from the code rather than only from reading 524 lines.\n\n## Constraints already discovered\n\n- `stella-protocol` is types-only: zero logic, zero I/O (AGENTS.md invariant\n  set, workspace layout table). An emitter belongs in a crate that may do I/O.\n- `stella-core` depends on `stella-protocol`, so these events deliberately\n  carry stable ids as strings rather than importing `stella-core` record\n  structs — importing them here would be a dependency cycle. Any wiring must\n  preserve that direction.\n- The module doc's two stated reasons for staying off `AgentEvent` (explicit\n  `schema_version`; keeping internal adaptive-context records out of the public\n  `stream-json` / serve SSE vocabulary) are design constraints on the wiring,\n  not incidental notes.\n- Editing *type* doc comments in this file re-exports into `docs/wire/` and\n  reddens `wire-schema` until the generated artifacts are regenerated and\n  committed. Module docs are not exported — which is why the citation lives at\n  module level. Prefer module-level prose for anything documentation-only.\n\n## Context\n\nFound during a first-pass adversarial audit of the workspace. The audit's one\ncode fix is #3137 (telemetry persistence off the reactor); this finding was not\nfixed there because wiring an emitter is a design decision, not a cleanup.\nSibling finding of the same shape at a smaller scale: #3136."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3135[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Unwired: `context_event.rs` ships 524 lines of lifecycle-event contract with no emitter and no tracking issue"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
