    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## A declared `tool_set` never reaches the container — the arm runs the full catalog\n\nRun `fivetool1` declared five tools and ran the whole catalog. Nothing warned.\n\n```toml\n[contestant.engine]\ntool_set = [\"search\", \"read_file\", \"edit_file\", \"write_file\", \"bash\"]\n```\n\nThe config layer parses it correctly — verified directly:\n\n```\n$ uv run python -c \"from pathlib import Path; from arenabench.config import load_match; \\\n    print(load_match(Path('matches/stella-five-tools.toml')).contestants[0].engine.tool_set)\"\n('search', 'read_file', 'edit_file', 'write_file', 'bash')\n```\n\n## Three independent pieces of evidence that it did not take effect\n\n**1. A withheld tool executed.** `verify_done` is not in the set. In trial\n`prove-plus-comm__BaJ2hxM` it was called and returned a full domain answer —\n`VACUOUS TEST — the witness test ALSO PASSES on the previous code (baseline\n3e75c842…)` — not an unknown-tool rejection. Only an advertised tool produces\nthat.\n\n**2. The menu got bigger, not smaller.** Same task, same model, same panel,\nfirst-request input tokens:\n\n| run | catalog | first-request tokens |\n|---|---|---|\n| `post1` (`prove-plus-comm__MdsJKwY`) | full 72-tool | 17,527 |\n| `post1` (`prove-plus-comm__ZXjzm7o`) | full 72-tool | 17,527 |\n| `fivetool1` (`prove-plus-comm__BaJ2hxM`) | \"five tools\" | **19,029** |\n\nA five-tool menu is ~1,194 tokens against the catalog's ~11,797, so the\nfirst request should have fallen by roughly 10,600. It rose by 1,502 —\nconsistent with a *newer SUT carrying more tools*, which is the opposite of the\ndeclared restriction.\n\n**3. The seat record has no such field.** `…-stella-….seat.json`, written by\nthe launcher and uploaded per trial, in full:\n\n```json\n{\"schema\": 1, \"contestant\": \"stella\", \"agent\": \"stella\", \"api\": \"openrouter\",\n \"model\": \"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5\", \"qualified_model\": \"…\", \"launch_model\": \"…\",\n \"base_url\": null, \"sut_ref\": \"af6552a944…\", \"sut_commit\": \"af6552a944…\",\n \"sut_sha256\": \"ddf80d57…\"}\n```\n\nNo `tool_set`. The declared restriction is absent from the record the launcher\nwrites, which is where to start looking.\n\n## Why this is severe\n\nThe tool-effectiveness programme (#3032) exists because *offered-and-unchosen*\nis indistinguishable from *absent* in a trace. This defect makes the instrument\nproduce exactly that confusion **while reporting the restriction as applied**:\nthe trials are named `…-five-tools-bare-loop-…`, the match file says five, the\nconfig object says five, and the container advertises everything.\n\nHad the trace not been read, this run would have been reported as \"the\nfive-tool arm\" with a solve rate and a tool-call count attached, and every\nnumber would have been wrong in a direction nobody could see. It cost a full\n10-trial run to find.\n\nIt is the same class as #3120 (`--tools \"*:off,…\"` advertising 13 when 5 are\nrequested) and both share a root property: **the enforcement layer is never\nasserted against the wire.** `ToolPolicy::allows` and\n`EngineConfig.tool_set` are both correct in isolation.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A declared `tool_set` restricts the container's advertised schemas, proved by\n  first-request input tokens falling by roughly the removed menu's size on a\n  same-task comparison — not by a unit test on the config object.\n- **`tool_set` appears in the seat record**, so a run's own artifacts state\n  what it ran with. A run that cannot say what its tool set was cannot be\n  audited later, and this one could not.\n- **Fail closed:** a declared `tool_set` that cannot be applied must refuse the\n  run, not run unrestricted. Silently running the opposite of the declared\n  configuration is worse than not supporting the field. #3082 already notes a\n  typo'd name is never checked against the catalog — same fail-open shape.\n- A trial-level assertion in the banned-behavior gate (#3044): a trial whose\n  declared `tool_set` is smaller than the tools it actually called is a banned\n  behavior, and this run is its witness.\n\n## Repro\n\n`arenabench/matches/stella-five-tools.toml` on branch\n`worktree-five-tool-arm`; run id `fivetool1`, artifacts under\n`s3://arenabench-artifacts-578673726240/runs/fivetool1/`.\n\n## Related\n\n#3081 (added `tool_set` → `STELLA_LEAN_TOOLS`), #3082 (a declared set is never\nvalidated against the catalog), #3120 (`--tools` leaks 8 tools), #3032, #3063.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3121[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"A declared tool_set never reaches the container — fivetool1 ran the full catalog while reporting five tools"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
