    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench/ui/components/arena/transcript-page.tsx` now colours a tool call's\nname by its CLASS — read/write/run/verify/repo/delegate — via\n`arenabench.toolclass` (a port of `crates/stella-tui/src/tool_class.rs`),\nmatching the Command Deck's own transcript grammar. `arenabench/recorder/render.py`\n— the MP4 recorder, the third surface that renders a trial's transcript\n(its module doc references \"the mp4 recorder, Stella's own Command Deck\" as\nthe two things the arena's tool-event decoding has to agree with) — was left\nuntouched: it renders every tool name in one flat colour (see its `VIOLET`/\n`CITRON`/`BONE` constants and the `kind == \"reasoning\"` special case around\nline 313; there is no `tool_class`-equivalent classification at all).\n\nNot fixed in the same pass because the recorder is a separate, harder-to-verify\nsurface: it ships into a Docker image whose build context is\n`arenabench/recorder/` alone (per `TestRecorderCopyStaysHonest` in\n`tests/test_toolout.py`), so it cannot import `arenabench.toolclass` and would\nneed its own acknowledged copy of the `(read_only, group)` table plus a test\nholding the two honest — the same pattern that module already uses for\n`decode_tool_output`/`strip_ansi`.\n\n## What \"done\" looks like\n\n- `recorder/render.py` classifies each tool call the same way\n  `arenabench.toolclass.classify` does (six classes, same catalog table) and\n  paints the tool name by that class's colour — the recorder's existing\n  terminal-emulation palette (`VIOLET`, `CITRON`, etc. around line 141) already\n  has some of the right hues; audit which of the six it's missing.\n- A copy-honesty test analogous to `TestRecorderCopyStaysHonest` in\n  `tests/test_toolout.py`, so the recorder's classification table cannot drift\n  from `arenabench.toolclass`'s silently.\n- A rendered MP4 frame (or the renderer's row-construction function, tested\n  directly without actually encoding video) shows a `write_file` row in a\n  different colour than a `bash` row.\n\n## Constraints / context\n\n- `arenabench.toolclass`'s `_CATALOG` table was itself generated from\n  `crates/stella-tools/src/catalog.rs` via a one-line `rg` command documented\n  in that module's own doc comment — reuse that generation command rather than\n  hand-transcribing the table a second time for the recorder's copy.\n- See `TestRecorderCopyStaysHonest` in `tests/test_toolout.py` for the\n  established pattern this should follow."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3111[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench recorder (MP4): tool names render in one flat colour, no tool-class parity with the deck or the /transcript page"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
