    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## The problem\n\n#3089's definition of done names three retrieval witnesses. PR #3095 built the mechanism they test and **could not assert any of them**, because all three need a real embedding backend and a populated `code_graph_chunk_vectors` table. A unit test with a hashing embedder cannot exhibit them — `SimilarityPosture::Surface` scores order candidates and certify nothing, which is exactly the property under test.\n\nSo the mechanism ships proven at the unit level (rendering, hashing, incremental re-stamping, the sweep, the relevance cut) and **unproven end to end**. That gap is what this issue closes.\n\n## The three witnesses\n\nThey test three different things, which is why #3089 asks for all three:\n\n1. **The measured regression.** `search(\"where is the prompt cache engaged on outbound requests\")` must return `crates/stella-model/src/anthropic.rs` in the **top 3**, and the top-10 score spread must exceed 0.05. Both halves matter: the old file-level index put the answer nowhere in the top 10 and spread only 0.05 across all of them.\n2. **A query whose answer is exactly one function.** Tests that the chunk granularity actually resolves to a symbol rather than to its file. Pick one with an unambiguous answer in this repository.\n3. **A query whose answer is prose, not code.** e.g. *\"why must a new AgentEvent variant declare what consumes it\"* → `AGENTS.md`'s invariant 10 section. **This is the honest test of the markdown half**: it is unanswerable from code at all, so a passing result cannot be an accident of the code index.\n\nA test that only asserts `code_graph_chunk_vectors` is non-empty proves the pass ran, not that it helped. Do not accept one.\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-graph/tests/semantic_recall.rs` — the existing integration test in this shape; follow it.\n- `crates/stella-graph/src/vectors/chunks.rs` — `pending_chunks`, `store_chunk_vectors`, `rank_chunks`.\n- `crates/stella-tools/src/search.rs` — `semantic_hits`, `catch_up_chunk_embeddings`, `group_chunks_by_file`.\n\n## How to run it\n\n- Needs a real Voyage key (`pa-` prefix); one is in SSM at `/arenabench/voyage_api_key` version 2. An `al-`-prefixed MongoDB Atlas key returns HTTP 403 against `api.voyageai.com`.\n- Must be env-gated or `#[ignore]`d so `cargo test --workspace` without a key stays green — `make gate` runs the full suite and must not require a credential.\n- The full cold pass over this workspace is ~11M tokens, under $1 at `voyage-code-3` rates, and incremental afterwards. Cost is not the obstacle; a hermetic default is.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- All three queries assert their named target, not merely a non-empty result.\n- The spread assertion on witness 1 is present (it is half the defect).\n- Green with a key, skipped-with-a-reason without one — never silently passing when it did not run. A skip that reads as a pass is the failure mode #3011 and the containment work already paid for.\n\nRefs #3089. Mechanism landed in #3095. Threshold calibration is #3096 and shares the same harness — consider doing both in one pass.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3097[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"The three #3089 retrieval witnesses — chunk search is unproven end to end"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
