    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## The problem\n\n`search` now decides how many results are relevant instead of returning a fixed ten (PR #3095). Three constants govern that decision and **none of them is a measured number**:\n\n| Constant | File | Value | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `DEFAULT_ADMISSION_FLOOR` | `crates/stella-embed/src/http.rs:59` | `0.25` | Pre-existing. Its own doc comment says \"**provisional and is not a measured separation point**\". |\n| `DEFAULT_RELEVANCE_GAP_RATIO` | `crates/stella-embed/src/rank.rs` | `2.5` | Added by #3095, labelled provisional. |\n| `DEFAULT_MIN_BOUNDARY_GAP` | `crates/stella-embed/src/rank.rs` | `0.05` | Added by #3095, labelled provisional. |\n\nThe floor is worse than provisional — it is **inert**. `voyage-code-3` scored *unrelated* files at `0.604` in the ranking recorded on #3089, so a floor of `0.25` admits everything and drops nothing. It is not currently doing the job the `SimilarityPosture` contract assigns it, and has not been since it was written.\n\n`SimilarityPosture::Semantic { admission_floor }` documents the standard explicitly: *\"declare it from measurement, the way a provider's cache posture names its witness test.\"* Three constants currently fail that standard.\n\n## Why this is not just tidiness\n\nThe relevance cut is now what decides whether the model sees an answer. A wrong constant here is not a cosmetic regression — it either hides the answer (cut too tight) or buries it (cut too loose), and in both cases the tool reports confidently. #3095 already contains one instance of this going wrong: written with the gap ratio alone, `relevant_prefix` cut the real #3089 ranking to a single result and named a file that was not the answer. That was caught only because someone had the measured distribution to test against. There is no such distribution for the other two constants.\n\n## What \"done\" looks like\n\n1. A reproducible harness that, given a workspace with a populated `code_graph_chunk_vectors` table and an embedding key, runs a fixed set of labelled queries and prints the full score distribution for each — relevant chunks and irrelevant chunks separately. It belongs beside the existing `crates/stella-graph/tests/semantic_recall.rs`, and must be `#[ignore]`d or env-gated so `cargo test` without a key still passes.\n2. A labelled query set. Start from the queries #3089's definition of done names, which have known correct answers in this repository:\n   - \"where is the prompt cache engaged on outbound requests\" → `crates/stella-model/src/anthropic.rs`\n   - a query whose answer is exactly one function\n   - \"why must a new AgentEvent variant declare what consumes it\" → `AGENTS.md`'s invariant 10 section (prose, unanswerable from code)\n3. From that distribution, set `admission_floor` **per backend** (it is already a per-`HttpEmbedder` field, so `voyage-code-3` and a local model can differ), and set the two `rank.rs` constants — or demonstrate that the shipped values already separate, which is also a result.\n4. Replace the \"provisional\" paragraph in each doc comment with the measurement and the date. Do **not** delete the paragraph without doing the measurement; that would convert an honest disclosure into a silent assumption.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Needs a real Voyage key (`pa-` prefix). One is in SSM at `/arenabench/voyage_api_key` version 2. An `al-` prefixed MongoDB Atlas key returns HTTP 403 against `api.voyageai.com` and is not usable.\n- `crates/stella-embed` is a leaf with no workspace-crate dependencies — keep the harness out of it, or gate it so the crate's own tests stay hermetic.\n- `rank.rs` is invariant-2 pure decision logic. The calibration harness may read a database; `relevant_prefix` and `top_k` must not.\n- Report the unflattering number if that is the true one. A constant tuned until a favourite query looks good is worse than the provisional one it replaced, because it carries authority it has not earned.\n\nRefs #3089, #3063. Introduced by #3095.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3096[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Calibrate the search relevance constants from measurement — all three are provisional and the admission floor is inert"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
