    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`crates/stella-cli/src/credential_handoff.rs` seals every model-provider\ncredential (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, etc.) inside a\nprocess-local `HANDOFF` map, readable only through `key_for()`. It is a\ndeliberate design: a raw credential never touches `std::env`, so a bash tool\ncall the agent spawns cannot inherit it via ordinary environment inheritance\nor `/proc/$PPID/environ`.\n\nThe embedding backend's credential (`VOYAGE_API_KEY`, added for #2995) is a\ndocumented exception: `consume_at_startup` re-exports it into real process\nenvironment (`std::env::set_var`) immediately after consuming the handoff,\nbecause `stella-embed`'s `EmbedderEnv::from_process`\n(`crates/stella-embed/src/http.rs`) has always read it ambiently — that\nambient-read contract predates the handoff and is unrelated to bench\ncredential security. Extending the handoff to `VOYAGE_API_KEY` was scoped\nnarrowly to \"keep it out of Harbor's environment and `docker compose exec`\nargv, and out of the model-provider selection contract\" — it does **not**\ngive the embedding credential the same guarantee providers get. See the \"one\ntarget that leaves the seal\" section of `credential_handoff.rs`'s module doc\nfor the full reasoning, written at the time this was added.\n\n## What this means concretely\n\nIn a bench container, once `stella` has consumed the FD handoff,\n`VOYAGE_API_KEY` sits in the process's real environment. Any `bash` tool call\nthe agent makes (including one driven by a malicious or adversarial task\nprompt) inherits it exactly as it would inherit a developer's own exported\nkey. This is a real, if narrow, secret-exfiltration surface a benchmark\ncontainer should probably not have for a credential with real billing\nattached.\n\n## What would fix it properly\n\nThread a typed, ambient-env-free embedding credential from\n`credential_handoff::key_for(\"VOYAGE_API_KEY\")` down to the actual call sites\nthat need it — `crates/stella-tools/src/search.rs`, `crates/stella-tools/src/graph/semantic.rs`,\nand `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/graph.rs` (`stella init`'s indexing path) —\nreplacing their direct `stella_embed::from_env()` / `EmbedderEnv::from_process()`\ncalls with an explicitly-constructed `EmbedderEnv` whose\n`voyage_api_key`/`openai_api_key` fields come from the handoff when present.\n`stella-embed` is a dependency leaf with no workspace-crate dependencies (see\nAGENTS.md), so it cannot know about `credential_handoff` itself — the override\nhas to happen at each call site in a crate that *can* see both.\n\nThis is real, cross-crate surgery (`stella-tools`, `stella-cli`), not a\none-file fix, which is why it was scoped out of the #2995 credential-forwarding\nchange rather than attempted inline.\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/credential_handoff.rs` — the handoff itself, and\n  where the ambient-env exception is currently documented.\n- `crates/stella-embed/src/http.rs` — `EmbedderEnv`, `EmbedderEnv::from_process`,\n  `resolve`.\n- `crates/stella-tools/src/search.rs`, `crates/stella-tools/src/graph/semantic.rs`,\n  `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/graph.rs` — the three call sites that would\n  need to switch from the ambient read to an injected `EmbedderEnv`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- `VOYAGE_API_KEY` (or `OPENAI_API_KEY` used as an embedding credential) never\n  appears in `std::env` inside a process that received it via the FD handoff.\n- A witness test proves a bash tool call spawned by the agent (or an\n  equivalent subprocess-inheritance check) does not see it, where it does\n  today.\n- The ambient-env fallback (`EmbedderEnv::from_process` reading directly from\n  `std::env`) is preserved for the non-handoff case (a developer's own\n  terminal), since that is stella-embed's pre-existing, still-valid contract.\n\nNot urgent — the credential is real but scoped (an embedding API key, not a\nmodel provider key with a much larger blast radius), and every honest tradeoff\nhere is already documented in the code. Filed so the gap is tracked rather\nthan silent.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3093[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"credential_handoff: VOYAGE_API_KEY is re-exported into ambient process env, unlike every provider credential"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
