    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n#2995 asked for the Voyage/embedding credential to reach a bench container\nindependent of the model provider route, with three explicit requirements:\n\n1. A container receives it, independent of provider — **done** (see the PR\n   that closes the credential-forwarding half).\n2. Optional, fails open — **done**.\n3. \"It enters the posture digest, or two arms differing only in embedder are\n   indistinguishable in the ledger.\" — **not done**, tracked here.\n\n`bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/posture.py`'s `_benchmark_engine_posture`\nand `read_posture_selectors` hash every host-side selector that changes what a\ntrial measures (worker effort, triage/research/plan pins, candidate count,\netc.) into `stella_engine_posture_sha256`. Whether the embedding credential was\npresent is not one of those selectors, so two runs — one with `VOYAGE_API_KEY`\nconfigured and one without — hash to the *same* posture digest today, even\nthough one of them can actually use `search`'s semantic rung and the other\ncannot.\n\n## What this costs, concretely\n\nAn analyst comparing two arms by posture digest (the documented way to check\n\"did these two runs measure the same configuration\") cannot detect that one\narm's `search` degraded to a plain lexical scan while the other's didn't. The\nnew `stella_embedding_credential_names` manifest field (added alongside the\ncredential-forwarding fix) records this *per trial*, but the manifest is not\nthe comparability key — the posture digest is.\n\n## What to do\n\nAdd an embedder-presence key to the posture the same way `POSTURE_SELECTOR_ENV`\nselectors are handled: append only when configured (unset omits the row, so\nevery digest recorded before this key existed still describes the posture that\nproduced it — see the existing convention documented at `posture.py`'s\n`research_model`/`plan_model` selectors for the exact append-only shape to\nfollow). A reasonable key: whether `VOYAGE_API_KEY` (or any name in\n`stella_harbor.credential_bundle.EMBEDDING_CREDENTIAL_NAMES`) was present,\nnever the value itself.\n\n## Files\n\n- `bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/posture.py` — `_benchmark_engine_posture`,\n  `read_posture_selectors`, `POSTURE_SELECTOR_ENV`.\n- `bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/credential_bundle.py` —\n  `EMBEDDING_CREDENTIAL_NAMES`, `optional_embedding_credentials`.\n- `bench/harbor_adapter/tests/test_posture.py` — where the new selector's\n  append-only and digest-stability properties should be witnessed.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- Two identical match configs differing only in whether `VOYAGE_API_KEY` is\n  configured on the host produce different `stella_engine_posture_sha256`.\n- A posture computed before this change (no embedder key present) hashes\n  identically to how it hashed before — proven by a witness test, matching the\n  append-only convention `posture.py` already documents for its other\n  selectors.\n\nRefs #2995"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3092[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench: embedder credential presence is missing from the posture digest (#2995 DoD item 3)"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
