    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench/tests/test_reauth_wiring.py::TestOnlyAVoidComesBack::test_a_retry_that_dies_on_the_new_token_pauses_again`\nfailed once on a real CI run (`harbor_adapter + analyzer pytest`, run\n[31645140472](https://github.com/macanderson/stella/actions/runs/31645140472/job/94276829454)),\non the merge commit for #3044 (`f0d2f874`, which already contains #3047 —\nunrelated to that fix):\n\n```\ntests/test_reauth_wiring.py:428: AssertionError\nFAILED tests/test_reauth_wiring.py::TestOnlyAVoidComesBack::test_a_retry_that_dies_on_the_new_token_pauses_again - assert False is True\n +  where False = tick()\n +    where tick = <test_reauth_wiring.Rig object at 0x7f21611a9370>.tick\n```\n\nAn immediate `gh run rerun --failed` on the identical commit passed clean\n(680 passed, 1 skipped). No other PR or push has reproduced it since.\n\n## What was ruled out\n\nThe test's docstring and its sibling\n(`test_a_retry_reusing_a_trial_id_still_pauses_when_it_dies`, which explicitly\nbumps `os.utime(trial / \"result.json\", (time.time() + 5.0, ...))` to dodge a\nsame-second collision) suggested a same-second `result.json` mtime race in\n`SupervisedSeat`/`MatchReauth._advance`'s `superseded` computation\n(`reauth.py:733-737`, keyed on `TrialView.concluded_at < seat.dispatched_at`).\n\nThat hypothesis does **not** hold up:\n\n- A deterministic repro that forces both `alpha__a` and `alpha__retry`'s\n  `result.json` to the *identical* `st_mtime` via `os.utime` still passes —\n  `reauth.py`'s tie-break is deliberate (`concluded_at < since`, strict\n  less-than, \"ties resolve toward not superseded\" per the comment above\n  `superseded` at `reauth.py:172`), so an equal-timestamp collision is already\n  handled correctly.\n- 200 consecutive local runs of the real test (macOS, same worktree, same\n  commit) all passed — no reproduction.\n\nSo this is not the mtime-granularity shape the sibling test guards against.\nSomething else made this one CI run intermittent — possibly something\ntiming-sensitive in the `Rig`/`FakeProcess` harness (`threading` is imported\nin the test module), possibly a Linux-runner-specific race not present on\nmacOS, or a rarer edge in `Supervisor`/`MatchReauth` state transitions not yet\nidentified. Genuinely unknown — flagging honestly rather than shipping a\nguessed fix.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nEither:\n- reproduce it deterministically (a tight loop on a Linux runner, or\n  instrumenting `_advance` to log `concluded_at`/`since`/`superseded` on the\n  next real occurrence) and fix the actual mechanism, or\n- after a stated number of clean occurrences with no repeat, close as\n  transient with the investigation notes left for whoever hits it next.\n\n## Related\n\n- #3058 — the `match.toml`/`trial.json` issue that *was* confirmed and fixed\n  by #3047; this is a separate, still-open question found while verifying\n  that fix landed clean on #3044's merge commit.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
