    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench/tests/test_cloud.py::TestFetchMergesIntoOneTrial::test_cloud_fetch_writes_a_merged_trial_alongside_the_flat_files`\nfails on `origin/main`:\n\n```\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '.../trial.json'\n```\n\nwith this printed just above the failure:\n\n```\nassembled : not yet — .../match.toml does not exist — the whole-match spec is\nwhat makes assembly a restoration rather than a guess. Re-fetch the run with\n`arenabench cloud fetch <run-id> --artifacts`.\n```\n\nSo the test expects `cloud fetch` to leave a merged `trial.json`, `_assemble_fetched`\ndeclines because the fixture's fetch produced no `match.toml`, and the assertion\nthen trips on the missing file.\n\n## It is pre-existing, not caused by the gate work\n\nConfirmed by control rather than by inspection — the failing test was run on a\ndetached worktree at `origin/main` with no gate changes present, and it fails\nidentically there:\n\n```sh\ngit worktree add --detach /tmp/abctl origin/main\ncd /tmp/abctl/arenabench && python3 -m pytest -q \\\n  \"tests/test_cloud.py::TestFetchMergesIntoOneTrial\"\n```\n\n## Likely relation to #3025\n\n#3025 records that \"a default `cloud fetch` cannot be assembled or read by the\ntrace tooling, and only says so after the download\" — the same `match.toml`\nprecondition, from the operator's side. This is that defect showing up in the\nsuite. Whether the right fix is to make the default fetch produce an assemblable\ntree (#3025's subject) or to make this test set up the `--artifacts` shape it\nactually needs is the decision to make; they may be one PR.\n\n## Also failing in the same run, and separate\n\n`tests/test_sut.py` — five tests fail with\n\n```\nAdapterUnavailableError: /usr/bin/python3 cannot build a Stella seat:\n`import arenabench.harbor_agent` failed with ModuleNotFoundError: No module\nnamed 'tomllib'\n```\n\nThat is environmental (`/usr/bin/python3` is 3.10; `tomllib` arrived in 3.11)\nrather than a code defect, but a test that silently depends on the *system*\ninterpreter having a stdlib module is worth either skipping explicitly with a\nstated reason or pinning to the project interpreter. Splitting that into its own\nissue is fine if it is judged unrelated.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n`cd arenabench && python3 -m pytest -q tests/` is green on a clean checkout, or\neach remaining failure is an explicit skip naming why.\n\n## Related\n\n- #3025 — the operator-facing half of the `match.toml` precondition\n- PR #3044 — where the failure was noticed (the control above was run from it)\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3058[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: TestFetchMergesIntoOneTrial fails on main — a default cloud fetch leaves no match.toml to assemble"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
