    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`Finding.rate_line()` in `bench/trace_triage/detectors.py` divides\n`Finding.count` (which counts **occurrences**) by `Finding.denominator` (which\ncounts **trials**). For any detector that can fire more than once inside one\ntrial, the result is arithmetically impossible and prints as such:\n\n```\n### grep answered `(no matches)` for a pattern the POSIX fallback could not execute\n- detector `grep-ere-false-negative` · site `crates/stella-tools/src/grep/fallback.rs`\n- 22 of 20 trials examined (110%).\n```\n\nReproduce:\n\n```sh\npython3 bench/trace_triage/postmortem.py arenabench/arenabench-cloud/s5b2 --stdout\n```\n\n`grep-ere-false-negative` is the loudest case (22 occurrences across 4 trials of\na 20-trial run), but it is not the only one: `tool-error-envelope`,\n`repeated-identical-tool-call` and `repeated-file-read` all emit one `Occurrence`\nper call or per path, so any of them can exceed its denominator on a bad enough\nrun. The three that have not are the ones that happened to fire at most once per\ntrial in the runs looked at so far.\n\n## Why it matters more than a cosmetic percentage\n\nThe module already takes this seriously in the other direction — `rate_line()`\nexists precisely so a single occurrence says \"single occurrence\" rather than\n`1/20 = 5%`, because \"the percentage is arithmetically true and epistemically a\nlie\". A `110%` is the same lie with the sign flipped, and it lands in GitHub\nissue bodies via `issues.py` and in `postmortem.md` via `postmortem.py`.\n\nThe gate is already immune: `banned.py::trials_affected()` counts distinct\n`occurrence.trial_uuid` rather than occurrences, and\n`tests/test_banned.py::test_trials_affected_counts_trials_not_occurrences` pins\nit. That helper is the fix in miniature — it just lives on the wrong side of the\nboundary to help the two rendering surfaces.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nGive `Finding` a `trials` property (distinct `trial_uuid` count, the same\ncomputation as `banned.trials_affected`) and have `rate_line()` report **both**\nnumbers when they differ — e.g.\n`22 occurrences across 4 of 20 trials examined (20%)` — so the incidence stays a\ntrial rate and the volume is not lost. Then have `banned.trials_affected`\ndelegate to it, so there is one definition rather than two.\n\n## Files\n\n- `bench/trace_triage/detectors.py` — `Finding.count`, `Finding.rate_line`,\n  `Finding.single_occurrence`\n- `bench/trace_triage/banned.py` — `trials_affected` (the existing correct\n  computation)\n- `bench/trace_triage/postmortem.py`, `bench/trace_triage/issues.py` — the two\n  consumers that render it\n\n## Definition of done\n\n`postmortem.py` over `arenabench/arenabench/../arenabench-cloud/s5b2` prints no\npercentage above 100, a test in `tests/test_detectors.py` pins the multi-\noccurrence-single-trial case, and `banned.trials_affected` has one implementation\nrather than two.\n\n## Related\n\n- Gate that exposed it: PR #3044\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3056[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench: a per-call detector reports more occurrences than trials, and rate_line prints \"22 of 20 trials (110%)\""[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
