    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench/pyproject.toml` declares a full ruff configuration and carries ruff\nas a dev dependency:\n\n```toml\ndev = [\"pytest>=8\", \"ruff>=0.6\"]\n\n[tool.ruff]\nline-length = 96\n\n[tool.ruff.lint]\n...\n```\n\nbut **no workflow ever runs it**. `.github/workflows/bench.yml` is the only\nworkflow that touches these trees, and every one of its steps is `pytest`:\n\n```\n- name: arenabench — pytest (until ejection)\n  working-directory: arenabench\n  run: uv run --with pytest --no-project pytest -q\n```\n\n`rg -n 'ruff|lint|format' .github/workflows/bench.yml` returns nothing.\n\nSo the lint config is decoration: it gates nothing, and a contributor who runs\n`ruff check` locally sees failures that CI is indifferent to. That is worse than\nhaving no config, because the file asserts a standard the repository does not\nactually hold anyone to.\n\n## Evidence it has already drifted\n\nTwo findings sit in `arenabench/arenabench/cloud.py` on `main` today:\n\n```\n$ cd arenabench && uv run --with 'ruff>=0.6' --no-project ruff check --output-format=concise arenabench/cloud.py\narenabench/cloud.py:1252:36: RUF100 [*] Unused `noqa` directive (unused: `N802`)\narenabench/cloud.py:1256:39: RUF100 [*] Unused `noqa` directive (non-enabled: `BLE001`)\n```\n\nBoth are stale `# noqa` suppressions for rules that are no longer enabled — the\nexact residue a lint gate exists to prevent. `ruff format --check` additionally\nreports that `arenabench/arenabench/cloud.py` and `arenabench/tests/test_cloud.py`\nwould both be reformatted.\n\nThey are untouched by #3047, which found them; folding an unrelated lint sweep\ninto a red-`main` repair is what CLAUDE.md's \"do not fix a red ratchet you did\nnot cause\" warns against.\n\n## Files\n\n- `.github/workflows/bench.yml` — the workflow that would gain the step(s)\n- `arenabench/pyproject.toml` — has `[tool.ruff]` + the dev dep already\n- `bench/trace_triage/`, `bench/harbor_adapter/`, `bench/terminal_bench_analysis/`,\n  `bench/evidence/`, `bench/telemetry_store/` — check each for the same shape\n  before deciding scope; `bench.yml` runs pytest for all of them\n\n## Constraints discovered\n\n- The Python trees here are **three separate uv projects**; `uv lock` only\n  affects the one in your cwd. Match each existing step's `working-directory`\n  and `uv run` incantation rather than adding one repo-wide invocation.\n- `arenabench` is documented as running \"until ejection\" — confirm it is still\n  worth gating before adding a step there, or scope the gate to `bench/` only.\n- Whether `ruff format --check` joins `ruff check` is a real decision: turning it\n  on means one reformatting commit across these trees first, which should land on\n  its own PR from a fresh `main` so it does not collide with in-flight work.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- `bench.yml` runs `ruff check` (and, if chosen, `ruff format --check`) for every\n  Python tree that has a ruff config, with the same `working-directory` /\n  `uv run` shape as that tree's existing pytest step.\n- The two `RUF100` findings above are resolved rather than suppressed, and any\n  reformatting needed to make the gate green has landed.\n- A deliberately-introduced lint violation fails CI — verified, not assumed.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3055[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench and bench/ configure ruff but no workflow runs it"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
