    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Context\n\nWhile fixing #3036 (widening `crates/stella-model/src/credential.rs`'s\ninteractive-prompt gate to also check whether the prompt is actually visible,\nnot just whether stdin is a terminal), I found that the \"visible on stdout\"\nassumption baked into that fix — mirroring `stella_tty::human_can_answer`'s\nexisting stdout-based shape — is a proxy, not an exact match, for this one\ncall site.\n\n`crate::credential::prompt_for_key` calls `rpassword::prompt_password`, whose\ndefault `Config` (`rpassword::ConfigBuilder::default()`) writes the prompt\ntext to, and reads the answer from, `/dev/tty` directly on Unix — see\n`rpassword-7.5.4/src/unix.rs::DEFAULT_OUTPUT_PATH` (\"/dev/tty\") and\n`config.rs`'s `ConfigBuilder::default()`. It does **not** go through\n`std::io::Stdin`/`std::io::Stdout` at all on that platform (Windows uses\n`CONOUT$`, same story; wasm uses `/dev/stdout`, which does match).\n\nSo the fix landed in #3036 checks `std::io::stdout().is_terminal()`, which is\nthe right question for every *other* consumer of\n`stella_tty::human_can_answer` (the `ask_user` tool and the CLI's approval\nresponder both really do print via `println!` to stdout) but is only a proxy\nhere: a process with a redirected stdout (`stella config > out.txt`) but a\nlive controlling terminal would, per the new check, decline to prompt even\nthough `rpassword` would have successfully shown the prompt on the real\nterminal via `/dev/tty` — a false negative (declines a prompt that would have\nworked). The reverse (false positive: stdout looks like a terminal but no\n`/dev/tty` is available, e.g. some containerized/CI shapes) is also possible in\nprinciple, though rarer.\n\n## Why this wasn't fixed in #3036\n\n`#3036`'s definition of done only asked for the fix to mirror\n`human_can_answer`'s existing (stdin, stdout) shape — the same shape already\nused by every other consumer. Making the credential-prompt check exactly right\nmeans either (a) checking `/dev/tty`'s openability directly, which is\n`rpassword`-implementation-specific and platform-conditional (Windows/wasm\ndiffer), or (b) getting `rpassword` to report what it will actually do before\ncommitting to the prompt. Both are a real design decision, not a mechanical\nmirror of the existing predicate, so it's out of scope for a \"reuse the shared\nderivation\" fix and belongs in its own PR.\n\n## Suggested approach\n\n- Investigate whether `rpassword` (or a lower-level equivalent) exposes a\n  cheap \"can I actually prompt right now\" probe, or whether opening `/dev/tty`\n  read-write and immediately closing it (mirroring what `prompt_password` will\n  do) is an acceptable cheap check.\n- Alternatively, configure `rpassword` via `ConfigBuilder::default().writer(...)`\n  or similar to route through `std::io::Stdout`/`Stdin` explicitly, so the\n  existing `stella_tty::human_can_answer(interactive, stdin_is_terminal,\n  stdout_is_terminal)` check is exactly correct instead of a proxy — trading\n  away `rpassword`'s \"survives a redirected stdin/stdout\" robustness on\n  purpose, if that tradeoff is judged acceptable.\n- Whichever direction: add a witness that distinguishes \"stdout redirected,\n  real controlling terminal present\" from \"no controlling terminal at all\",\n  since those are the two cases the current stdout-based check cannot tell\n  apart.\n\n## Files involved\n\n- `crates/stella-model/src/credential.rs` (`prompt_for_key`, `ApiKey::resolve`)\n- `crates/stella-tty/src/lib.rs` (the shared `human_can_answer` predicate,\n  added in #3036)\n- `crates/stella-model/tests/credential_prompt_degrade.rs` (existing witness;\n  keep its documented seam — `stdin().is_terminal()` reports `true` under the\n  `cargo test` harness even though the stream isn't really readable)\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- The credential prompt's interactivity check reflects what `rpassword` will\n  actually do on the current platform, not a stdout proxy for it.\n- A witness test distinguishing the two cases named above.\n- `make gate` green; no new god-file lines, no baseline raised."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3052[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"credential prompt visibility check reads stdout, but rpassword writes its prompt to /dev/tty on Unix"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
