    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Outcome\n\nEvery behavioural claim Stella has already shipped is measured on the bench, or\nis explicitly labelled unmeasured. Today five shipped mechanisms rest on a\nhypothesis nobody has run an arm against, and in at least two cases the trace\nalready suggests the hypothesis is wrong.\n\nThis is CLAUDE.md's \"correctness is demonstrated or it is not claimed\" pointed\nat the changes that already landed rather than at the next PR.\n\n## Why this is one epic and not five measurement chores\n\nThey share one failure mode, one method, and one standing trap.\n\n**The failure mode.** A change ships on a plausible mechanism, the mechanism is\nnever exercised in a trial, and the claim then circulates as if established:\n\n- **#2983** — the verification apparatus (witness authoring, witness\n  *debugging*, `verify_done`, `repo_status`/`repo_recover` bookkeeping) is\n  **24–36% of every tool call** and Claude Code spends **zero** while solving\n  20/20. Partitioning the same 20-trial arms shows residual task work identical\n  to two decimal places (20.70 vs 20.75 calls), so the entire \"decisive prompt\"\n  reduction was the apparatus shrinking — nothing about how Stella solves the\n  task changed. Whether the apparatus buys solves is **unresolved**: 18/20 vs\n  17/20 at n=20 is noise.\n- **#2995** — semantic `graph_query` shipped on the hypothesis that a semantic\n  index removes the name-guessing grep spiral (13 of 58 calls on\n  `fix-code-vulnerability` were spelling variants of one concept). That those 13\n  calls exist is proven. That an index stops them is not — the model has to\n  *choose* the new op.\n- **#2993** — `SimilarityPosture::Semantic { admission_floor }` asks for a\n  number derived from observed relevant/irrelevant score distributions.\n  `HttpEmbedder` supplies `0.25`, which nobody measured. The code says so; the\n  declaration does not, and it will be quoted as measured by the first reader\n  who skips the comment. This is upstream of #2995: retrieval quality is one of\n  its three ways to get a zero result.\n- **#3038** — the `tool_steering!` amendment naming `$STELLA_SCRATCH` was\n  motivated by three trials where the worker deleted its own witness test ~16s\n  after writing it, citing the no-scratch rule. Nothing demonstrates the amended\n  rule stops that.\n- **#1604** — `graph_query` used on 0/4 nightly trials and `project_overview` on\n  1/4. The code-intelligence adoption signal has never been non-zero, across\n  three months and every remedy tried.\n\n**The method**, identical for all five and non-negotiable per CLAUDE.md:\narms differ by exactly one commit or the comparison is confounded and must be\nreported as such; repeats per task; **no budget or token cap**; read\n`stella-events.jsonl`, never `result.json` or the UI; census `(role, model)`\nfrom `step_usage`; join `tool_start` → `tool_result` for real wall clock.\n\n**The standing trap:** a five-task solve rate cannot resolve anything smaller\nthan a catastrophe. In all five, solve rate is a **guardrail** and the mechanism\nmetric is the measurement. Three prompt experiments in one week looked strong at\npartial samples and finished flat — and a dead arm scores as a win, so\noperational aborts get named and excluded explicitly.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- **#2983** — either a measurement with repeats per task showing what the\n  verification apparatus buys in solve rate, so its cost is a trade a maintainer\n  can see, or a design change holding the same guarantee at materially fewer\n  calls with the same measurement proving it cost no solves. Its two separable\n  items (`ask_user` answering 0 bytes in a headless run; `repo_status` /\n  `repo_recover` firing 2.45–3.95 times per trial with no task-visible\n  consequence) may land first.\n- **#2995** — arms **A** (`fcf2b4cbc`, #3014 merged, prompt untouched) vs **B**\n  (#3020 merged), so \"the description alone\" is separable from \"the description\n  plus a prompt rule\". Report which of the three zero-reduction mechanisms\n  happened if the number does not move: the model never calls the op, it calls\n  it and the answer is wrong, or it calls it and greps anyway to confirm.\n- **#2993** — a per-model floor table, each entry citing the measurement that\n  produced it; any model whose distributions overlap declares\n  `SimilarityPosture::Surface` and says so.\n- **#3038** — a reported count of self-authored-test deletions per arm with the\n  trace paths, and a stated conclusion or an explicit \"the sample cannot resolve\n  this\" naming the sample size that would.\n- **#1604** — the adoption signal is either non-zero on a measured run, or the\n  reason it is not is named from the traces.\n\nIn every case: **report the unflattering number when it is the true one.** A\nnumber that flatters Stella because of a measurement artifact spends the exact\nreputation the project exists to build.\n\n## Children\n\n#1604 #2983 #2993 #2995 #3038\n\n## Not in scope\n\nThe trustworthiness of the harness itself is #2775 (capture) and the trace-read\nchain epic (assembly, replay, postmortem). This epic assumes those hold and\nasks a different question: **has the arm been run at all?**\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3050[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Epic: the behavioural claims we shipped are measured, not assumed"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
