    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Outcome\n\nThe documentation a reader relies on — the published docs site, the in-repo\nprompt rendering, and AGENTS.md's gotchas — says what the code actually does,\nand something mechanical fails when it stops doing so.\n\nEvery child was found by the same 2026-08-12 freshness audit against `main` at\nc9511b5e8, and every one has the same cause: **nothing relates a shipped surface\nto its documentation**, so drift is invisible until a human goes looking.\n\n## Why this is one epic and not five docs chores\n\n`scripts/check-command-docs.sh` proves the shape works — it relates a\n*subcommand* to a reference page and has held that level since #993. One level\ndown (flags), one level sideways (prompt contracts), and one level out (a whole\nplane with no page at all), nothing relates anything, and the audit found\nexactly the predictable result in each place:\n\n- **flags** — 10 of the CLI's 17 global session flags were undocumented, seven\n  of them absent from the site entirely; `--upstream-pin` shipped 2026-08-10\n  (#2786) and was undocumented within two days of a docs-touching commit\n  (#3041).\n- **prompt contracts** — `docs/prompts/worker.md` renders 4 of the 9 shared\n  contracts and states an assembly order that is wrong in the same direction.\n  It is `status: living`, so it reads as current (#3029).\n- **a flag with no home** — `--upstream-pin` needs to be where someone\n  reasoning about gateway routing and about a comparable head-to-head run will\n  actually be reading, and #2786's recorded-upstream half is undocumented\n  anywhere (#3042).\n- **a whole plane with no page** — `-v`, `--log-level`, `--log-file` and\n  `STELLA_LOG` appeared nowhere under `website/content/docs/`; the in-repo\n  reference at `docs/reference/diagnostics.md` is not published (#3043).\n- **a gotcha that produced a false green** — `cargo` colourises, so the escape\n  precedes the word and `rg '^error'` over build output prints a reassuring\n  nothing while the build is failing. AGENTS.md warns about piped `cargo`\n  hiding an exit code; a reader who internalised that lesson still writes this\n  filter (#3006).\n\nThis is also the explainability half of the project's mission: a reader who\ncannot find out what Stella does, or reads a rendering that is half the truth,\ncannot audit it.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A gate step (or a `stella-cli` test) fails when a flag is added to any command\n  without a corresponding docs edit, and when a page names a flag that no longer\n  exists — both directions, with a committed, reviewable exemption file (#3041).\n- `docs/prompts/worker.md` carries a section per shared contract in declaration\n  order with the literal quoted verbatim, both assembly summaries name the real\n  order and count, and a test in `prompt/parity.rs` fails when the doc falls\n  behind (#3029).\n- `--upstream-pin` is documented in `api-providers/index.mdx` and named as a\n  precondition of a comparable run in `guides/terminal-bench-head-to-head.mdx`,\n  and #2786's recorded-upstream field is documented wherever run receipts are —\n  after verifying the field's real name in the code (#3042).\n- A published diagnostics page exists under `website/content/docs/`, listed in\n  the root `meta.json`, stating the privacy contract **with its enforcement\n  mechanism** (a `stella-diag` field value cannot hold a `String` or a `Path` —\n  that is a compile error) rather than as a promise (#3043).\n- AGENTS.md § Gotchas states that a grep over build output is not a build\n  result, and that `--color=never` / `CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never` is required when\n  filtering deliberately — plus an audit of whether any committed script under\n  `scripts/` carries the same filter (#3006).\n\n## Children\n\n#3006 #3029 #3041 #3042 #3043\n\n## Constraint every child shares\n\n`website/content/docs/**` and `*.md` are in `ci.yml`'s ignored paths, so a\ndocs-only PR does not start the required job — `docs-guards.yml` is where a\nshell-guard version has to run, and a test-based implementation still wants a\n`docs-guards.yml` entry so a docs-only PR that deletes a card is caught.\n\nRelated: #993 (the subcommand-level guard this extends), #928, #1314, #1493.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3048[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Epic: the documentation matches the shipped surface, and something mechanical fails when it stops"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`website/content/docs/diagnostics.mdx` (added in #3043) carries a hand-picked,\nhand-transcribed subset of the diagnostic codes table as a plain markdown\ntable. `docs/reference/diagnostics.md` — the source of truth — is itself\n**generated** from the emit sites by `make diag-reference`\n(`scripts/diagnostic-codes.py`), and the gate (`make diagnostic-codes`) fails\nthe two ever disagreeing.\n\nThe website copy has no such guarantee. It will drift the first time a code is\nadded, renamed, or its level changes, exactly the failure mode the generator\nexists to prevent for the in-repo copy.\n\n## What to build\n\nGenerate the website table's rows from the same source\n`scripts/diagnostic-codes.py` reads (the emit-site scan), rather than hand\ncopying prose out of `docs/reference/diagnostics.md`. Options worth weighing:\n\n- Extend `scripts/diagnostic-codes.py` with a second output mode that emits\n  the curated/reader-facing subset as MDX-embeddable data (e.g. a JSON file\n  the page imports), keeping the \"hand-picked for troubleshooting symptoms\"\n  curation but generating the per-code level/description cells.\n- Or render the *complete* table on the website page instead of a curated\n  subset, generated in full, and let the page's own prose do the\n  symptom-oriented curation/linking instead of the table itself.\n\nEither way: a `make` target (or an extension of `make diag-reference`) should\nregenerate the website's copy, and `make gate` (or `docs-guards.yml`, since\n`website/content/docs/**` is outside `ci.yml`) should fail when the website\ntable and the emit sites disagree, the same way `make diagnostic-codes`\nalready does for `docs/reference/diagnostics.md`.\n\n## Verify\n\nAdd or rename a diagnostic code's level in a facet enum; confirm the website\npage's table is now stale and the new gate catches it.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- The website diagnostics page's code table is produced from the emit-site\n  scan, not transcribed by hand.\n- A gate step catches drift between the website table and the tree, matching\n  `diagnostic-codes`'s guarantee for the in-repo reference.\n- `docs/reference/diagnostics.md` remains the canonical, fully generated\n  reference; the website page may still curate *which* codes it surfaces, but\n  not their content.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Source: `scripts/diagnostic-codes.py`, `docs/reference/diagnostics.md`,\n  `docs/spec/diagnostics.md` §11.\n- Related: #3043 (added the page this table lives on)."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3045[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"docs: generate the website diagnostics codes table from docs/reference/diagnostics.md instead of hand-transcribing it"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
