    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`docs/prompts/worker.md` documents the shared prompt contracts by quoting each\n`macro_rules!` literal from `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/prompt.rs`. It has\nfallen five contracts behind, and nothing in `make gate` or CI notices.\n\n`prompt.rs` declares nine shared contracts (the authoritative list is\n`SHARED_CONTRACTS` in `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/prompt/parity.rs`):\n\n`tool_steering`, `skill_use`, `scope_discipline`, `measurement_discipline`,\n`verification_proportionality`, `faithful_reporting`, `complexity_discipline`,\n`action_care`, `injection_defense`.\n\n`docs/prompts/worker.md` has a `### <macro>!` section for only four of them —\n`tool_steering!`, `scope_discipline!`, `measurement_discipline!`,\n`verification_proportionality!` — and its two assembly summaries are wrong in\nthe same direction:\n\n- line 160: \"Assembled as: opener, blank line, `tool_steering!`, blank line,\n  `scope_discipline!`, blank line, `measurement_discipline!`, blank line,\n  `verification_proportionality!`, blank line, rules.\" — omits `skill_use!`\n  (which is second, right after `tool_steering!`) and the four contracts after\n  `verification_proportionality!`.\n- line 186: \"Same five shared blocks in the same positions.\" — there are nine.\n\n`skill_use!` (#2724), `faithful_reporting!`, `complexity_discipline!` (#2690),\n`action_care!` (#2688) and `injection_defense!` (#2689, #2722) each landed with\ntheir provenance in a `prompt.rs` doc comment and none of it reached this doc.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThis is the only human-readable rendering of the effective worker prompt. A\nreader auditing \"what does Stella actually tell the model\" sees roughly half of\nit and an assembly order that is wrong, which is the failure mode the\n`SHARED_CONTRACTS` derivation in `parity.rs` was built to prevent one level\ndown. The doc is `status: living`, so it reads as current.\n\n## Verify the drift\n\n```sh\nrg -n '^### `' docs/prompts/worker.md                           # 4 contract sections\nrg -n '^macro_rules! ' crates/stella-cli/src/agent/prompt.rs    # 9 contracts\nrg -n 'Assembled as:|Same five shared blocks' docs/prompts/worker.md\n```\n\n## Definition of done\n\nTwo halves, and the second is the one that makes this not recur:\n\n1. `docs/prompts/worker.md` carries a section per contract in declaration\n   order, each quoting the literal verbatim, and both assembly summaries name\n   the real order and count.\n2. A guard makes the doc fail when it falls behind. The cheap shape already\n   exists: `parity.rs` reads `prompt.rs`'s source with `include_str!` and\n   derives the contract set (`scan`, `the_registries_match_the_source`). A test\n   in the same module can `include_str!` the doc and assert every contract in\n   `SHARED_CONTRACTS` appears in it verbatim — same anti-vacuity discipline\n   (`MIN_CONTRACT_CHARS`, a source anchor) — and it would have failed the day\n   `skill_use!` landed.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/prompt.rs` is at 1492 of its 1500-line ceiling\n  (#2985) — the test belongs in `prompt/parity.rs`, which is where prompt\n  content pins already live.\n- Cite the doc by id (`prompt-worker`), not by path — see AGENTS.md.\n- Prompt literals stay compile-time constants (invariant 7 / L-E8); a check\n  that reads them is fine, anything that computes them at runtime is not.\n\n## Context\n\nNoticed while adding two bullets to `tool_steering!` (the batching and\nshell-routing instructions), which updated that one block's quote in this doc\nand left the rest of the drift untouched as out of scope.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3029[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"docs/prompts/worker.md documents 4 of the 9 shared prompt contracts, and nothing checks it"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
