    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`bench/trace_triage/bands.py` records a nine-arm survey (2026-08-12) of what a\nhealthy bench arm looks like. Three of its four per-trial columns replay\nexactly from the traces; the fourth does not, so it ships as an observation on\n`bands.TrialMetrics.empty_ok_results` and as **no band at all** — there is no\nthreshold, and the postmortem's band table has three rows rather than four.\n\nReplaying `arenabench-cloud/s5b2` (the arm the survey scores at **2.4 empty\nok-results per trial**) with `run_trace.load_run` gives:\n\n| candidate definition | s5b2, per trial |\n|---|---|\n| `output.ok.content` is empty or whitespace (what ships today) | 0.0 |\n| `output.ok` carries no `content` key at all | 0.0 |\n| `output.ok.content` under 20 characters | 1.3 |\n\nand the sub-20-character strings are real content — `(no matches)` (11\noccurrences), a bare `\\n[exit code: 0]` trailer (8), `OK\\n\\n[exit code: 0]` (4).\nNone of the three reaches 2.4.\n\nThe same replay reproduces the other three columns for s5b2 **exactly** —\ntools 32.5, identical consecutive calls 0.0, cache hit 100.0% — so the\ndisagreement is this metric's definition, not the loader and not the fixture.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nA threshold whose measurement cannot be reproduced fires or stays silent for\nreasons nobody can check. The survey's unhealthy arms sit at 3.3-9.2 on this\ncolumn and one healthy-cache arm sits at 3.5, so it was never going to be a\nverdict-capable separator — but as a *directional* row it is still one of the\nfour things the postmortem reports, and a row whose observed value is 0.0 on an\narm the survey calls 2.4 is worse than a missing row.\n\n## Files\n\n- `bench/trace_triage/bands.py` — `EMPTY_OK_UNRESOLVED`, `BANDS`,\n  `TrialMetrics.empty_ok_results`, `trial_metrics`\n- `bench/trace_triage/tests/test_postmortem.py::test_a_band_that_cannot_separate_says_so`\n  asserts `empty_ok_results` is **not** in `BANDS`; it flips when this lands.\n\n## Verify\n\n```sh\npython3 bench/trace_triage/postmortem.py arenabench-cloud/s5b2 --stdout\n```\n\nThe band table must show a row whose observed value matches the survey's 2.4\nfor s5b2, and the same definition must place w10f near 9.2 and dec1 near 1.5.\n\n## Done when\n\nEither (a) a definition is found that replays all nine surveyed arms within\nrounding, at which point it becomes a `Band(verdict_capable=False, ...)` row\nand `EMPTY_OK_UNRESOLVED` is deleted; or (b) the survey column is re-measured\nfrom the traces and the table in `bands.py`'s docstring is corrected to what\nreplays. Whichever it is, the constant and this issue reference go away in the\nsame PR.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3023[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench: the survey's \"empty ok-results\" column does not replay from the traces, so it ships as no band at all"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
