    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`stella_graph::vectors::pending` now returns a `PendingScan { files, unreadable }`\n(#3016), where `unreadable` counts the indexed files a scan stepped over because\ntheir content could not be read from disk. The **eager** `stella init` pass\n(`crates/stella-tools/src/graph/semantic.rs::warm_opened`) carries that count out\nto the CLI, which renders it as a distinct sentence — `! semantic index: 68 files\nembedded … 32 left unembedded, 32 of them because their content could not be\nread`.\n\nThe **lazy per-query** pass does not. `catch_up_embeddings`\n(same file) reads `scan.files` and drops `scan.unreadable` on the floor, so\n`semantic_code_search`'s answer footer still says only\n\n```\n(N of M files embedded by <model>)\n(embedding is incremental — files not yet embedded cannot rank; re-run to continue)\n```\n\n\"re-run to continue\" is the same wrong promise #3016 removed from the eager\npath: re-running will not embed a file whose content cannot be read, so a\nworkspace with a permanently unreadable indexed file shows a gap that never\ncloses and a note that says it will. The agent reading that footer has no way\nto tell \"still catching up\" from \"these files will never rank\".\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/stella-tools/src/graph/semantic.rs` — `catch_up_embeddings` (drops the\n  count), `semantic_query_with` (renders the footer).\n- The eager path's shape is the reference: `warm_opened` +\n  `WarmOutcome::Warmed { unreadable }` + `format_warm_outcome` in\n  `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/graph.rs`.\n\n## Verify / repro\n\n1. Index a workspace (`stella init`, or `CodeGraph::open` + `index_all`).\n2. Delete or `chmod 000` one indexed source file, leaving its graph row.\n3. Run a `semantic_code_search` query with an embedder configured.\n4. Observed: the footer reports `N of M embedded` and invites a re-run, naming\n   no reason. Expected: the answer says some files could not be read, the same\n   way the init pass does.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not fork `pending` — `crates/stella-graph/src/vectors.rs`'s header states\n  there is exactly one way a file becomes embeddable text, and #3016 kept the\n  fill-past-skips fix inside it. The count is already on the return value; this\n  is a rendering change, not a scan change.\n- `catch_up_embeddings` returns `Result<(), String>` today. An unreadable file\n  is **not** an error — the answer must still come back — so the count needs to\n  reach the renderer as data, not as an `Err`.\n- The footer is model-facing text. Keep it one short clause; the point is to let\n  the agent stop expecting a re-run to fix it.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A `semantic_code_search` answer over a workspace with an unreadable indexed\n  file names that fact and does not promise a re-run will close the gap.\n- A witness test in `crates/stella-tools/src/graph/semantic/tests.rs` (the\n  wiremock `concept_server` fixture is already set up for this — see\n  `an_unreadable_file_does_not_stop_the_eager_pass_at_the_readable_ones`, added\n  by #3016) that fails without the change.\n- `make gate` green.\n\nRelated: #3016 (the scan fix and the eager path's version of this), #3014 (the\neager pass), #3003 (the vector plane).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3021[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"graph: the lazy semantic pass drops the unreadable-file count, so its answer still promises a re-run that cannot help"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
