    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench/arenabench/agents.py` can only register a slug for an agent Harbor\n0.6.1's `AgentFactory` (`harbor/agents/factory.py` in the installed `harbor`\npackage) actually knows how to install and drive as a `--agent <slug>`\nbuilt-in, or one ArenaBench ships itself via `import_path` (the pattern\n`STELLA` in `agents.py` uses — a `module:Class` Harbor loads with\n`--agent-import-path`).\n\nA reference Dockerfile was shared (see PR that closed #<fill-in-if-applicable>\nadding `nemo-agent`/`openhands-sdk`/`pi`) listing a much larger CLI-agent\nroster than Harbor 0.6.1 supports:\n\n- Factory Droid (`@factory/cli`)\n- Kilo Code (`@kilocode/cli`)\n- OpenClaw (`openclaw`)\n- Sourcegraph Amp (`@sourcegraph/amp`)\n- xAI Grok CLI (`@xai-official/grok`)\n- Xiaomi Mimo (`mimo`)\n- Google Antigravity CLI (`agy`)\n\nNone of these have a class registered in\n`harbor.agents.factory.AgentFactory._AGENTS` (checked directly against the\ninstalled `harbor==0.6.1` package — `AgentName` may list a slug like\n`terminus`/`terminus-1` with no backing class, which is a different, already\n-handled case). Right now `resolve_agent()` in `arenabench/agents.py` has no\nway to seat any of the CLIs above: they are not Harbor built-ins, and nobody\nhas written an ArenaBench-native adapter for them the way `harbor_agent.py`\ndoes for Stella.\n\n## What \"done\" looks like\n\nPick one path per agent (or as a batch decision) and implement it:\n\n1. **Wait for Harbor to add native support**, bump `HARBOR_VERSION` in\n   `arenabench/infra/runner/Dockerfile` when it lands, and add the\n   corresponding `_builtin(...)` entry to `AGENTS` in\n   `arenabench/arenabench/agents.py` (same shape as the `nemo-agent`,\n   `openhands-sdk`, `pi` entries).\n2. **Write an ArenaBench-native adapter**, following the\n   `arenabench.harbor_agent:ArenaStellaAgent` pattern (subclass Harbor's\n   `BaseInstalledAgent`/`BaseAgent`, handle install + run + credential\n   plumbing), register it via `import_path` in `AGENTS`, and cover it with a\n   test in `tests/test_arena.py` the way `STELLA` is covered.\n\nEither way, a witness test belongs in `tests/test_arena.py`\n(`resolve_agent(\"<slug>\")` currently raises `KeyError`) and the new entry\nneeds real `honours`/`token_env`/`base_url_env`/`effort_env` values backed by\nwhat the CLI actually reads — not copied from a sibling agent's declaration,\nper the \"honest-reporting bias\" the `agents.py` module docstring commits to.\n\n## Constraints / context\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/agents.py`'s module docstring: \"Harbor already knows\n  how to install and drive ~23 coding agents; ArenaBench does not reimplement\n  any of them.\" Adding a native adapter for any of these is a deliberate\n  exception to that rule, so it should be a conscious per-agent decision, not\n  a default.\n- `arenabench/infra/runner/Dockerfile` currently only bakes in Claude Code;\n  every other Harbor built-in is installed by Harbor itself inside the task\n  container at trial time (see the file's own comments). A native-adapter CLI\n  would need its own install step there too, mirroring how Claude Code is\n  installed today."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 3012[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: no seat path for agents outside Harbor's factory (Factory Droid, Kilo Code, OpenClaw, Sourcegraph Amp, xAI Grok CLI, Mimo, Google Antigravity)"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
