    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`SimilarityPosture::Semantic { admission_floor }` asks for a number derived\nfrom a model's *observed* relevant/irrelevant score distributions — the same\ndiscipline a provider's cache posture applies when it names its witness test.\n`HttpEmbedder` declares `Semantic` and supplies a floor that nobody measured:\n\n```rust\n// crates/stella-embed/src/http.rs\n/// **This number is provisional and is not a measured separation point.**\nconst DEFAULT_ADMISSION_FLOOR: f32 = 0.25;\n```\n\nIt is deliberately permissive and its only current job is to drop the\nobviously-unrelated tail from an ordered list. That is a defensible interim\nposition and it is stated in the code, the crate README and the PR — but it is\nan unmeasured constant in the one place the type system asked for a measured\none, and it will be quoted as if measured the first time someone reads the\ndeclaration and not the comment.\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-embed/src/http.rs` — `DEFAULT_ADMISSION_FLOOR`,\n  `HttpEmbedder::similarity_posture`, `STELLA_EMBED_FLOOR` override.\n- `crates/stella-embed/src/seam.rs` — `SimilarityPosture` and its contract.\n- `crates/stella-embed/README.md` § \"Semantics worth knowing\" — the paragraph\n  that must be rewritten once numbers exist.\n\n## How to measure\n\n1. Take a real repository (this one) and a labelled query set: N questions in\n   English, each with the file(s) a human says is the answer. 30–50 is enough\n   to see a separation.\n2. Index with `graph_query op=semantic` under each candidate model\n   (`voyage-code-3`, `text-embedding-3-small`, `text-embedding-3-large`, a\n   local `nomic-embed-text`).\n3. Record the cosine of every (query, file) pair, split by the label.\n4. The floor is where the two distributions separate; report the overlap, not\n   just the point. If they overlap materially the honest answer is\n   `SimilarityPosture::Surface` for that model, exactly as `HashEmbedder`\n   reports today.\n\n## Done looks like\n\n- A per-model floor table in `stella-embed`, each entry citing the measurement\n  that produced it.\n- `DEFAULT_ADMISSION_FLOOR` either gone or documented as the value for an\n  unknown model, with its own justification.\n- Any model whose distributions overlap declares `Surface` and says so."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2993[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"stella-embed: the admission floor is provisional, not measured — measure it per model on a code corpus"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
