    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Outcome\n\nA running turn can be corrected mid-flight — by the engine when it detects a\nloop, and by the user when they hit Esc with something to say — and the\ncorrection lands on the lane that is actually running, carrying an honest\naccount of how much budget is left.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- `Checkpoint` records the loop-steer budget's `spent` count, so a resumed turn\n  cannot re-open a warning it already paid for (#2809).\n- The last steer says it is the last one. Since #1743 the same sentence means\n  two different things depending on which of `MAX_LOOP_STEERS` it is, and #1473\n  is the precedent that this wording changes model behaviour materially — so\n  this ships measured, not guessed (#2810).\n- Esc-steering reaches a **worker** lane instead of falling back to the backlog.\n  `SubSessions` must hand back the lane's `SteeringTap` so the driver can inject\n  at its step boundary (#2899).\n\n## Why one epic\n\nAll three are the same seam — the step-boundary injection point — seen from\nthree sides: what the engine may say there (#2810), what survives a resume of it\n(#2809), and who can reach it (#2899).\n\n## Children\n\n#2809 #2810 #2899\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2953[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Epic: mid-turn steering — the engine and the user can both correct a running turn"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Outcome\n\nThe trace records what a run actually did and what it actually cost. This is\nthe enabling condition for every rule in CLAUDE.md about reading the trace\ninstead of a surface signal: those rules assume the trace is complete, and in\nfive measured places it is not.\n\nThe recurring sub-shape is the one the triage rubric names as a P0 case: **a\nmissing measurement rendering as a negative measurement.** `file_change_events:\n0` beside `mutating_actions: 99` does not read as \"not wired\"; it reads as\n\"this run changed nothing.\"\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A cancelled execution reports its full cost, not the pre-cancel prefix —\n  exec 99 recorded 0.87 USD of a 5.29 USD run (#2570).\n- `usage_incomplete` names the model that made the failed call instead of\n  `\"unknown\"` — 435 such rows in one 16-trial panel, which is exactly the\n  population you need when mid-turn fallback (#2769) is re-resolving *because*\n  calls are failing (#2831).\n- `files_touched` and `execution_reflection.wrote_files` see the edits an\n  isolated pipeline candidate makes, instead of reading 0 (#2907).\n- `ladder.file_change_events` is either wired or removed — it is `0` in every\n  verdict of every trial, winners included (#2934).\n- Candidate delivery emits a declared event, so \"adoption ran\" stops being an\n  inference from a `file_change` burst, and a withheld candidate is\n  distinguishable from an empty one (#2942).\n\n## Children\n\n#2570 #2831 #2907 #2934 #2942\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2952[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Epic: the trace faithfully records what a run did and what it cost"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Outcome\n\nEvery check this repository believes it runs actually runs, on the paths it\nclaims to cover, before the code lands. The failure shape shared by all four\nchildren is the one AGENTS.md calls out as the direction that misleads: a\nreader runs the short list, sees green, and believes the gate is green.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- `make bench-test` runs the same six Python suites `.github/workflows/bench.yml`\n  runs, and a red arenabench test is catchable before push (#2847).\n- The brand builders' `--check` runs as a gate step, so a stale or corrupt\n  generated asset cannot reach the remote (#2910).\n- Something reads the *rendered* website page, so a swallowed JSX space cannot\n  ship \"stellaspeaks\" to the landing page again (#2894).\n- `dependency-review.yml` has the `pull-requests: write` permission its\n  configured `comment-summary-in-pr` needs, so the summary it was configured to\n  post actually posts (#2533).\n\n## The class\n\nEach child is a configured-but-inert check, not a missing idea. #2847 has a\nmeasured instance (#2844 merged with its own pytest job already `failure`, and\n`main` went red). #2894 has a shipped instance (live on the landing page).\n#2533 has never posted at all. #2910's guard exists and no gate step calls it.\n\n## Children\n\n#2533 #2847 #2894 #2910\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2949[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Epic: every configured check actually runs before the code lands"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
