    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nPR #2937 made a lineage-seeded match structurally non-aggregable with a clean one, and `arenabench.series.match_row` now emits the facts a reader needs:\n\n```json\n\"comparability\": {\n  \"contaminated\": true,\n  \"lineage\": \"lineage:self-improve.v1@3\",\n  \"group_key\": \"...|lineage:self-improve.v1@3\"\n}\n```\n\nThe **client renders none of it.** The trends view groups by `group_key`, so it already refuses to draw one line through a seeded and a clean point — that part works. But a seeded point is drawn looking exactly like a clean one, in its own series, with nothing on the page saying the agents in it had already seen the tasks.\n\nThat is the weakest link in the chain the marker travels: provenance carries it, `result.json` carries it, the CLI prints `!! SEEDED RUN` above the numbers, the runner logs a WARNING per seat — and then the one surface people actually screenshot and paste into Slack shows an unlabelled chart.\n\n## Files\n\n- Producer (done, no change needed): `arenabench/arenabench/series.py::match_row` → `row[\"comparability\"][\"contaminated\"]` and `[\"lineage\"]`\n- Also available per match: `row[\"provenance\"][\"contaminated\"]`, `[\"lineage_label\"]`, `[\"lineage_id\"]`, `[\"lineage_seats\"]`\n- Consumer (the work): the trends view under `arenabench/ui/` (and `arenabench/web/` if the built export needs regenerating)\n- Precedent for rendering a comparability warning: whatever the client already does with `mixed_version_seats` / `violated_pins` — if it does nothing with those either, that is part of this issue.\n\n## What \"done\" looks like\n\n1. A seeded match is visibly marked in the trends view — a badge on the point and a line in whatever tooltip or detail panel the point opens, carrying the lineage label and the generations (`lineage_seats[seat].generations`, `.trials`, `.unseeded`).\n2. The label says what it *means*, not just that a flag is set: these agents had seen these tasks before; this number is not comparable with a clean run.\n3. `unseeded` is surfaced, not swallowed — \"3 of 5 trials were seeded\" and \"5 of 5 were\" are different amounts of contamination and the label must not overclaim the first.\n4. A test at whatever level the UI is tested (snapshot or DOM) proving the badge appears for a contaminated row and does not for a clean one.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not change `group_key`. The grouping refusal is the load-bearing half and it already works.\n- A clean match must render byte-identically to how it rendered before lineage existed; `contaminated` is `false` and `lineage` is `\"\"` for every legacy row, and legacy provenance records carry neither attribute at all (`series.py` reads both with `getattr`).\n\n## Why it matters\n\nPer `arenabench/provenance.py`'s docstring, the archive's recurring failure is not that anyone lies — it is that a confounded result looks exactly like a clean one until someone thinks to ask. This is the last surface where that is still true for lineage.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2940[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench trends: a lineage-seeded match renders unlabelled — the contamination marker reaches the payload and stops there"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
