    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`reauth.is_credential_void` keys on `telemetry.VOID_CREDENTIALS`\n(`AuthenticationError`, `OAuthCallbackError`, `RefreshTokenExpiredError`) — deliberately,\nbecause the re-dispatch set must be keyed on the abort taxonomy and never on \"did not\npass\". That is the honesty property #2545 is built around.\n\nBut there is a second shape of the same fault, and it wears an agent-failure name. Some\nagents swallow their own 401/429 and exit nonzero, so Harbor records\n`NonZeroAgentExitCodeError`. `telemetry.MetricsReader.read` already catches this on\n*observed spend* — a trial that ran with zero tokens and zero cost is reclassified\n`infrastructure=True, resolved=None` (the #1480 fix, `arenabench/arenabench/telemetry.py`,\nthe block commented \"A trial that 'ran' without one observed token was never a fair\nattempt\").\n\n`metrics.failure` keeps the name `NonZeroAgentExitCodeError`, so:\n\n- the scoreboard correctly voids the trial (it is out of `solve_rate`'s denominator), but\n- `reauth` sees a non-credential failure, `TrialView.measured` is `True`, and the task is\n  **never re-dispatched**.\n\nSo a rotation that manifests this way still truncates the arm: the trials void, and\nnothing re-runs them. Measured for real on match `dd52a57a6f49` — three trials,\n`api_error_status:429`, scored as Claude Code losses before #1480.\n\nThe current behaviour is conservative in the safe direction (it under-retries, never\nre-runs a real loss), which is why this is a gap rather than a bug in the shipped wiring.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/reauth.py` — `is_credential_void`, `TrialView.measured`\n- `arenabench/arenabench/telemetry.py` — `VOID_CREDENTIALS`, the zero-spend reclassification\n- `arenabench/tests/test_reauth.py` — `test_every_credential_error_class_is_recognised`\n- `arenabench/tests/test_reauth_wiring.py` — the rig to write the wiring-level witness in\n\n## The design question to settle first\n\n`TrialView` currently carries only `status` and `failure`. Deciding this needs one more\nfact from `TrialMetrics` — either `infrastructure` plus the zero-spend signal, or a\ndedicated \"the agent was never served\" flag computed in `telemetry.py` where the\nreclassification already happens. Prefer the latter: the classification lives in one\nplace today and splitting it is how the two copies drift.\n\n**Do not** widen the re-dispatch set to `infrastructure` generally. A setup timeout, a\ncompose failure and a broken verifier are all voids that a fresh credential cannot fix,\nand re-dispatching them burns the retry budget against something unrelated.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A trial that died of a credential fault Harbor named as an agent exit is re-dispatched.\n- A trial that died of any *other* infrastructure fault is still not re-dispatched.\n- A measured loss is still never re-dispatched (the existing witnesses in\n  `test_reauth_wiring.py::TestOnlyAVoidComesBack` must stay green).\n- A witness at the wiring layer, not just on `decide`.\n\n## Related\n\n- #2545 — the wiring.\n- #1480 — where this failure shape was diagnosed.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2857[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: a credential failure Harbor names `NonZeroAgentExitCodeError` is invisible to the reauth re-dispatch set"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
