    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n#2545 wired the OAuth-rotation supervisor into `MatchRunner`. When a Claude Code seat\nloses its credential and the local login cannot supply a different one, the seat enters\n`SeatState.PAUSED`, its Harbor process is stopped, and its unmeasured tasks are held.\n\nTwo resume paths exist in the design. Only one is reachable:\n\n- **Auto-heal (reachable).** Every supervisor tick re-reads this machine's Claude Code\n  login, so an operator who runs `claude login` in another terminal resumes the sweep\n  with no further involvement. This is the common case, because rotation leaves the new\n  token in the keychain.\n- **Operator hand-off (unreachable).** `MatchRunner.provide_token(match, token,\n  contestant=None)` exists and is tested, and **no surface calls it**. There is no HTTP\n  route and no CLI verb, so a token that came from somewhere other than this machine's\n  Claude Code login cannot be delivered to a paused seat.\n\nConsequence today: such a seat waits out `reauth.PAUSE_GRACE_SECONDS` (30 min) and is\nthen released with a named shortfall. Honest, but the sweep is lost when a working\ncredential was available the whole time.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/runner.py` — `MatchRunner.provide_token` (the entry point to call)\n- `arenabench/arenabench/reauth.py` — `MatchReauth.provide_token`, `MatchReauth.waiting`,\n  `SupervisedSeat.to_json` (the `waiting` flag a surface would read)\n- `arenabench/arenabench/server.py` — where a route would live (`/api/matches/<id>/...`)\n- `arenabench/arenabench/cli.py` — `_cmd_run`, which polls the match and could prompt\n\n## Constraints\n\n- **The token must never touch disk.** `claude_oauth.py`'s contract; the hand-off is\n  in-memory by design and a file/queue channel would break it for every seat at once.\n- The value must not reach a log, a `repr`, or any snapshot field. `Contestant.redacted()`\n  discloses env *names* only, and `test_reauth_wiring.py::test_no_credential_reaches_the_record`\n  pins that for the match record.\n- A POST body carrying a credential needs the same care as the seat `.env` paste path —\n  see `Match.snapshot`'s \"no secrets, by construction\" comment.\n- `provide_token` returns the contestant ids that took the token; empty means no seat is\n  waiting. A surface must report that rather than claim a resume (there is already a test\n  for the empty case).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A paused seat can be resumed with a credential from outside this machine's Claude Code\n  login, through at least one surface.\n- The response distinguishes \"resumed seat X\" from \"no seat is waiting for a credential\".\n- A witness test that fails without the surface: paused seat → call the surface → the\n  supervisor re-dispatches on the supplied token. `tests/test_reauth_wiring.py` shows the\n  fake rig (no Harbor, no Docker, no keychain) to drive it from.\n\n## Related\n\n- #2545 — the wiring this is the missing half of.\n- #1980 — the underlying mid-run rotation problem.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2855[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: nothing calls MatchRunner.provide_token — a paused seat can only be resumed by re-logging in"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
