    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`_ClaudeCodeFold.consume` (`arenabench/arenabench/harness.py`) recognises the\nCLI's continuous reasoning-token estimate without parsing it, because those\nlines are ~99% of a real stream by count:\n\n```python\nif _THINKING_MARK.encode() in raw:      # _THINKING_MARK = '\"thinking_tokens\"'\n    thinking = raw                       # only the last one in this drain matters\n    continue\n```\n\nThe match is an **unanchored substring over the whole line**. Any other event\nwhose serialized text happens to contain `\"thinking_tokens\"` is therefore\ndiverted into the `thinking` slot instead of being folded, and if it is not the\nlast such line in the drain it is discarded entirely. Even when it *is* last,\nthe recovery path only reads `estimated_tokens`, so the event's real content —\nan assistant message's usage, or a `tool_result` — is lost.\n\nThe realistic trigger is an agent whose tool output quotes the string: reading\nor grepping a Claude Code stream, a Harbor log, or this repository's own\n`arenabench/arenabench/harness.py`. The trial's measured tokens or tool count\nare then quietly short, which is precisely the \"plausible number nobody\nquestions\" class the module's own docstring is written against.\n\n## Why it was not fixed alongside #2519/#2520\n\nThe obvious repair — anchor the mark at the head of the line — is not\navailable as-is. The stdout tee's lines are not guaranteed compact (the test\nfixtures in `tests/test_harness.py` are written with `json.dumps`' default\n`\", \"` / `\": \"` separators, so `{\"type\": \"system\", \"subtype\":\n\"thinking_tokens\"…`), and the key order across CLI versions is not something\nArenaBench controls. Anchoring on a guessed prefix would trade a rare\ndata-loss bug for a common one — the fast path would stop matching and every\narchived stream would re-parse 38k lines per drain.\n\nNote the sibling case was decided the other way and is already settled:\n`_StellaFold.consume` deliberately has **no** fast path, because Stella's\njournal stamps `{\"ts\":…,\"type\":…}` so no mark can be anchored there either, and\nlosing a `step_usage` is a measurement error while parsing every line is only\ntime. That reasoning is in a docstring on the method.\n\n## Options for the fix\n\n1. **Parse everything, as the Stella fold does.** Simplest and provably\n   correct; costs one `json.loads` per line, paid once per line because\n   `StreamReader` never re-reads. Measure it against a real 15 MB archived\n   stream before choosing — that measurement is the whole decision.\n2. **Confirm the candidate before diverting it**: keep the substring test as a\n   *filter*, then parse the candidates and fold any that are not\n   `{\"type\": \"system\", \"subtype\": \"thinking_tokens\"}`. Correct, and cheap only\n   if false positives are rare — which is the assumption to be checked, not\n   assumed.\n3. Anchor on a tokenizer-ish check (mark within the first N bytes) — rejected\n   here as arithmetic that a future line-length change silently breaks.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A stream in which an ordinary event's text contains `\"thinking_tokens\"` is\n  folded with no loss: a witness test with a `tool_result` carrying that string\n  in its output, asserting the tool and its usage still land, and that the\n  reasoning estimate is still the last real estimate.\n- Whichever option is taken, the tradeoff is stated in the docstring beside the\n  code, in the same terms the Stella fold's is.\n- The existing `test_the_reasoning_estimate_is_the_last_one_not_their_sum` still\n  passes unchanged.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/harness.py` — `_THINKING_MARK`,\n  `_ClaudeCodeFold.consume`, `_StellaFold.consume` (the decided sibling case)\n- `arenabench/tests/test_harness.py`\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Standard library only (`arenabench/pyproject.toml`).\n- Whatever replaces it must stay incremental: `StreamReader` holds a byte\n  cursor because one archived stream is 15 MB and a live dashboard polls it.\n\nParent epic: #2775. Found while landing #2519 / #2520.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2853[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench harness: the Claude Code reader's `_THINKING_MARK` fast path silently drops any stream line whose text contains \"thinking_tokens\""[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
