    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## The problem\n\n`.github/workflows/bench.yml`'s `harbor_adapter + analyzer pytest` job runs **six** Python suites. `make bench-test` (`Makefile:147-151`) runs **two** of them, and `bench-test` is not in `GATE_STEPS` (`Makefile:45`) at all — so `make gate` runs none.\n\n| Suite | bench.yml | `make bench-test` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bench/harbor_adapter` | yes | yes |\n| `bench/terminal_bench_analysis` | yes | yes |\n| `bench/telemetry_store/tests` | yes | **no** |\n| `bench/evidence/tests` | yes | **no** |\n| `bench/evidence/frontier/tests` | yes | **no** |\n| `arenabench/` (767 tests) | yes | **no** |\n\nThe consequence is not hypothetical. On 2026-08-11, #2844 merged at 06:55:00Z while its own `harbor_adapter + analyzer pytest` check had already reported `failure`, and `main` went red on `arenabench/tests/test_runner_netns.py::test_a_lock_whose_holder_died_is_reclaimed`. The failure was **deterministic**, not flaky — `flock(1)` forks, so killing the `Popen` left the orphaned `sleep` child holding the lock — and it would have been caught by any local run of that file. There was no local command that ran it.\n\nThe pre-push hook is the repository's stated answer to `enforce_admins` being off (AGENTS.md § \"The gate\"), and for these four suites it has nothing to run.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```bash\ngit checkout 25e743121890c57bcf21f161e17f3b63a7eec6ce   # main, red\nmake bench-test                                          # passes — the broken suite is not in it\ncd arenabench && uv run --with pytest --no-project pytest -q tests/test_runner_netns.py\n# 1 failed — the test that made main red\n```\n\n## Constraints already discovered\n\n- **Runtime is the real tension.** The arenabench suite is ~62s locally on top of a `uv` resolve; the other three are ~3s combined. Putting all four in `make gate` taxes every Rust-only push. Consider (a) adding all four to `bench-test` and leaving `bench-test` out of `GATE_STEPS`, plus (b) teaching `.githooks/pre-push` to select `bench-test` from the pushed diff the way it already derives `CARGO_SCOPE` via `scripts/impacted-crates.sh` — the paths are exactly bench.yml's own scope filter (`^(bench/|arenabench/|crates/stella-model/src/catalog\\.rs$|\\.github/workflows/bench\\.yml$)`).\n- **`gate-parity` will fail you** if `GATE_STEPS` changes without the matching prose edit in both AGENTS.md § \"The gate\" and CONTRIBUTING.md (`scripts/check-gate-parity.sh`).\n- **The suite list is now duplicated** between `bench.yml` and the `Makefile`, which is the shape that produced this gap. Whatever the fix, derive one from the other or guard the pair — a second copy that drifts silently just moves the defect.\n- `bench/telemetry_store`, `bench/evidence` and `bench/evidence/frontier` run `--no-project` deliberately (standard-library only, so recomputing a published score needs no harness install). Preserve that.\n- Do **not** widen this into the ruff gap — that is #2193 (arenabench) and #2167 (harbor_adapter), tracked separately.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- One command a contributor can run that covers every Python suite `bench.yml` runs, with the suite list held to `bench.yml`'s by a guard or by construction rather than by a second hand-maintained copy.\n- A push touching `arenabench/**` runs that suite before it leaves the machine.\n- A witness: reintroduce the #2844 defect (`Popen([\"flock\", lock, \"sleep\", \"30\"])` + `holder.kill()`) in `arenabench/tests/test_runner_netns.py` and confirm the new path goes red; revert.\n\nFound while fixing `main` after #2844 (see the PR that references this issue)."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2847[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench: `make bench-test` runs 2 of the 6 Python suites CI runs, so a red arenabench test cannot be caught before push"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
