    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Problem: `crates/stella-core/src/engine_markers.rs` declares the closed table of engine/CLI-authored User-role marker prefixes (#2722), now six entries (summary, loop steer, continuation, stop-hook feedback #2684, recall, working-set restore #2685). Two engine/CLI-authored User-role markers are absent: `WAKE_MARKER = \"[parked wait\"` (`crates/stella-core/src/waiting.rs`, written by `driver/waiting.rs::maybe_park`) and `SKILL_INVOCATION_PREFIX = \"[skill invocation\"` (`crates/stella-core/src/skills/invoke.rs`, written by the #2682 inline-invocation injection).\n\nConsequences: (1) `crates/stella-core/src/receipts.rs::user_block_kind` classifies both as `BlockKind::UserGoal`, attributing engine/CLI text to the person — the exact defect #2722 fixed for the other markers; (2) the static prompts' injection-defense clause (`crates/stella-cli/src/agent/prompt.rs`, `injection_defense!` macro) tells the model engine guidance is recognizable by its markers, so a wake message or invocation body — both instruction-shaped — fails the prompt's own test.\n\nVerify: grep WAKE_MARKER / SKILL_INVOCATION_PREFIX in engine_markers.rs and receipts.rs — absent.\n\nConstraints: adding a table entry fails `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/prompt/parity.rs::every_engine_marker_is_taught_verbatim_by_every_static_prompt` until the `injection_defense!` literal teaches it, and fails the receipts completeness test until `user_block_kind` gains an arm (pick kinds deliberately: an invocation body is closest to Steered; a wake is arguably Steered too — decide and document, the wire enum should not grow casually). Also decide whether the invocation marker joining the table affects `loop_evidence::turn_start_index`.\n\nDone: both markers in ENGINE_MARKERS, classified non-UserGoal with a doc-comment rationale, taught by both prompts, all parity/receipts/engine_markers tests green. Related: #2795 (source-scan parity that would have caught these mechanically).\n\nRefs #2722, #2682, #2685, #2787."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2837[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"ENGINE_MARKERS omits the parked-wait wake marker and the skill invocation marker — receipts misattribute both to the user and the prompts do not teach them"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
