    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`docs/wire/agentevent.schema.json` is generated from the Rust types and gate-enforced by `wire-schema` — but the enforcement only proves *the schema matches the Rust*. Nothing checks that the **non-Rust consumers of that schema still read fields that exist.**\n\narenabench is such a consumer: it reads `result.json` / the ladder snapshot in Python (`arenabench/arenabench/proof.py`, `transcript.py`) and TypeScript (`arenabench/ui/lib/types.ts`, `ui/components/arena/*.tsx`). Those reads are `dict.get(...)` and structural TS types, so a field rename in `stella-protocol` produces **no error anywhere** — it produces a wrong number.\n\n## How it was found (a real instance, not a hypothetical)\n\nPR #2814 renamed `LadderSnapshot.flip_achieved: bool` to `flip: FlipOutcome` (a tri-state) for #2556. Every Rust consumer moved with it because the compiler said so. arenabench did not, and the result was silent and scoring-relevant:\n\n```python\n# arenabench/arenabench/proof.py:445\nproof.flip_achieved = bool(ladder.get(\"flip_achieved\"))\n```\n\nOn a post-rename record the key is absent → `.get` returns `None` → `bool(None)` is `False`. **Every run scores as no-flip, including a genuinely flip-verified one.** `proof.py:316-318` then branches on that for proof classification.\n\nIt was caught by a review bot on the PR, not by any gate. That is the part worth fixing: the next rename gets no bot.\n\nThis is the same hazard class the repo already solved *within* Rust — `crates/stella-protocol/tests/wire_contract.rs` fails if an enum arm never reaches a sample — and the same class as the cross-crate parity tests (`crates/stella-cli/src/candidate_ws.rs:128-131`: \"A `const` array cannot embed the other crate's constant, so a parity test below pins the two spellings together instead\"). The gap is only across the language boundary.\n\n## Files\n\n- `docs/wire/agentevent.schema.json`, `docs/wire/agentevent.d.ts` — the generated contract\n- `scripts/check-wire-schema.sh`, `Makefile` target `wire-schema`, `.github/workflows/wire-schema.yml`\n- Consumers: `arenabench/arenabench/proof.py`, `arenabench/arenabench/transcript.py`, `arenabench/ui/lib/types.ts`, `arenabench/ui/components/arena/proof-panel.tsx`, `arenabench/ui/components/arena/proof-badge.tsx`\n\n## Suggested approaches (pick one deliberately; each has a real cost)\n\n1. **A key-existence check.** Collect the string literals arenabench reads out of ladder/verdict JSON (a small declared allowlist in the Python, not a regex sweep of the tree) and assert each is a property in `agentevent.schema.json`. Cheap, catches exactly this failure, and is honest about being a *name* check rather than a *type* check. The declared list is the load-bearing part — a regex over `.get(\"...\")` calls would be brittle in the way the thing it guards is.\n2. **Generate the TS types.** `docs/wire/agentevent.d.ts` already exists; have `arenabench/ui/lib/types.ts` import from it rather than restate it. Closes the TS half properly and leaves the Python half open.\n3. **Validate a recorded fixture against the schema in arenabench's own tests.** `arenabench/tests/fixtures/matches/**/trajectory.json` are real records; validating a *newly recorded* one against the committed schema would catch a shape change. Note this does NOT catch the present bug on its own — the old fixtures still validate, since the break is that the *reader* wants a key the *new* records no longer carry.\n\nOption 1 is probably the right first step, and it is deliberately not option 3.\n\n## Constraints a fresh agent needs\n\n- **arenabench is standard-library-only by contract** (see #2519, #2520) — a JSON-schema validation dependency is not free and may be disqualifying for option 3.\n- `ci.yml` ignores `docs/**`, which is why `wire-schema.yml` exists as its own workflow. Any new guard needs to trigger on both `docs/wire/**` and `arenabench/**`, or it will not run on the PR that breaks it.\n- The legacy-fallback requirement is real and must survive: recorded fixtures under `arenabench/tests/fixtures/matches/**` carry the *old* spelling and must keep parsing. A guard that demands the new key everywhere would fail on them.\n- `make gate` runs no browser and no Node today; option 2 needs to respect that (`deck-fit.yml` is the precedent for a check that needs a browser living outside the gate).\n\n## Definition of done\n\nA PR that renames or removes a field in `crates/stella-protocol` which arenabench reads **fails a check**, on the PR that does it, naming the consumer that would break — instead of shipping a bench number that is wrong in a way no test reports.\n\n## Related\n\n- #2556 — the rename that exposed this\n- #2814 — the PR, including the fix to the arenabench consumers\n- #2519, #2520 — arenabench's standard-library-only contract"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2820[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Nothing pins arenabench's JSON reads against docs/wire/ — a compile-checked rename silently broke bench scoring"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
