    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`VerifierScopedTools` (`crates/stella-cli/src/agent/goal.rs`, ~L1035) is a `ToolExecutor` decorator\n— it filters the inner executor's schemas and executions to `VERIFIER_TOOL_ALLOWLIST`. The port's\ncontract (`crates/stella-core/src/ports.rs`) states that decorators MUST forward every defaulted\nmethod, because each default is silently wrong for a wrapper and no compiler says so.\n\nIt forwards `drain_sub_agent_spend_usd` (with a comment citing the rule) and, since #2764,\n`live_services`. It does **not** forward:\n\n- `drain_wait_request` — so a parked wait (#1471) deposited by a verifier tool never reaches the\n  engine, and the verifier falls back to burning model steps on polling. `ci_status` is on the\n  verifier's allowlist and is the canonical depositor, so this is not hypothetical: the goal loop's\n  verifier is exactly the agent that waits on CI.\n- `parallel_safe_names` — so sibling calls this view does allow are serialized. Lower impact (the\n  shipped parallel-safe tool is the sub-agent spawn, which is not on the allowlist), but the empty\n  default here is an accident rather than a decision.\n\nNoticed while wiring #2764's forwarding across the decorator set; out of scope for that change,\nwhich only added the new method.\n\n## What to build\n\nForward both, each with the reason a reviewer can check — and if `parallel_safe_names` should stay\nempty (nothing on the allowlist claims it), say so in a comment the way\n`stella_core::ports::ReadOnlyTools` does, so it reads as a decision rather than an omission.\n\n## Verify\n\n`the_production_tool_stack_forwards_wait_requests` in `crates/stella-cli/src/subagent/tests.rs`\npins the *session* stack, which does not include this view. Either extend that harness to compose\n`VerifierScopedTools` too, or add a targeted test in `goal.rs`'s own test module: a base executor\nholding a deposited `WaitRequest`, wrapped in `VerifierScopedTools`, must hand it through.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The allowlist filter must NOT be applied to the forwarded values — a wait request is deposited by\n  a tool this view already permitted, and the filter's job is execution authority, not bookkeeping.\n\n## Done when\n\nEvery defaulted `ToolExecutor` method on this view is either forwarded or carries a comment saying\nwhy it is not, and the wait forwarding has a witness.\n\nRefs #1471, #2764\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Redirected by the turn-loop wrapper architecture (2026-08-16)\n\nDesign: `doc:turn-loop-wrappers` §4. Umbrella: #3380.\n\nThis issue is a real defect and the fix below is still correct. What changes is\nwhere it should live, because this bug is a **symptom of the duplication #3380\nremoves**, not a one-off.\n\n`VerifierScopedTools` is goal mode's own hand-rolled read-only verifier view. The\nstaged pipeline has its own equivalent. They are two implementations of one idea\n— \"the judge sees a read-only tool stack and cannot edit its way to a passing\nverdict\" — and this issue is the two copies having drifted: one forwards\n`drain_wait_request`, the other silently does not.\n\nUnder #3380, goal mode's rounds and the pipeline's revise loop are the same\nwrapper contract, and the judge's read-only view is **one** thing at the `judge`\npoint rather than one per surface.\n\n**So this issue takes one of two shapes, and either is acceptable:**\n\n1. **Fix it now, as written.** Forward both methods, add the witness. Cheap,\n   removes a live defect (`ci_status` is on the verifier allowlist and is the\n   canonical wait depositor, so the goal verifier is exactly the agent that\n   needs this), and it does not make #3380 harder. **Preferred** — do not sit on\n   a shipped bug waiting for an epic.\n2. **Close as moot when #3380 lands**, if the shared judge view arrives first.\n\n**What must not happen:** a fix that adds a *third* scoped-verifier view, or one\nthat hardens `VerifierScopedTools` into a design worth keeping. Whatever lands\nhere should be deletable by #3380 without argument.\n\n**One extra note for whoever picks this up.** The port contract says a decorator\nmust forward every defaulted method because each default is silently wrong for a\nwrapper and no compiler says so. That is a rule enforced by prose, and it has now\nfailed at least twice. When #3380 defines the judge's view, it should make the\nforwarding a compile error instead — that is the durable version of this fix, and\nit belongs in #3380's definition of done rather than here.\n\nRefs #3380, #1471, #2764.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2819[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"cli: VerifierScopedTools swallows drain_wait_request and parallel_safe_names — the goal loop's verifier cannot park or fan out"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
