    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nThis is the second half of #2570's \"Done when\", split out because it cannot be\ndone inside `crates/stella-store/` alone: the store has nowhere to learn about\ndelivery, and the crate that does know (`stella-cli`) has nowhere to put it.\n\nExecution 99 is recorded as `outcome = 'cancelled'`. What happened is that the\nworker had already pushed and merged PR #2554 before the cancel landed. The\nrecord says a cancelled run that (after #2570's cost fix) cost $5.29; the truth\nis a $5.29 run that shipped a merged PR. `outcome` is a single terminal label\nand it is being asked to describe two independent facts:\n\n- **how the run ended** (completed / aborted / cancelled / failed / error), and\n- **whether it delivered anything** (a commit, a push, an opened or merged PR).\n\nThose are orthogonal. A completed run can deliver nothing; a cancelled run can\ndeliver everything. Collapsing them means every analysis that filters on\n`outcome = 'completed'` — `usage_stats`'s `resolved` count\n(`crates/stella-store/src/export.rs`), the scoreboard, cost-per-resolved-task,\nand the responsibility-ablation controls #2374 needs — silently scores delivered\nwork as zero.\n\n## What exists today\n\n- `executions.outcome` — `crates/stella-store/src/ddl.rs` (`EXECUTIONS_DDL`).\n- `pull_requests` — already in the schema, but keyed by **session**\n  (`upsert_pull_request`), not by execution, so it cannot answer \"did *this*\n  turn deliver?\".\n- `files_touched` / `tool_calls` per execution — evidence of local edits, but\n  not of a commit or a push.\n\nSo the fact is partially derivable and nowhere recorded.\n\n## Suggested shape\n\n1. Add an execution-scoped delivery record to `stella-store` — a nullable\n   column (`delivered_at` / a small `delivery` kind enum) or an\n   `execution_delivery` table keyed on `execution_id`, with a migration in\n   `crates/stella-store/src/migrations.rs` and the DDL in `src/ddl.rs`. Keep it\n   additive; `executions` rows written before the migration must read as\n   \"unknown\", not \"did not deliver\".\n2. Wire the writer in `stella-cli` where commits/pushes/PRs are already\n   observed (the `pr_nudge` reconcile in `command_deck.rs`, `fleet` commit\n   ledger, the git tool call sites).\n3. Decide explicitly whether `usage_stats.resolved` should count a delivered\n   cancelled run. Changing it moves every published cost-per-resolved number,\n   so it wants to be a stated decision with a witness, not a side effect.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Invariant #3: if this reaches the enterprise rollup or the hub, the new\n  column must be added to the reviewed allowlist in\n  `crates/stella-store/src/content_free.rs` in the same PR, with an argument\n  that a delivery *flag* is not content. A PR **number** or URL is closer to\n  content than a boolean is — prefer the boolean unless there is a named\n  consumer for more.\n- `crates/stella-store/src/lib.rs`, `src/tests.rs`, `src/usage.rs` and\n  `crates/stella-cli/src/command_deck.rs` are grandfathered god files closed to\n  growth (AGENTS.md § God files) — new logic goes in sibling modules.\n- Invariant #10: whatever signal this emits names its consumer in\n  `crates/stella-protocol/src/event/consumers.rs` if it rides an `AgentEvent`.\n\n## Done when\n\nA run that pushed a commit or opened a PR before being cancelled records that\nit delivered, a reader can distinguish \"ended early and shipped nothing\" from\n\"ended early and shipped a merged PR\" without inferring it from absence, and a\nwitness test fails on today's code.\n\nRefs #2570, #2374.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2808[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"store/cli: record what an execution delivered, separately from its outcome — a cancelled run that merged a PR reads as pure loss"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
