    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n#2570 fixed the **persisted** number: `executions.cost_usd` is now kept at or\nabove the sum of the execution's `telemetry` receipts, both as each receipt\nlands (`Store::record_telemetry`) and again at close-out\n(`Store::finish_execution_accounted`) — see\n`crates/stella-store/src/telemetry.rs`.\n\nIt did **not** fix the number the driver computes and shows. On the deck's\ncancel path the cost handed to the store — and printed to the user, and\nreturned to callers — is still the truncated in-memory aggregate:\n\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/command_deck.rs:2234`\n  ```rust\n  let cancelled_cost =\n      agent::settled_cost_since(dispatch_spend_usd, budget.session_spent_usd());\n  ```\n  `dispatch_spend_usd` is captured at `command_deck.rs:1595`. When the turn\n  future is dropped mid-cancel, the roles still settling (worker, witness\n  author — the expensive ones) have not folded into `budget.session_spent_usd()`,\n  so this delta is the pre-cancel stage prefix. Execution 99 in #2570:\n  `$0.8659773` reported against `$5.28786465` of receipts, an exact\n  triage+research+plan prefix.\n\n- The same call site does not await the forwarder drain before closing the\n  row. `spawn_forwarder`'s `JoinHandle` and the event `tx` are created inside\n  `run_lead_turn` (`command_deck.rs:4162`), and `close_turn_stream`\n  (`crates/stella-cli/src/command_deck/forwarder.rs:172`) — the only thing that\n  awaits the forwarder — lives inside that same future, which the cancel drops.\n  So the last calls' `StepUsage` events can be persisted (and priced) *after*\n  `record_execution_end` has already run.\n\nThe store now survives both of those (the per-receipt floor heals a late\nreceipt after close-out), but everything that reads the driver's own figure\ninstead of the row still under-reports: the deck's cost display, the\n`cancelled_cost` argument itself, and any caller of\n`PipelineOutcome::total_cost_usd` / `WorkerOutcome::cost_usd` on a cancelled\npath.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nSame reason as #2570: the bias is one-directional and worst on the most\nexpensive runs, and it is the number a human sees on screen at the moment they\ncancel. A user reading `$0.87` for a run that cost `$5.29` is being misinformed\nby the surface even though the database is now right.\n\n## Suggested shape\n\nTwo independent fixes, either of which helps:\n\n1. Read the truth back instead of recomputing it: after the store closeout,\n   take `Store::execution_settled_cost_usd(execution_id)` (or re-read\n   `execution_summary(...).cost_usd`, which is now the floor over both sources)\n   as the figure to display and return.\n2. Drain before closing: give the cancel path a way to await the forwarder —\n   the pieces `close_turn_stream` needs (`tx`, the `JoinHandle`,\n   `registry.detach_event_stream()`) are owned by `run_lead_turn`, so this\n   likely means hoisting them to the driver loop or handing the cancel path a\n   drain handle. Note #2290 is the reason `detach_event_stream()` exists;\n   whatever shape this takes must not reintroduce the wedge it fixed.\n\n## Verify\n\nWitness in `crates/stella-cli/`: drive a turn that persists receipts for\nseveral roles, cancel it, and assert the cost the driver reports equals the\nreceipts total — not the prefix. The store-side witnesses in\n`crates/stella-store/src/telemetry.rs`\n(`a_cancelled_execution_reports_every_receipt_it_paid_for`,\n`a_receipt_landing_after_closeout_still_raises_the_rollup`) show the shape and\nalready pass, so a failure here is unambiguously the driver's number.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/command_deck.rs` and `src/agent.rs` are grandfathered\n  god files closed to growth (AGENTS.md § God files) — new logic goes in a\n  sibling module.\n- Do not lower `executions.cost_usd`: it is a floor over both the receipts and\n  the caller's aggregate, deliberately (see `finish_execution_accounted`'s doc).\n\n## Done when\n\nThe cost a cancelled turn reports on screen and returns to its callers agrees\nwith the receipts the run actually paid for, with a witness test that fails on\ntoday's code.\n\nRefs #2570, #2290.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2807[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"cli: the cancelled turn's in-memory cost is still the pre-cancel prefix — only the persisted row was fixed by #2570"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
