    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Standing tracker for issues that pass triage's other five facets but have no epic whose stated outcome actually contains theirs. Per `/backlog-triage`'s contract, an orphan keeps the `triage` label rather than being force-parented into a thin single-issue epic. Each row explains why nothing fit.\n\n**Last reconciled: the 2026-08-12 evening sweep** (26 issues in the `triage` queue worked; 5 new epics created, absorbing 17 issues that would otherwise have landed here; 4 orphans confirmed). This sweep also pruned the table: **12 of the 15 rows below it were closed by the 2026-08-12 mission-scope backlog sweep** and are recorded at the bottom rather than left standing as current orphans.\n\n## Current orphans\n\n| # | Reason no epic fit |\n|---|---|\n| #2837 | Standalone as of this sweep. Its former two-issue cluster partner #2795 (source-scan parity that would have caught these markers mechanically) was closed on 2026-08-12, so the pairing that put it below the 3-issue bar is gone and it is now strictly alone. Still **not** #2701: that epic's scope is the `AgentEvent` variant→consumer ledger (`consumers.rs` / `KNOWN_TYPE_TAGS`), a different mechanism from `engine_markers.rs`'s constant→table completeness. The natural parent #2722 is an open issue, not an epic, and Facet 6 requires an epic. |\n| #2838 | Standalone: #2685's three declared, documented follow-ups (non-`read_file` reads, fence collision in chained skill bodies, the budget-abort arm). #2685 was itself excluded from #2694 by that epic's own scope, so its residue inherits the exclusion, and no epic covers overflow-summarization working-set restoration. Re-checked against the five epics created this sweep — none of them contains it. |\n| #2889 | Standalone: the experiment plane (hypotheses / experiments / datasets / runs / traces as first-class linked objects) is epic-shaped in size but still has no sibling issues to parent under it; promoting it to `epic` type with zero children is the dishonest hierarchy this rule forbids (confirmed for the third time this sweep). **Nearest miss re-examined and rejected:** the new #3049 (a fetched bench run reads itself) covers the *analysis* chain — fetch → assemble → replay → postmortem — over one run's artifacts on disk. #2889 is a durable cross-run **lineage schema** in `stella-store` plus a CLI to query it. Same subject matter, different outcome; folding one into the other would make both untrue. Still worth a maintainer decision on whether to decompose it into children, which would legitimately earn it a home. |\n| #3012 | New this sweep. ArenaBench has no seat path for seven CLI agents outside Harbor 0.6.1's factory (Factory Droid, Kilo Code, OpenClaw, Sourcegraph Amp, xAI Grok CLI, Xiaomi Mimo, Google Antigravity). Only one candidate sibling — #1584 (N contestants and solo runs, per-seat voiding, non-comparative reporting) — which is two, below the bar. **Not** #2775: that epic's outcome is that an *existing* arm's telemetry, credentials and infra state are captured correctly so a comparison is trustworthy; seating a new agent adds a contestant rather than making a measurement honest. |\n\n## Closed by the 2026-08-12 mission-scope sweep\n\nTwelve rows left this table without being parented or fixed: they were closed `not planned` as work that does not serve the four mission goals (beat Claude Code head-to-head at matched config, be cheaper, be more explainable, ship dataset generation for open-weight models). Recorded here because \"an orphan was closed as out of scope\" is a different outcome from \"an orphan found a home\", and the distinction is the thing this tracker exists to preserve.\n\n#2527 #2563 #2598 #2629 #2630 #2658 #2725 #2726 #2795 #2796 #2862 #2866\n\nOne of them has since been re-filed with a mission tie: **#2796 → #2985** (`prompt.rs` against the 1500-line ceiling), now a child of #2694 because #3031 §4 makes the split the strict blocking prerequisite of the cross-tool-steering series. That is the closing comment's own invitation — \"reopen with a mission-tie if that's wrong\" — taken up, and it is the pattern to follow for any other row above that turns out to block mission work.\n\n## Resolved since the follow-up sweep\n\n| # | Now parented under | Why the earlier orphan call no longer holds |\n|---|---|---|\n| #2733 | #2776 — provider resilience: transport, overflow, streaming-fallback completeness | #2776 didn't exist (or wasn't yet scoped this way) when #2733 was first triaged orphan; breaker feedback not reaching bare engine sites is squarely a resilience-completeness gap. |\n| #2761 | #2694 — tool-first architecture / context-record contract polish | Promotion-tier follow-ups (cumulative footprint accounting, review printout, spec docs) are the direct continuation of #2694's context-record contract work, not #2772's narrower model-verifier-removal scope. |\n| #2836 | #2816 — interactive approval flow completeness | UserPromptSubmit's deny/modify-before-turn-build is the same host-obligation gate shape #2816 already covers; re-read this sweep found the fit the earlier pass missed. |\n| #2854 | — closed, not planned | Already fixed on `main`: `GrantedTools` forwards both `drain_wait_request` and `live_services` (`crates/stella-core/src/ports.rs:339-357`), landed in PR #2787 (commit c13b763cc). The issue's premise no longer holds. |\n\n## Resolved since the 2026-08-10 sweep\n\nTen rows left this table in the 2026-08-12 sweep. Eight dissolved because the 55 issues filed since 2026-08-10 supplied the siblings they lacked — the orphan judgment was correct when made and stopped being correct when the population changed:\n\n| # | Now parented under | Sibling that arrived |\n|---|---|---|\n| #2533 | #2949 — every configured check actually runs | #2847, #2894, #2910 |\n| #2570 | #2952 — the trace faithfully records what a run did and cost | #2831, #2907, #2934, #2942 |\n| #2603 | #2948 — the test suite is deterministic under parallel load | #2757, #2804 |\n| #2757 | #2948 | #2603, #2804 |\n| #2804 | #2948 | #2603, #2757 |\n| #2802 | #2951 — MCP client surface completeness | #2834 |\n| #2803 | #2951 | #2834 |\n| #2589 | #2815 — candidate workspace lifecycle correctness | re-read, not a new sibling: `repo_recover` is the recovery surface #2815's outcome depends on |\n\nTwo more left on re-reading rather than on new evidence:\n\n- **#2738** → #2694. That epic's own \"why now\" section names web search and fetch-with-extraction as Claude Code's separating tool-shaped behaviors, which is exactly this issue's P7 half.\n- **#2800** → #2694. Previously deferred to #2716 (an open issue, not an epic); #2716 is itself the governance half of #2694, so the epic is a legitimate ancestor.\n\n**#2685 and #2764 are removed from the table because both are now closed.**\n\n## Note on epics referenced above that have since closed\n\n#2948 (test suite deterministic under parallel load) and #2951 (MCP client surface completeness) were both closed `wontfix` in the 2026-08-12 mission sweep, along with their children. The rows naming them are kept as history, not as live parenting.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2778[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Triage defect: unparented issues"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Outcome\nThe verification ladder's every signal, prompt, and evidence artifact must accurately reflect what was actually verified — no fabricated review claims, no lost detail folded away, no irreversible waived-witness holes, no dead or contradictory evidence flags. This is the cluster CLAUDE.md's \"a bench conclusion comes from the trace, never a surface signal\" rule exists to prevent.\n\n## Definition of done\n- A triage-time `WITNESS: no` is recoverable once the warrant, post-execution, wants one (#2530).\n- The revise prompt carries the witness source and its failing invocation (#2542).\n- `flip_achieved` is a tri-state, not a bool that conflates \"never ran\" with \"ran and failed\" (#2556).\n- The witness author no longer re-derives repo test conventions on every run at ~$0.67/run for zero tests written (#2559).\n- `opaque_actions > 0` no longer short-circuits path-rule waivers before they run (#2560).\n- The PROOF panel folds all 5 ladder findings, not 3 (#2567).\n- `LadderDecision::Unverified` no longer emits `AgentEvent::Verdict{passed:true}` (#2569).\n- Diff-coverage/witness-tautology guards keep feeding correctly once the witness author is removed (#2607).\n- The evidence-demand prompt stops claiming \"your work was reviewed and looks correct\" when nothing reviewed it (#2619).\n- The two completion paths sharing one deterministic predicate emit one non-contradictory `deterministic` flag (#2620).\n- The diagnostics-veto UNVERIFIED path reports its specific shortfall, not a generic fallthrough (#2640).\n\n## Children\n#2530 #2542 #2556 #2559 #2560 #2567 #2569 #2607 #2619 #2620 #2640\n\n\n## Children adopted in the 2026-08-12 triage sweep\n\nEleven more issues share this outcome. #2912/#2913 are the measured finding that the worker authors better oracles than `witness_author` and the design call it forces; #2929 is the ladder driving a worker to delete a correct deliverable; #2839/#2841 are the unfinished half of #2569, already a child here; the rest are witness-artifact and vacuity-screen fidelity.\n\n#2821 #2822 #2823 #2824 #2839 #2840 #2841 #2912 #2913 #2917 #2929\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Alignment note — this outcome survives, its landing site changes (2026-08-16)\n\nDesign: `doc:turn-loop-wrappers` §4. Refs #3380, #3381.\n\nNothing in this epic's outcome or definition of done changes. Every child here\nis about evidence telling the truth, and that is a permanent requirement.\n\nWhat changes is **where a fix is allowed to land**.\n\nThe turn-loop wrapper architecture makes the staged pipeline a plugin over a\nfour-point contract (`before_turn` / `after_turn` / `judge` / `again?`, #3380),\nwith its stage sequence declared in a manifest rather than in code (#3381). The\nverification ladder is that contract's `judge`, and witness authoring is\n`after_turn`.\n\n**Two constraints for anyone picking up a child of this epic**\n\n1. **Do not grow `crates/stella-pipeline/src/pipeline.rs`.** It is on the\n   god-file list in `scripts/file-size-baseline.txt` and is closed to growth.\n   That was already true; it is now also the wrong place structurally, because\n   that file is being taken apart into a manifest plus four bound points. Land\n   in a sibling module, or behind the point the fix actually belongs to.\n2. **A fix that adds a new stage should wait for #3381**, or land as a\n   sibling that can become a manifest entry without a redesign. A hardcoded\n   conditional branch added now is work that gets deleted twice.\n\n**One child is load-bearing for the wrapper contract and worth pulling\nforward:** `flip_achieved` as a tri-state rather than a bool (#2556). `judge`\nturns evidence into a verdict with no model call, so the evidence has to be able\nto say \"never ran\" separately from \"ran and failed\". A bool cannot, and a\ndeterministic judge reading a lossy input is a deterministic wrong answer.\n\n**What does not change, and is not up for renegotiation by any of this:**\nverification buys no model call; the witness author is the one surviving\nverifier-tier call because it builds the measuring stick; a different model\nwrites the test, blind to the change, with three tools; tampering voids credit.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2773[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Epic: verification ladder evidence integrity"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
