    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`Engine::settle_model_call_failure` (crates/stella-core/src/driver/overflow_recovery.rs) has two recovery rungs that never compose: a `ContextOverflow` whose 2-rung compaction ladder is spent aborts terminally, even though a configured fallback provider (#2679, `driver/model_fallback.rs`) may carry a larger context window that would accept the transcript as-is.\n\n## Why it was left out of #2679\n\nDeliberate scoping: #2752 classified an oversized request as \"the engine's accounting miss, not provider ill-health\" — it does not feed the breaker, so a router re-resolution has no signal to route around the small-window provider, and blindly swapping could burn a paid call on a same-size window. Composing the rungs needs a decision: either window-size-aware resolution (the router's `ProviderProfile` does not carry window size today) or an explicit \"last rung: try the fallback once\" with the same latch discipline.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/stella-core/src/driver/overflow_recovery.rs` — the `None` arm of `state.overflow_recovery.arm(...)` is the seam; `self.attempt_provider_fallback(...)` is one call away.\n- `crates/stella-core/src/router.rs` — `ProviderProfile` would need a window-size field for the informed variant.\n\n## Verify / done\n\nA witness in `crates/stella-core/src/driver/tests/` mirroring `context_overflow.rs`: a provider that always rejects with `ContextOverflow`, a fallback that accepts, spent ladder → swap → turn completes; plus the bound test (fallback also overflows → terminal, no loop). The one-swap-per-engine latch from #2679 must remain the single bound.\n\nRefs #2679, #2680, #2752, #2765"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2770[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"overflow recovery: when the compaction ladder is spent, consider the mid-turn provider fallback before aborting"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
