    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Why this issue exists\n\n#2671 bundled two problem areas. The accounting half of P8 — token estimates running ~1.8x low and mis-timing compaction — is fixed by anchoring context-size accounting to provider-reported usage (#2681, PR forthcoming), and that PR closes #2671 per the build plan's closing discipline. Everything else in #2671 is still real and lands here so it is not stranded by the close. Full evidence and transcripts: see #2671's body (bench runs `turnloop-rerun-bare` build-pov-ray vs `ccglm-bar-A`).\n\n## P7 — retrieval gap (unchanged from #2671)\n\nStella has no web-search tool and `web_fetch` cannot fetch bytes. On build-pov-ray the bare run burned 51 `web_fetch` calls scraping SERP HTML, mis-shaped a Wayback CDX query, fetched a 404 and abandoned the correct path; CC-on-GLM solved the same task in 31 steps with `WebSearch` + `WebFetch` + an extraction prompt.\n\nFix directions (from #2671):\n- a real `web_search` tool (`crates/stella-tools/`, implement the `Tool` trait, register in `ToolRegistry` — see that crate's README extension recipe);\n- `web_fetch` binary/output-file mode and an extraction-prompt mode;\n- a vintage-artifact retrieval skill (Wayback CDX -> `<TS>id_/` raw URL);\n- after N failed retrievals against one host/query family, change query SHAPE.\n\nConstraint: any new tool output must stay deterministic — never put timings or other nondeterministic values in `ToolOutput` content (the loop detector keys on it).\n\n## P8 leftovers not covered by the usage anchor\n\n- **Progress-aware step cap**: the per-turn step cap (16) fired mid-investigation (\"reached the step cap (16) without completing\"). Seam: `max_steps` / `step_cap_reason` in `crates/stella-core/src/driver.rs`.\n- **Cost persisted on timeout**: `complete.cost_usd == 0` on all 11 timeout trials — cost telemetry lost exactly where it matters. Seams: the abort/timeout paths in `crates/stella-core/src/driver.rs` and how the bench harness reads the store.\n- **Fewer, larger compaction passes that actually summarize**: 8 compaction events on one trial, all `summarized: 0, evicted: 0`, reclaiming ~10% each. The usage anchor fixes the *timing* input; whether the passes reclaim enough once they fire (`crates/stella-core/src/compaction.rs` hysteresis, `summarize_overflow_span`) should be re-measured on a bench run after #2681 lands and tuned only if the thrash persists.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nEach bullet lands as its own PR with a witness test (or a named bench re-measurement for the compaction-thrash bullet). Verify P8 leftovers against fresh `stella-events.jsonl` traces, not summary projections.\n\nRefs #2671, #2681."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2738[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Carve-out from #2671: P7 web retrieval (web_search tool, web_fetch byte/extraction modes) and P8 leftovers (progress-aware step cap, cost persisted on timeout, larger compaction passes)"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
