    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem (two small, related worker-behavior defects, one issue)\n\n**P4 — example over-fit + self-confirming verification.** extract-elf bare: Stella derived a +0x400000 rebase from the task's example output, then itself concluded \"the example values are generic illustrations, not from this file\" — and KEPT the offset, then \"verified\" 698/698 against its own model. CC emitted vaddr as-is and passed; a one-constant diff after 100% of the work. build-pov-ray bare: 2 of 3 tests passed (SSIM 0.873); failed only on `file_id.diz not found` — its own zip's members were uppercase (`FILE_ID.DIZ`, proven by its own S150). `unzip -LL` or a filename-case check flips the cell. 2/16 cells, both one-line diffs.\n\n**P6 — the 120s bash wall + no persistent state.** path-tracing: three identical-shape `timeout 110/115 python3 <<EOF` kills in a row; then discovers numpy missing at second ~1676; then `pip: command not found`; never tries `apt-get install python3-numpy` (apt worked in the same dataset). Every step re-parses the 48MB PPM from scratch (verbatim parse in S36–S54, ~2s each); CC cached to `/tmp/img.bin` once. Same re-parse pattern in raman-fitting (8 steps). Loop detector inconsistency: 38 byte-identical `read_output`/`send_stdin` polls unflagged (qemu) while 3 identical calls elsewhere drew a warning. 4/16 cells' dominant time sink.\n\n## Fix directions\n\nP4: (a) prompt/skill rule — \"if your output disagrees with a task-supplied example, treat it as your defect until proven synthetic; never keep a transform derived from an example you then invalidated\"; (b) done-check on deliverable shape (filename case, path, extension); (c) verification must compare against task ground truth, never a re-derivation of the agent's own model.\nP6: (a) escalating command timeout the model can request, and exit-124 responses that direct a strategy change instead of a resubmit; (b) a persistent scratch/session store (or a warm `python` tool) so parsed data survives steps; (c) turn-0 environment capability probe (interpreters, pip/apt, numpy, file/xxd/ps, network); (d) loop-detector thresholds for read_output/send_stdin polling.\n\nEvidence: `turnloop-rerun-bare` extract-elf/build-pov-ray; `turnloop-cert-panel1` + `turnloop-rerun-pipe2` path-tracing/raman transcripts; `ccglm-bar-B` contrasts.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
