    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench cloud watch <run-id>` renders every cell `UNKNOWN` (\"0 of 16 trials settled\") for a run whose trials have all finished and written results. Observed 2026-08-10 against run `turnloop-cert-panel1` (16 completed trials, results fetched fine by `cloud fetch`).\n\n`arenabench/cloud_watch.py` documents its contract as \"Batch job states plus `runs/<id>/<job>/results.json` in S3\", but the runner's artifact sync writes per-trial output under `runs/<run-id>/<ddb-uuid>/…` (UUID job ids, with the per-trial `results.json` nested inside the synced work tree), and the per-trial match tomls under `runs/<run-id>/trials/<job-name>/match.toml`. Whatever key shape `cloud_watch` derives, it is not finding the settled results — so the one surface meant to watch a cloud run live shows nothing, before or after completion.\n\n`cloud fetch` resolves results correctly (it goes through the DDB rows), so the fix is probably to make `cloud_watch` resolve results the same way `fetch` does rather than guessing S3 keys.\n\n## Repro\n\n1. `uv run arenabench cloud watch turnloop-cert-panel1 --port 8377 --no-browser`\n2. `curl localhost:8377` → header says \"0 of 16 trials settled\", every task cell `UNKNOWN`, reward row `0.0` for both seats — for a run that scored 16 trials.\n\n## Done looks like\n\n`cloud watch` on a finished run shows the same rewards `cloud fetch` + `results.json` show; on a live run, cells settle as trials finish. A unit test pinning the S3/DDB key shape shared with `fetch` would witness it.\n\nRefs #2656 (the run used to observe this), #2113 (array-job submission may change key shapes again — coordinate).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2660[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench cloud watch: every cell UNKNOWN for a finished run — results key shape disagrees with what the runner syncs"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
