    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench run` wires an **ambient** credential into a seat that declared none — the exact bypass #1827's last constraint says must not exist, and the exact outcome `test_an_ambient_subscription_token_never_reaches_a_seat` was written to prevent. The server path is correct; the CLI path is not, so the two disagree.\n\n`cli.py`'s `run` docstring states the contract it breaks:\n\n> The layers are the server's, in the server's order, on purpose: a template that launches from the UI and the same template run here must resolve the same credentials, or \"reproduces this match exactly\" is false in the one place nobody checks.\n\nThey do not resolve the same credentials.\n\n* `arenabench/arenabench/server.py:431` calls `apply_ambient_credentials(spec)`, which fills from `contestant.required_env` — **declared names only** (`arenabench/arenabench/credentials.py:114-143`). Its docstring is explicit that this is the one sanctioned exception to the seat env scrub.\n* `arenabench/arenabench/cli.py:105-111` does its own inline ambient fill from `required_env(spec)` — declared names **or**, for an undeclared seat, the provider/agent-derived candidate set (`arenabench/arenabench/config.py:375-398`).\n\nFor an undeclared seat the derived set includes `alt_credential_env`, i.e. the Claude subscription token. So a `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` exported in the operator's shell silently credentials an undeclared `claude-code` seat via `arenabench run`, and does not via the UI.\n\nThat is verbatim the hazard the guard test's own docstring names: *\"a token exported in the operator's shell silently credentials every Claude Code seat — two arms you believed were on different credentials, both on the plan.\"* The existing guard only asserts on `_base_environment()` (`arenabench/tests/test_arena.py:794`), so it never sees this second route.\n\n## Reproduce\n\nRuns offline, no containers, no keys — the token below is a literal.\n\n```python\nimport os\nfrom arenabench.agents import resolve_agent\nfrom arenabench.config import required_env\nfrom arenabench.credentials import apply_ambient_credentials\nfrom arenabench.model import Contestant, Engine, MatchSpec\n\nos.environ[\"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\"] = \"sk-ant-oat-ambient\"\n\nseat = Contestant(\n    id=\"cc\", name=\"Claude Code (declares nothing)\", agent=\"claude-code\",\n    engine=Engine(api=\"anthropic\", model=\"claude-fable-5\"),\n)\nspec = MatchSpec(id=\"probe\", name=\"probe\", dataset=\"terminal-bench-2.1\",\n                 tasks=(\"fix-git\",), contestants=(seat,))\n\nderived = required_env(spec)[seat.id]\nprint(\"derived      :\", derived)\nprint(\"server path  :\", sorted(apply_ambient_credentials(spec).contestants[0].env))\nprint(\"`run` path   :\", sorted(n for n in derived if os.environ.get(n)))\n```\n\nObserved on `045f1735a`:\n\n```\nclaude-code alt_credential_env  : ('CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN',)\nderived      : ['ANTHROPIC_API_KEY', 'ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN', 'CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN']\nserver path  : []\n`run` path   : ['CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN']\n```\n\nThe same shape reproduces for a metered provider key: an undeclared `openrouter` Stella seat picks up an ambient `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` through `run` and nothing through the server.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nTwo ways, and the second is the expensive one:\n\n1. **Credential isolation.** A template that withholds a metered key from one arm on purpose (#1777's stated reason for the declaration mechanism) does not withhold it under `arenabench run` if that arm declares nothing — the derived set hands it over.\n2. **The comparison silently changes.** A head-to-head where both arms resolve to the operator's ambient subscription token measures one account's rate limit, not two agent architectures. Nothing in the output says so; #1827 already records that the only signal on the lenient path is a `run.warnings` line.\n\n## What done looks like\n\n`cli.py`'s `run` calls `apply_ambient_credentials(spec)` instead of its inline loop, so both paths share one implementation of \"which ambient names may a seat receive\". The refusal check below it may keep using `required_env(spec)`'s derived set — #1827 explicitly allows the *refusal* to consider derived names while the *fill* stays declaration-only, and those are separate decisions.\n\nWatch for the behaviour change this is: a hand-written template with no `[contestant.env] required` that works today via `arenabench run` will stop being credentialled. That is the intended correction, but it wants a clear error rather than a silent 0.0 — the `missing` block at `cli.py:130-141` only reports seats with a non-empty declared list, so an undeclared seat currently falls through it entirely. Fix both together or the change trades a quiet mis-credential for a quiet un-credential.\n\n## Tests\n\n* A witness in `arenabench/tests/test_credentials.py` mirroring `test_an_ambient_subscription_token_never_reaches_a_seat`, but exercising the **CLI fill layer**: ambient `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` + an undeclared `claude-code` seat, asserting the seat's resolved `env` stays empty. It fails on `main` today.\n* A parity test asserting the server path and the `run` path resolve identical `contestant.env` for the same spec — the contract `cli.py`'s docstring already claims and nothing checks.\n* Check no existing test in `arenabench/tests/` relies on an undeclared seat being ambient-credentialled through `run`.\n\n## Notes\n\n* Committed templates under `arenabench/matches/` all declare `[contestant.env] required`, and `dump_match` re-emits a resolved `required` list for every seat (`config.py:493`), so generated templates declare too. Exposure is hand-written or hand-edited templates that omit the table — which is exactly what an operator writes first.\n* Found while building `scripts/arena-local.sh`, which had to replay the CLI's fill layers to report which credential reaches which seat; the two implementations disagreeing is what surfaced it.\n\nRefs #1777, #1825, #1827.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2654[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: `arenabench run` wires an ambient credential into an undeclared seat; the server does not"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
