    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nOn TB2.1 `fix-git`, every scored loss on recent builds has the same shape: the\nworker does its work inside a **candidate shadow worktree**\n(`/tmp/stella_candidate_N_0`), the run ends abnormally on the turn budget, and\nthe work is **never promoted to the graded tree** at `/app/personal-site`. The\nexternal verifier hashes two files in the graded tree, so a correct fix that\nlives only in the candidate scores exactly the same as no work at all: **0.0**.\n\nThe measured cost is not marginal. The one trial that never entered a candidate\nworkspace solved the task **in 417s**; every trial that did took **823–895s**\nagainst an **840s turn budget** (`--turn-budget 840`, reserving 60s of the\ntask's 900s for the verifier). The candidate roughly doubles wall clock on this\ntask and then consumes the margin that would have absorbed the risk.\n\n### Evidence\n\nTraced from `stella-events.jsonl` in each trial (ground truth, not the\nscoreboard). \"Candidate engaged\" is the first `repo_status` whose\n`worktree.candidate_shadow` flips true — it engages mid-run, not at startup:\n\n| match / trial | candidate engaged | promoted | reward | wall |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `c5a0d49b59da` / `fix-git__QS5Uz8y` | yes @27s | no | **0** | 823s |\n| `2e6f8455a471` / `fix-git__jg8vZ6M` | yes @107s | no | **0** | 855s |\n| `8bb068165b08` / `fix-git__BLZvkHR` | yes @45s | `repo_push` @664s | 1 | 895s |\n| `f9693a9d460d` / `fix-git__mX3gZBt` | **never** | n/a | 1 | **417s** |\n\nAll four ran Sonnet 5 / xhigh / full pipeline. SUTs `703976eba` and `868af3e05`.\n\n`c5a0d49b59da` is the clearest trace. It **solved the task at 288s and then\nbacked the solution out**:\n\n```\n 27s  repo_status                       -> lists unreachable c499730 \"Move to Stanford\" (the target)\n288s  git branch -f master c499730      -> the correct fix, applied\n334s  git update-ref refs/heads/master d7d3e4b   -> \"restored\" — backs it out\n371s..823s  490s re-verifying the same ancestry facts; never retries the fix\n840s  turn budget -> DeliberateStopError -> repo_push never called -> reward 0\n```\n\nIts verifier failure is the graded file never changing at all:\n\n```\nAssertionError: File /app/personal-site/_includes/about.md is not in the correct state\nassert '86f5f5d1de3e...' == '0273104059c6...'\n```\n\n### Why this task collides with the candidate design\n\n`fix-git`'s solution is **moving a branch pointer** (`master` to a merge of the\ndangling `c499730`), not a file edit. Two consequences:\n\n1. The candidate is a **linked worktree sharing the graded tree's ref\n   namespace**, so the correct answer *is itself a ref escape* — the exact\n   conflict #2641 describes from the guard's side. The 288s→334s\n   apply-then-revert above is a worker walking into that wall and retreating\n   with no legal path forward.\n2. Candidate adoption is diff-based (`git apply`; see the `candidate_ws` module\n   doc's \"Boundaries\"). A ref move does not travel in a diff. For *this* task a\n   file-level diff would in fact satisfy the verifier (it only hashes\n   `_includes/about.md` and `_layouts/default.html`), but the worker is\n   reasoning about refs, not files, because refs are what the task is about.\n\nNote also that **whether a candidate engages at all varies run to run** on\nidentical config — `mX3gZBt` never got one. That nondeterminism is unexplained\nand is part of what needs establishing below.\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/candidate_ws.rs` — shadow creation, the\n  `stella: candidate baseline snapshot` commit, and the\n  `WITNESS_BASELINE_WORKTREE_REF` pin (around L560-590); winner adoption\n- `crates/stella-tools/src/repo.rs` L532-551 — `candidate_shadow` is derived\n  purely from the presence of `WITNESS_BASELINE_WORKTREE_REF`\n- `crates/stella-tools/src/verify.rs` L169 — the ref constant\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/candidate_ws/ref_escape.rs` — the refuse-without-repair\n  guard (#2641)\n\n## Reproduce / verify\n\nArtifacts are on the bench box under `~/.arenabench/matches/<id>/jobs/*stella*/fix-git__*/`:\n\n```\nagent/stella-events.jsonl   # ground truth: stages, errors, tool_start/result\nverifier/reward.txt         # 0 or 1\nverifier/ctrf.json          # which graded assertion failed\nexception.txt               # DeliberateStopError on the losses\n```\n\nA fresh run is `arenabench run` with a Stella-only fix-git match; see\n`~/.arenabench/tip-fixgit-x3.toml`. Census the workspace mode with:\n\n```\nrg -o '\"candidate_shadow\":(true|false)' agent/stella-events.jsonl | head\n```\n\n## Constraints already discovered\n\n- **Do not \"fix\" this by having the candidate write refs into the real repo.**\n  That is deliberately forbidden (`candidate_ws` module doc, \"Boundaries\"), and\n  #2641 explains why silently rewriting a user's branch on a mis-attribution is\n  worse than the damage it repairs.\n- **Do not raise the turn budget to make the symptom go away.** 840s of a 900s\n  task budget is the harness contract, it is what Claude Code is measured\n  against, and raising it measures a different benchmark. CC solves this task in\n  114-199s.\n- No `budget_usd` / `max_tokens` on any bench run (standing order) — those are\n  absent from the match files on purpose.\n- Feature freeze #2374 is in force; this is bug-fix / reliability work, which\n  the directive keeps in scope.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n1. Establish **why the candidate engages on some runs and not others** on\n   identical config — that nondeterminism is the first thing a fix has to\n   stand on.\n2. A run that ends on the turn budget with correct work in the candidate must\n   either **promote that work** or **report plainly that it discarded it**.\n   Silently scoring identical to \"did nothing\" is the defect.\n3. A witness test that fails on current `main` and passes with the change —\n   ideally at the `candidate_ws` seam rather than through a paid bench trial.\n4. Re-measure `fix-git` x3 on the tip SUT and report the pass count against the\n   pre-change baseline recorded above (2 losses in 4 traced trials).\n\nRelated: #2641 (ref-escape refusal does not repair), #2600 (`pipeline_candidates`\nis allow-listed but unreachable from arenabench, so the candidate count cannot\ncurrently be controlled from a match file), #2374 (prove-value: this is\nmeasured evidence about whether the candidate workspace earns its keep on a\nref-moving task).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2651[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"candidate_ws: work done in the candidate is silently discarded when the turn budget ends the run — a solved fix-git scores 0, and the candidate doubles wall clock on the task"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
