    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n#2580 settled that the bare step loop (`stella run --no-pipeline`) losing sub-agent\ndelegation was collateral from #2410's `task` group key, not a decision, and its\ndefinition of done asks for a bench arm before that restoration is trusted:\n\n> If option 2: a bench arm showing the delegation restoration does not regress solve\n> rate or cost.\n\nThe code change is on branch `claude/bare-loop-delegation-loss-cxiouy`. **The arm was\nnot run** — that session's container had no provider API key (Stella is BYOK), so\nTerminal-Bench could not be started at all. This issue is that missing measurement.\n\n## What changed, and what it could plausibly do\n\n`bare_loop_config` in `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/goal.rs` used to narrow the bare\nloop's policy with `(\"task\", false)` — a **group** key covering the six `task_*` board\ntools *and* the delegation tool named `task`. It now names the six board tools\nindividually, so `task` is advertised to the bare loop again.\n\nThe risk that needs measuring is not correctness (the policy behaviour is unit-tested)\nbut economics and solve rate:\n\n- **Cost.** Delegation spends money. `subagent::session_pool_limit_usd` installs a $2\n  pool ceiling in `Observed` mode — it *warns* and children keep running, so the\n  enforcing bound is the parent's `--budget` guard. A bare loop that reaches for `task`\n  where it previously could not may cost materially more per solve.\n- **Latency.** The bare loop is the \"speed beats ceremony\" door and Terminal-Bench runs\n  under a 900s ceiling. A child that burns wall clock inside a parent step could push\n  trials into timeout, which surfaces as a solve-rate loss with a completely different\n  cause.\n- **Solve rate.** Could move either way. Fan-out may help on the multi-part tasks; it\n  may also distract a loop that would otherwise have run bash.\n\n## What to run\n\nTerminal-Bench 2.1, same worker config on both arms, differing only in this commit:\n\n- **Control:** `main` (or the branch's merge base).\n- **Treatment:** `claude/bare-loop-delegation-loss-cxiouy`.\n\nConstraints that come from `CLAUDE.md` and are easy to trip:\n\n- **Repeats per task.** A five-task solve rate cannot resolve anything smaller than a\n  catastrophe. Treat solve rate as a guardrail and read the mechanism metrics.\n- **Two runs differing by more than one commit are confounded** and must be reported as\n  such. Branch the treatment from the control commit rather than from a newer `main`.\n- **Conclusions come from `stella-events.jsonl`, not from `result.json` or the UI.**\n  Census `(role, model)` from `step_usage`; join `tool_start` → `tool_result` for real\n  tool wall clock; read full `proof` reason strings.\n- Name and exclude operational aborts explicitly rather than letting them score.\n\n## The mechanism metrics that actually answer the question\n\nSolve rate is the guardrail; these are the measurement:\n\n- **Did the bare loop use it at all?** Count `task` dispatches per trial in the events\n  log. If the count is ~0, the arms are the same run and the comparison says nothing\n  about delegation — report that rather than reporting a null result as reassurance.\n- **Sub-agent spend per trial** (the pool ledger the engine drains at each step\n  boundary), and how often the $2 `Observed` ceiling warned.\n- **Wall clock per trial**, and the count of trials that hit the 900s ceiling on each\n  arm.\n- **Steps and output tokens per solve** — the same pair #2410 was trying to move.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- Both arms run with repeats, on commits differing only by this change.\n- A comparison posted to #2580 (or to the PR) reporting solve rate, sub-agent spend,\n  wall clock, timeout count, and `task` dispatch count per arm — with aborts named and\n  excluded, and any confound stated.\n- If the arm shows a regression: say so and revert the narrowing to the group key, with\n  the doc comment's `# Blast radius` section updated to record that the measurement, not\n  the argument, is what settled it. That outcome is #2580's option 1 arrived at\n  honestly, and it is a perfectly good result.\n- If it shows neutral-or-better: the PR merges and this closes.\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/goal.rs` — `WITHHELD_BOARD_TOOLS`, `bare_loop_config`,\n  `mod bare_loop_board_tests`\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/subagent.rs` — `install_for_session`, `session_pool_limit_usd`,\n  `DEFAULT_POOL_LIMIT_USD`\n- `bench/` — `RUNBOOK.md`, `terminal-bench-2.1-protocol.md`, `tb21_preregistration.py`\n\nRefs #2580, #2410."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2632[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench: measure the bare loop with sub-agent delegation restored (#2580's unrun arm)"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
