    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem (unconfirmed — investigation first)\n\nIn the rendered transcript for trial `7d025330abad`, every assistant message appears **twice**: once as a standalone row and once attached to the following `STEP` record (88.0s then 89.7s, and again at 227.2s, 314.1s, 341.2s). Separately, the header reports `steps: 55` while the step counter visibly resets to `step 0` at least seven times (each plan step is dispatched as its own turn) and the research stage runs two concurrently-numbered lanes.\n\nNet effect: the headline `steps` figure cannot be mapped onto 55 distinct, ordered model calls — the \"read the trace, not the projection\" hazard, in the projection layer itself.\n\n## What has been ruled out\n\n`arenabench/arenabench/transcript.py` already has the dedup, and it looks correct:\n\n- the `text` handler (~line 305) reuses the fragment run's `seq` via `state.open_entries.get(\"text\") or state.pending_text`, with a comment noting that appending \"rendered every response twice\";\n- `pending_text` deliberately outlives `open_entries` for exactly this case;\n- `TranscriptState` is per-path (`self._states.setdefault(path, ...)`), so concurrent lanes do not share a cursor;\n- `arenabench/ui/components/arena/transcript-page.tsx:91` collapses by seq (`bySeq.set(entry.seq, entry)`).\n\nSo a duplicate implies the `text` event allocated a **fresh** seq, i.e. `pending_text` was `None` when the consolidated event arrived. Not yet reproduced.\n\n## Repro\n\nRead the trial's `stella-events.jsonl`, count `text_delta` vs `text` events around a step boundary, feed it through `TranscriptReader.read`, and assert one entry per assistant message. No archived `stella-events.jsonl` was available on the investigating machine, which is why this is filed as unconfirmed rather than as a bug.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/transcript.py` (~lines 261-330)\n- `arenabench/ui/components/arena/transcript-page.tsx` (~line 91)\n\n## Done when\n\nEither a test proves one rendered entry per assistant message across a step boundary, or the duplication is confirmed to be faithful rendering and the header's `steps` is redefined to something a reader can interpret (distinct model calls), with the two lanes and the per-plan-step counter reset made legible.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2544[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: assistant text may render twice in the trial transcript, and steps does not map to distinct model calls"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
