    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nA Claude Code seat routed through `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` to a non-Anthropic gateway (GLM via OpenRouter, z.ai, anything Anthropic-shaped) streams **zeroed** usage counters on every assistant message:\n\n```\n$ python3 - <<'PY'   # against a real archived trial\nassistant msgs with usage: 87, of which any nonzero: 0\n   {\"input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 0}\nPY\n```\n\nThe same trial on the **Anthropic** route carries real figures:\n\n```\nassistant msgs with usage: 48, of which any nonzero: 48\n   {\"input_tokens\": 2, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 18948, \"output_tokens\": 6, ...}\n```\n\nRepro: `~/.arenabench/matches/c53a132565cd/jobs/c53a132565cd-claude-code/make-mips-interpreter__t9JJ7Fm/agent/claude-code.txt` (zeroed) versus `~/.arenabench/matches/b952369cafd8/jobs/b952369cafd8-claude-code-opus-5-xhigh/sqlite-with-gcov__AVGWreg/agent/claude-code.txt` (real).\n\n## Consequence\n\n`arenabench/arenabench/harness.py` gave that arm live steps, tools, tool wall clock, cost and reasoning tokens, but its **token counts still only arrive at teardown**, from the ATIF trajectory Harbor writes in `populate_context_post_run`. So for gateway-routed seats — which is most GLM head-to-heads — the live token and cache columns are the one thing still dark mid-match.\n\n`telemetry.MetricsReader.read` handles this correctly today (`totals.prompt_tokens or metrics.tokens_in` keeps the ATIF value when the stream reports zero) and `_cmd_harness` discloses it rather than printing `0 tokens` beside a nonzero cost. Neither is wrong; both are working around a gap.\n\n## Where the numbers actually are, live\n\nClaude Code's own session transcript, under `agent/sessions/projects/-app/<session>/*.jsonl` in the trial directory (`CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` is set to `/logs/agent/sessions` by Harbor's `ClaudeCode.run`). It is appended as the agent works — `telemetry.LIVENESS_NAMES` already probes `agent/sessions` for exactly that reason — and Harbor's own ATIF converter reads `message.usage` out of it.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- `StreamReader` (or a sibling) also drains the session transcript when the stdout stream's usage is zeroed, so a gateway-routed arm's tokens are live.\n- The **same message-id delta-crediting** as the stdout reader: Harbor's converter notes that \"Claude-Code accumulates usage, so the real usage is the last message in the chain\", and the transcript has the same shape. A naive sum over the transcript will over-count exactly as it did over the stdout stream (measured there: 1.76x on output tokens, 2.4x on steps).\n- Must stay incremental: the transcript is the same order of magnitude as the stdout stream.\n- Witness test: a synthetic trial with a zeroed stdout stream and a populated transcript reports the transcript's tokens **before** any `trajectory.json` exists. It fails today.\n- The two sources must not double-credit when both carry usage. Prefer the stdout stream where it is nonzero; the transcript is the fallback, not an addend.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/harness.py`\n- `arenabench/arenabench/telemetry.py` — `LIVENESS_NAMES`, `MetricsReader.read`\n- `arenabench/tests/test_harness.py`\n- Reference: `/opt/homebrew/lib/python3.14/site-packages/harbor/agents/installed/claude_code.py` — `_get_session_dir`, `_convert_events_to_trajectory`, `_build_metrics`\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Standard library only.\n- Do not add hooks for this. The stdout stream and the transcript are both already written; a hook would put a process spawn on the critical path of the arm whose numbers are the bar (see the \"Why not hooks\" section in `harness.py`).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2520[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: a gateway-routed Claude Code seat streams zeroed usage, so its tokens are still dark until teardown"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench harness <match>` (added alongside `arenabench/arenabench/harness.py`) reports the tool mix, per-tool wall clock, tool error rate and reasoning spend for a **Claude Code** arm, because that arm publishes `agent/claude-code.txt` — Harbor's tee of the CLI's `--output-format=stream-json`.\n\nA Stella arm publishes `agent/stella-events.jsonl` instead, which is richer but spelled differently, so the command prints nothing for it:\n\n```\n$ arenabench harness <a stella-only match>\nno arm published a harness stream.\n```\n\nThe result is that the one command whose whole purpose is \"compare the two harnesses\" can currently only describe one of them. An operator asking \"did we win at 5/8 by doing the same thing they did, or something different?\" gets half an answer.\n\n## What is missing\n\n`arenabench.harness.HarnessTotals` is the shared vocabulary — `tool_calls`, `tool_ms`, `tool_errors`, `steps`, `tools`, token counters, `thinking_tokens`. Everything in it is derivable from Stella's own stream:\n\n| `HarnessTotals` field | Stella event source |\n|---|---|\n| `tool_calls`, `tools` | `tool_start` (`name`) |\n| `tool_ms` | join `tool_start` → `tool_result` (**do not** add a duration to `ToolOutput` — the loop detector keys on tool output and a timing there makes every call look distinct; use the existing timestamps) |\n| `tool_errors` | `tool_result` error flag |\n| `steps`, token counters | `step_usage` (already folded by `telemetry._reduce_events`) |\n| `models` | `step_usage.model` |\n\n`HarnessProfile` has no clean Stella analogue for `version` (the SUT commit already identifies it, in `provenance.sut_seats`) — the profile fields that do map are the tool roster and the effective posture.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A reducer that folds `agent/stella-events.jsonl` into `HarnessTotals`, living beside the existing one so the two share the dataclass rather than two parallel shapes.\n- `arenabench harness <match>` prints one block per arm, Stella included, in the same layout — so the two are read side by side rather than in two commands.\n- A witness test: a synthetic match with one Stella job and one Claude Code job produces two blocks with comparable `tool_calls`/`tool_ms`.\n- The report must state where the two vocabularies genuinely differ rather than forcing a false equivalence. Stella's `steps` counts pipeline-role calls (worker, verifier, triage — see `call_seq` in the glossary) while Claude Code's counts model turns in one loop; a table that puts those in one column is the sort of \"plausible number\" this repo treats as worse than a crash.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/harness.py` — `HarnessTotals`, `HarnessProfile`, `StreamReader`\n- `arenabench/arenabench/telemetry.py` — `_reduce_events` already folds the Stella stream for the scoreboard\n- `arenabench/arenabench/cli.py` — `_cmd_harness`\n- `arenabench/tests/test_harness.py` — fixtures for both stream shapes\n\n## Constraints\n\n- ArenaBench is standard-library only by contract (`arenabench/pyproject.toml` says so and explains why). No new dependencies.\n- The reducer must stay incremental — `StreamReader` holds a byte cursor because one archived stream is 15 MB and a live dashboard polls it. A Stella-side reducer that re-reads the whole file per poll would reintroduce exactly the cost the cursor removed.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2519[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench harness: the Stella arm has no behavioural block, so the comparison is one-sided"[m
