    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`verify_done` now reports its per-phase wall clock as a `stella-diag` record\n(`tools.verify_done.phases`, #2486). In a local run with `--log-file` those\nrecords are collected and can be censused. **In an arena trial they are\nnot**, because the harbor adapter never asks for a log file — so the\npopulation that produced #2486's numbers (61 matches) is exactly the\npopulation where the answer cannot be read back.\n\nThe consequence is narrow but real: #2486's instrument answers \"which phase\"\non a developer's machine, and the follow-up optimisation's before/after has\nto be run locally rather than over a real trial distribution. Anything that\nwants a p90 across a match is still stuck with subtraction.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/__init__.py` builds the agent argv\n  around line 1314: `--model`, optional `--budget` / `--turn-budget` /\n  `--base-url`, then `--output-format stream-json -- <instruction>`. No\n  `--log-file`, and no `STELLA_LOG` in the environment it exports.\n- `bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/__init__.py` line 158 sets\n  `_STREAM_EVENTS_PATH = \"/logs/agent/stella-events.jsonl\"`, and\n  `arenabench/arenabench/telemetry.py` reads that file back as\n  `agent/stella-events.jsonl` — so `/logs/` is the trial's collected\n  directory and a sibling file written there should be collected the same\n  way. **Verify this rather than assuming it**; it is the load-bearing\n  premise of the fix below.\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/diag_boot.rs`: with no `--log-file`, the only sinks\n  are stderr at `warn` and the crash ring, which reaches disk only on a\n  panic or a non-zero exit. A phase record is `info`, so it goes nowhere.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Add `--log-file /logs/agent/stella-diag.jsonl` to the adapter's stella\n   argv. It is a global arg (`GlobalArgs` in `crates/stella-cli/src/cli.rs`),\n   and `diag_boot::install` floors a log file at `info`, so no `--log-level`\n   is needed and stderr stays quiet at `warn`.\n2. Confirm the file is collected into the match archive beside\n   `agent/stella-events.jsonl`.\n3. Teach `arenabench/arenabench/telemetry.py` about the new artifact only if\n   something is going to read it there. A census script that opens the file\n   directly is sufficient for the immediate need and adds no coupling.\n\n## Constraints a fresh agent will hit\n\n- The adapter registers a canonical claim command and hashes its own\n  executable sources (`_hash_sources` in the same package); changing the argv\n  may require updating a registration constant, and\n  `bench/harbor_adapter/tests/test_adapter.py` and\n  `tests/test_secure_launcher.py` both assert on the launch shape. Expect to\n  update those in the same change.\n- `bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/secure_launcher.py` refuses anything\n  that is not a direct stella argv and rejects credential-shaped values in\n  the exec argv; a literal path flag is neither, but read\n  `_secure_exec_with_credential_fd` before editing.\n- Several files in `bench/harbor_adapter/` are over their file-size ceilings\n  in the base tree already. That drift is not caused by this change and must\n  not be \"fixed\" by folding a baseline regeneration into it (AGENTS.md\n  § \"God files\" — the ratchet judges your change, not the tree).\n- The diagnostic plane is content-free by construction (invariant 3,\n  `crates/stella-diag/src/field.rs` §5.2), so this adds no new egress or\n  privacy question: a record cannot carry a path, a prompt, or model output.\n  Worth stating in the PR, because \"the agent now writes a second log file\n  in the trial container\" reads like it might.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nAn arena trial leaves `agent/stella-diag.jsonl` in its match directory\ncontaining `tools.verify_done.phases` records, and a one-liner over a\ncompleted match reports median and p90 of `machinery`, `worktree_add` and\n`cleanup` — the same census #2486's issue text had to approximate by\nsubtracting a proxy.\n\n## Related\n\n- #2486 — the instrument this makes collectable\n- #2424 — the estimate that motivated it\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2506[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench: the harbor adapter asks for no log file, so verify_done's phase records never reach a match archive"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
