    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nStella's task-board tools (`task_create`, `task_start`, `task_complete`, plus `project_overview`) are\ncharged at the most expensive possible rate: a **separate model round trip per card**. Measured against\nthe ground-truth journals of match `5292a68cdabf`, they consumed **12–16% of the session budget on the\nthree trials that lost**, and on one of them the *final purchased step of the entire run* was a card\nupdate rather than the one-line command that would have won the task.\n\nThese calls read no workspace state and change no file. Claude Code, on the same tasks, issues zero of\nthem.\n\n## Evidence\n\nPer-trial attribution from `agent/stella-events.jsonl`, summing `step_usage.cost_usd` and classifying a\nstep as ledger-only when every `tool_start` in it names a task-board tool:\n\n| trial | reward | total spend | ledger-only spend | share | tool calls | ledger calls |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `git-multibranch__S4PjQ6Q` | 0 | $1.0090 | $0.1412 | 14.0% | 42 | 14 |\n| `git-multibranch__wWarrQF` | 0 | $1.0775 | $0.1310 | 12.2% | 36 | 10 |\n| `sqlite-with-gcov__iDi8mCw` | 0 | $1.0010 | $0.1603 | 16.0% | 45 | 13 |\n| `sqlite-with-gcov__5ruCbkc` | 1 | $1.0008 | $0.1585 | 15.8% | 43 | 14 |\n| `regex-log__zX9x6Wm` | 1 | $1.0121 | $0.2669 | 26.4% | 11 | 4 |\n| `large-scale-text-editing__72WaM2D` | 1 | $0.9659 | $0.2035 | 21.1% | 24 | 9 |\n\nTwo specific shapes, both visible in `git-multibranch__S4PjQ6Q`'s step table:\n\n1. **Unbatched creation.** Step 5 issued **six** `task_create` calls in one step for $0.0650 and 2026\n   output tokens — 6.5% of the whole budget spent writing a to-do list.\n2. **Ledger-only steps.** Steps 6, 10, 17 and 24 contain nothing but `task_complete` / `task_start`\n   pairs, costing $0.0161 + $0.0208 + $0.0178 + $0.0215 = $0.0762. Each is a full request/response\n   round trip that moves a card, touches no file, and returns no information to the agent.\n\nThe median working step in that run cost ~$0.025, so **$0.14 of ledger ≈ 5 working steps of runway**.\nEach of the three losses was 1–4 steps from done. On `sqlite-with-gcov__iDi8mCw` the sequence is exact:\n\n```\nstep 31  bash    → gcov decodes real counters, \"Lines executed:15.87% of 58950\"   ✓\nstep 32  task_start {\"id\":\"4\"}  → \"Put the instrumented sqlite3 on PATH persistently\"\n         => error: \"not executed — turn aborted on budget\"\n```\n\nThe grader then failed all three of that task's tests on `sqlite3 not found in PATH`.\n\nNote also the variance: ledger share ranges 0% → 26% across trials of the same build, so board usage is\nmodel-discretionary and unpredictable — it cannot be budgeted for.\n\n## Why this is a defect and not a design tradeoff\n\nThe task board is genuinely valuable for long autonomous runs: it is what makes them legible and\nresumable. The defect is the *pricing*, not the feature. Nothing about updating a local card requires a\ndedicated inference call, yet the current shape buys one per transition.\n\n## Files\n\n- Task-board tools and registration: `crates/stella-tools/src/registry.rs` (note: a god file, closed to\n  growth — new logic goes in a sibling submodule)\n- Task board decision logic and the `TaskUpdate` event: `crates/stella-core`,\n  `crates/stella-protocol/src/event.rs`\n- Store mirror of the board: `stella-store` `tasks` table (see AGENTS.md glossary, \"task\")\n- Evidence journals: `~/.arenabench/matches/5292a68cdabf/jobs/5292a68cdabf-stella-opus-5-xhigh-bare-step-loop/<trial>/agent/stella-events.jsonl` on the EC2 rig\n\n## Candidate fixes, cheapest first\n\n1. **Let ledger calls ride along instead of occupying a step.** If a card transition is executed in the\n   same step as real work rather than alone, the ~25 ledger-only steps measured across the solved trials\n   disappear with no behaviour change. Highest value per unit of risk.\n2. **Batch the board.** Accept a list: four `task_create` calls become one call with four items. Removes\n   roughly 15 calls per solved trial on the observed traces.\n3. **Withhold the board when it cannot pay for itself.** A single-turn one-shot under a hard deadline has\n   nothing to resume. The bare step loop could withhold the task tools the way `tools.bash: \"off\"`\n   already withholds the shell (`.stella/settings.json` tool switches).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A witness test that fails on `main` and passes with the change, proving a card transition no longer\n  requires its own model round trip (option 1) and/or that N cards are creatable in one call (option 2).\n- Re-attribution on a fresh match shows ledger-only spend materially below the 12–16% measured here.\n- No regression in board fidelity: the `tasks` rows mirrored from `TaskUpdate` must be unchanged for an\n  equivalent run.\n\nRefs the arenabench budget-parity issue filed alongside this one: under the $1.00 cap Stella was given in\nthat match, this overhead converted directly into losses.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2412[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"stella-tools: the task board costs a full model round trip per card — 12-16% of the session budget on the trials that lost, and the last step one loss ever bought was a task_start"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
