    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`stella ingest <doc>` extracts records from at most the first 24,000 characters\nof a document. Everything past that is dropped before the model ever sees it:\n\n```rust\n// crates/stella-cli/src/ingest_cmd/extract.rs\nconst MAX_PROMPT_CHARS: usize = 24_000;\n```\n\nThis repository's own `AGENTS.md` is **44,545 characters**, so a\n`stella ingest AGENTS.md` extracts **54% of it** and skips 20,545 characters.\nThe extractor's last line is the middle of the workspace-layout table:\n\n```\n| Triage → … → verifier orchestrat\n```\n\nEverything below that point — the god-file rules, the glossary, the code-style\nconventions, the testing approach, and the whole gotchas section — cannot\nproduce a record, and could not have. The run still reports success: on the run\nthat motivated this issue it wrote 93 proposals to `.stella/proposals/agents.toml`\nand said nothing about the missing half.\n\nThe steering documents this feature exists to ingest are exactly the documents\nthat exceed the cap. `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are named directly by the\nfirst-run dialog (`ingest_cmd.rs::run_scan`, tier `Primary`), so the headline\nuse case is the one that silently loses content.\n\n## What already landed\n\nPR (branch `fix/ingest-silent-during-model-call`) makes the loss **visible** —\n`bounded_content` returns the dropped character count and `run_named` prints:\n\n```\n    heads up: only the first 24000 of 44545 characters are extracted — 20545 (46%) are skipped, so nothing below that point can become a record\n```\n\nThat is a warning, not a fix. A person who ingests AGENTS.md still cannot get\nrecords out of the second half without splitting the file by hand.\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/ingest_cmd/extract.rs` — `MAX_PROMPT_CHARS`,\n  `bounded_content`, `call_model`, `extract_document`\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/ingest_cmd.rs` — `run_named`, `truncation_notice`\n\n## Proposed shape\n\nChunk the document and merge the claims, rather than raising the cap. Raising it\ntrades one silent failure for another: `call_model` already starts at a 16,384\noutput-token budget and a 9,401-token input filled it exactly\n(`\"finish_reason\":\"length\"`, execution 89 in `.stella/private/store.db`), so a\nlarger input makes the cut-off retry the normal path instead of the exception.\n\nConstraints a design has to respect:\n\n- **Split on structure, not on a character offset.** Cutting mid-table produced\n  the truncation above; markdown headings are the natural seam, and a chunk that\n  begins mid-section gives the extractor no context for what it is reading.\n- **`lineage_suffix` is only unique within one model reply.** The system prompt\n  asks for a slug \"unique within the document\"; two chunks extracted by two\n  calls can collide, and `build_proposal` turns the suffix into\n  `ctx.<set_id>.<suffix>`. Deduplicate on merge, or scope the suffix per chunk.\n- **Cost and wall clock are per chunk.** One AGENTS.md call already costs ~$0.47\n  and 135s; four chunks is four of those. The progress ticker must say which\n  chunk is running (`Progress::start` takes the label, so this is a label\n  change), and the run summary must fold the per-chunk costs.\n- **`source_digest` is the whole document** (`build_defaults`), which stays\n  correct across chunks; `source_lines` is per claim and must stay in\n  whole-document coordinates, not chunk-relative ones.\n- Keep the deterministic half unchanged: chunking is an extraction concern, and\n  `stella_core::ingest::gate` must still see every claim.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- Ingesting a document larger than one prompt's worth produces records drawn\n  from all of it, with no hand-splitting.\n- A witness test that fails on `main`: a fixture document whose *last* section\n  contains a distinctive claim, asserted to appear in the proposals.\n- The truncation notice either disappears or changes to state what was chunked.\n- The run summary reports total cost across every call the document needed.\n\nRefs #2374\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2407[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"ingest: extraction reads only the first 24,000 characters, so AGENTS.md is ingested at 54% and reports success"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
