    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`stella-cli/src/domains.rs::infer_domains` carries the exact defect PR #1096\nfixed in its sibling, and has carried it since: a hardcoded output cap with no\ncut-off detection.\n\n```rust\n// crates/stella-cli/src/domains.rs:195\nmax_output_tokens: Some(2048),\n```\n\nThere is no `finish_reason` check anywhere in the file (`rg -n \"finish_reason\"\ncrates/stella-cli/src/domains.rs` returns only a struct-literal `None` in a test\nfixture at line 338). When the reply fills the budget, the JSON is cut off\nmid-object and the parse failure is reported as a generic serde error rather\nthan as \"the budget was too small\" — and the bounded repair re-asks the same\nquestion at `temperature: 0.0`, which tends to truncate at the same point.\n\n`extract.rs`'s own module doc says it \"mirrors `infer_domains`\", so this is the\nsame bug in the function the fixed one was copied from. PR #1096 named it as a\nfast-follow in its description and it was never filed, so it has been invisible\nsince 2026-08-01.\n\nIt is **more** likely to bite than the one that was fixed: 2048 is one eighth of\nthe 16384 `extract.rs` now uses, and reasoning models spend part of that budget\nbefore emitting a token of JSON (a real `ingest_extraction` call on Opus 5 spent\n1,093 reasoning tokens — over half of this entire budget — see execution 89 in\nthis repo's `.stella/private/store.db`).\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/domains.rs` — `infer_domains`, the cap at line 195\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/ingest_cmd/extract.rs` — `call_model`, the fixed shape\n  to copy: `BASE_OUTPUT_TOKENS`, the `FinishReason::Length` check, and the\n  budget-doubling retry arm\n\n## Verify\n\n`stella init` in a workspace with many source directories drives\n`infer_domains`. A witness test does not need a provider: the mock-provider\npattern already used in `crates/stella-cli/src/accounted_call.rs`'s tests can\nreturn a `CompletionResult` with `finish_reason: Some(FinishReason::Length)` and\na truncated body, and assert the retry widens the budget rather than re-sending\nthe same request.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- `infer_domains` reads `finish_reason` and doubles its budget on\n  `FinishReason::Length`, exactly as `extract.rs::call_model` does.\n- The base cap is raised from 2048 to a figure that survives a reasoning model;\n  16384 matches `EngineConfig` and `extract.rs`.\n- A cut-off that survives every attempt reports itself as a cut-off, not as a\n  serde syntax error.\n- A witness test that fails on `main` covers the widening retry.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Under the #2374 feature freeze this is hardening an existing feature, which\n  the directive keeps in scope.\n- Whatever the two functions end up sharing, they must not drift again — either\n  extract the shared retry-on-length loop into one helper both call, or add a\n  test that fails when one has a `finish_reason` check and the other does not.\n\nRefs #1096\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2406[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"ingest: infer_domains has the identical unfixed truncation bug PR #1096 fixed in extract.rs (2048-token cap, no finish_reason check)"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
