    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench cloud run` now prints the resolved SUT identity at submit time\n(`sut       : main -> 4f718d9a…`, #2388) and `submit_run` persists it to\n`s3://<bucket>/runs/<run-id>/jobs.json`:\n\n```python\n\"sut\": None if sut is None else {\n    \"ref\": sut.ref, \"commit\": sut.commit, \"uri\": sut.uri,\n},\n```\n\nBut that identity never reaches the place people actually read a run from. The\nlive scoreboard (`arenabench cloud watch <run-id>`,\n`arenabench/arenabench/cloud_watch.py`) contains no reference to the SUT at\nall — `rg -n \"sut|commit\" arenabench/arenabench/cloud_watch.py` returns\nnothing. Neither does `arenabench cloud status <run-id>`, which loads the very\nrecord that holds it (`executor.load_jobs(args.run_id)` in `_cmd_cloud_status`)\nand prints only the run id, the trial count and the queue.\n\nSo the answer to \"which commit is this scoreboard measuring?\" lives only in the\nscrollback of whoever submitted, on the machine they submitted from. Anyone\nopening the watch page later, or running `cloud status` from another machine —\nwhich is a headline feature of that verb — cannot tell. That is the same gap\n#2388 closed at submit time, left open at read time, and it matters for exactly\nthe same reason: a number nobody can attribute to a tree is not a measurement.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/cloud_watch.py` — `CloudScoreboard.fetch`, `render_html`\n- `arenabench/arenabench/cloud.py` — `_cmd_cloud_status` (the one-line header\n  print), `submit_run` (writes the `sut` block into `jobs.json`),\n  `load_jobs` (reads it back)\n- `arenabench/tests/test_cloud_watch.py`, `arenabench/tests/test_cloud.py` —\n  the recorded-call fakes to extend\n\n## Verify\n\nNo AWS needed; both suites run against fake clients.\n\n1. `jobs.json` already carries `{\"sut\": {\"ref\", \"commit\", \"uri\"}}` — see\n   `TestSubmitContract` in `tests/test_cloud.py` for how the record is built.\n2. Feed a scoreboard a `jobs.json` containing that block and assert the\n   rendered HTML names the ref and the commit.\n3. Assert `_cmd_cloud_status` prints `ref -> commit` on its header line, the\n   same shape `_cmd_cloud_run` prints at submit time.\n\nA run submitted before this exists has no `sut` block (or a `null` one, for a\nmatch with no Stella seat) — that has to render as an explicit \"unknown\"\nrather than as a blank, since a missing identity and an unrecorded one are\ndifferent facts.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- `cloud watch`'s page shows the SUT ref and commit for the run, or says\n  plainly that the run recorded none.\n- `cloud status` prints the same `ref -> commit` line `cloud run` prints.\n- Both covered against the existing recorded-call fakes.\n- No new AWS calls: `jobs.json` is already fetched by both paths.\n\nRefs #2388, #2112\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2400[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench cloud: the resolved SUT commit never reaches `cloud watch` or `cloud status` — only the submitter's scrollback"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
