    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`doc:trace-replay-learning-harness` §6 asks the replay summary for \"**Artifacts built, by class** — memories, skills, rules, tools — and **turns-to-first-artifact for each**.\"\n\nAs shipped in #2350, `ReplaySummary` (`crates/stella-cli/src/memory/replay/summary.rs`) delivers that metric honestly for two of the four classes and not for the other two:\n\n| Class | `turns-to-first` |\n|---|---|\n| memories | **exact** — folded per turn from `ReflectionReport::recorded` |\n| tools | **exact** — folded per turn from the foundry's proposal count |\n| skills | **approximated** — set to the total turn count whenever any skill exists |\n| rules | **absent** — no field at all |\n\nThe skill approximation is currently commented in place:\n\n```rust\nif !self.skills.is_empty() && self.first_skill_turn.is_none() {\n    // Skills are only observable on disk, so the best we can honestly\n    // say is \"by the end\". A per-turn probe would cost a directory walk\n    // per turn to sharpen a number nothing asserts on.\n    self.first_skill_turn = Some(self.turns);\n}\n```\n\nThat reasoning was right for #2350 — nothing asserted on it, and a directory walk per turn is real cost for a number nobody read. It is wrong to leave standing, because the printed report says `turns-to-first: memory 1, skill 10, tool 3` and **`skill 10` reads as a measurement when it is a placeholder**. A reader comparing two corpora would draw a conclusion from a field that only ever reports \"the last turn\".\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe whole design premise of §6 is that the metric block is trustworthy enough to publish beside a claim, and §11's honesty guard (\"the corpus proves the corpus\") is about exactly this failure mode. A placeholder rendered in the same table as two measured values is the kind of number that gets quoted.\n\nLatency-to-first-artifact is also the interesting cross-corpus quantity: it is how you would compare \"does a denser corpus teach faster\" between two fixtures, which is the natural next question after #2305.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Probe the workspace skills dir and the rules dir **per turn** in `Replayer::turn`, and fold the first non-empty observation into `first_skill_turn` / a new `first_rule_turn`.\n   - Both are small directory reads (`crate::memory::skill_paths_on_disk`, `summary::published_rules`) against a temp workspace of a handful of files. Measure before optimizing; if the corpus grows enough for it to matter, cache the directory mtime instead of walking.\n2. Render `rules` in the `turns-to-first` line beside the other three.\n3. Either drop the \"by the end\" fallback entirely, or — if a class genuinely cannot be measured — render it as `—` rather than as a number. **A placeholder must never be formatted like a measurement.**\n\n## Verify\n\n```sh\nmake replay-learning\n```\n\nThe `turns-to-first` line should name four classes, and the skill and rule figures should be **less than** the total turn count for `crates/stella-cli/tests/fixtures/traces/simulated-months.json` (the registry convention's fourth re-encounter lands on turn 8 of 10, so both should read 8, not 10).\n\nAdd an assertion in `crates/stella-cli/src/memory/replay/tests.rs` pinning that — it fails today, since `first_skill_turn` is 10.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- `first_skill_turn` and a new `first_rule_turn` are measured per turn, not approximated.\n- The rendered `turns-to-first` line covers all four classes.\n- A test asserts the skill figure is strictly less than the total turn count on the committed corpus (i.e. it is a measurement, not the fallback).\n- No class renders a placeholder as a number.\n- `make gate` green.\n\n## Related\n\n- #2304 — the epic; §6 is the metrics phase.\n- #2350 — where the approximation shipped, with this reasoning recorded in the code comment above.\n- #2305 — the paid with-records bench arm, which measures *outcome*; this measures *formation* and is the number a formation-vs-formation comparison would use.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2359[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"cli(replay): turns-to-first-artifact is a placeholder for skills and absent for rules, but renders like a measurement"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
