    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`scripts/arena-run.sh` picks \"the first free port at or above 8900\" with a scan range of 40 ports (`range(start, start + 40)` in its launch block), but `serve`'s reuse discovery (`ARENA_DISCOVERY_PORTS` in `arenabench/arenabench/server.py`) deliberately stops at 8905. An arena that legitimately lands on 8906–8939 — which happens exactly when the low ports are busy, i.e. on the multi-tenant box the script was written for — is invisible to every later `serve`'s reuse sweep. The next launch then starts a second arena over the same workspace, which is the precise hazard #2322 exists to prevent: \"two arenas over one workspace can both drive a run.\"\n\nThis does not cause misreports anymore (#2351 made crash-vs-handoff classification read the child's log), it causes silent *non-reuse*.\n\nFor the gap to bite, ports 8900–8905 must all be held by processes that are not arenas serving this workspace (other services, or arenas over `ARENABENCH_HOME` overrides), with the this-workspace arena sitting at 8906+. Low-moderate likelihood, but the failure it produces is the one #2322 calls a real hazard, and `server.py`'s own comment records arenas historically landing on 8917 and 8933.\n\n## Constraint\n\n`ARENA_DISCOVERY_PORTS` is bounded and deterministic **on purpose** — \"discovery must cost a handful of loopback connects, never a port scan\" (comment above the constant). The fix is not \"sweep 40 ports in serve.\" Candidate shapes, maintainer's pick:\n\n- Cap `arena-run.sh`'s free-port scan at the same bound serve discovers (8900–8905, then fail loudly with \"clear the box with make kill-arena\"), so every arena the script can create is one serve can find. Simplest; makes the two ranges one fact.\n- Or have serve record its port in a workspace-local file (e.g. `$ARENABENCH_HOME/arena-port`) and check that single address before the bounded sweep — one loopback connect, no scan, finds an arena on any port.\n\n## Verify\n\nHermetic, in `scripts/test-arena-scripts.sh` style: assert the script's scan bound equals `ARENA_DISCOVERY_PORTS`' span (parity check across the two files, same spirit as the handoff-marker wire contract), or for the port-file shape, a stub test that discovery consults the file first.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nA `make run-arena` can never create an arena that a subsequent `serve --reuse` (the default) cannot discover, and a test pins whichever mechanism guarantees it.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2352[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: run-arena can place an arena beyond serve's reuse discovery, recreating the two-arenas-one-store hazard (#2322)"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
