    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nPR #2322 landed. Its arena-reuse discovery is sound in the part that matters most (`/api/health` is a genuine handshake: `ok` truthy **and** a workspace resolving to exactly this one). Three defects landed with it; the first is a measurement-honesty problem in the tool used to judge bench results.\n\n### 1. A live match swept in from disk is reported as `finished`\n\n`_refresh_from_disk` → `runner.restore_from_disk()` → `_restore_one` (`arenabench/arenabench/runner.py:559`) **unconditionally** sets `match.status = \"finished\"`, a note reading \"restored from artifacts on disk after a server restart\", and `finished_at` from a file mtime. `restore_from_disk` skips ids already in `self.matches` (`runner.py:543`, `setdefault` at `:553`), so it never corrects itself, and status is memory-only — never persisted (`runner.py:230/595/639/1069/1072/1076`).\n\nReproduced:\n\n```\nrestored: 1\nstatus  : finished\nnote    : restored from artifacts on disk after a server restart\nsnapshot status: finished | elapsed: 0.0\nsecond sweep restored: 0 -> status still finished\n```\n\nThis lands on #2322's own headline flow: `run` prints `watch: http://127.0.0.1:PORT/matches/<id>` for a match it *just started*; the operator opens it; the arena misses, force-sweeps, and renders the **live** match as **finished** with `elapsed: 0.0` and a note describing a restart that never happened. `list_matches` emits the same status. Meanwhile `metrics_for` (`runner.py:281`) re-reads job dirs every snapshot, so cells keep filling — **a partial scoreboard labeled final**, in the surface used to decide whether Stella beat Fable 5. Worse than the 404 it replaced: honest absence became a confident wrong answer.\n\n**Fix:** stop reusing the *restart* path for the *live-sweep* path. Persist match state (a `state.json` beside `spec.json`, written at the existing transitions) or derive liveness from the seat manifest (`runner.py:845`), and let a later sweep update a non-terminal match rather than pinning it. The existing witness asserts only membership and `isinstance(..., dict)`, so it passes with the wrong status — it must assert status.\n\n### 2. `probe_arena` does not catch `http.client.HTTPException`\n\n`BadStatusLine`, `InvalidURL` and `IncompleteRead` subclass neither `OSError` nor `ValueError`, so the except tuple misses exactly the \"a foreign service is listening\" case the docstring promises to collapse to `None`. Repro against a loopback socket returning non-HTTP bytes:\n\n```\nUNCAUGHT http.client.BadStatusLine:  P not http at all\n```\n\nBlast radius is the concern: in `arenabench run`, `find_running_arena` sits **after** `runner.start(match)`, and seats are `start_new_session=True` (`runner.py:867`) — an uncaught exception there kills the CLI **with the match already launched**, leaving a paid run with no supervisor, no monitor and no cancel.\n\n**Fix:** catch `Exception` (or add `http.client.HTTPException`), and add a direct test of `probe_arena`. All four tests added by #2322 monkeypatch it, so the predicate has zero coverage.\n\n### 3. The reuse banner records nothing identifying what was attached to\n\n`default_workspace()` (`server.py:951`) is `$ARENABENCH_HOME` or `~/.arenabench` — **one workspace for every checkout on the machine** — so matching on workspace path is near-tautological. `serve` from worktree A attaches to an arena launched from worktree B, running B's `ARENABENCH_STELLA_ADAPTER`, B's `STELLA_BINARY`, B's interpreter, and the arena is the *launcher* (`ArenaServer` owns the runner and `SutBuilder`). The banner prints URL and workspace — the two fields guaranteed to match — and nothing else. #2325 exists because a server was running on this rig with exactly the wrong interpreter.\n\n**Fix:** have `/api/health` report arena identity (pid, adapter root, `STELLA_BINARY`) and print it in the reuse banner.\n\n### 4. Smaller\n\n- **`--allow-remote` is silently a no-op**: the reuse probe runs after the allow-remote gate on `args.host`, and `is_loopback` (`server.py:111`) excludes `0.0.0.0`, so `--allow-remote --host 0.0.0.0` probes, can attach to a local arena, and returns without binding the requested interface. The code comment claiming outbound connections go to `127.0.0.1` only is false as written.\n- **The throttle bypasses itself**: `match()` sets `_last_disk_sweep = 0.0` on every miss, so any 404 forces a full sweep (56 match dirs on this rig). A tab polling a deleted id re-sweeps continuously.\n- `ARENA_DISCOVERY_PORTS = (8900..8905)` covers 3 of the 6 arenas in the evidence that justified it, and #2328's probe scans 8900..8939 — two different discovery windows for one question.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nA live match is never rendered `finished`; `probe_arena` returns `None` for any non-arena listener with a test that does not monkeypatch it; the reuse banner names the arena it attached to.\n\nRefs #2322, #2308, #2325, #2328.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2343[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: a live match swept in from disk renders as finished with elapsed 0.0 — a partial scoreboard labeled final (#2322)"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
