    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nA headless `stella run` in a workspace that is not trusted (`STELLA_TRUST_PROJECT` unset) silently withholds every piece of project steering: `.stella/memories/*.md`, the workspace rules section (published context records), project scripts, orientation, and the exploration index. Nothing on stdout, stderr, the stream-json event feed, or the diagnostics log says this happened.\n\nThe suppression itself is correct fail-closed security (a cloned repo's `.stella/` must not steer sessions until the user opts in). The defect is the silence: the user believes their memories and rules are active, and the only way to discover otherwise is to reconstruct the wire prompt with `stella inspect`.\n\nObserved on a release build of `main` at 7b2a0b44 (v0.7.25), 2026-08-08:\n\n- Run 1 (untrusted): seeded memories + tracked rules absent from the digest-verified system prompt (`stella inspect 1 --step 0 --full`); stderr contained only the code-graph lines.\n- Run 2 (`STELLA_TRUST_PROJECT=1`, same workspace/goal/model): memories and rules present and honored by the model.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/agent/prompt.rs` — `assemble_system_prompt` skips the four project appenders when `authority.project_prompts_allowed` is false; no notice is emitted on that branch.\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/settings/authority.rs` — `AuthorityPolicy::compute` (`project_prompts_allowed = project_trusted && …`).\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/settings/merge.rs:457-494` — the existing untrusted-repo notices; they cover project hooks, context sources, and credential redirects, but not withheld memories/rules/prompt steering.\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/settings.rs::project_trust` — the `STELLA_TRUST_PROJECT` gate.\n\n## Repro\n\n1. Create a fresh worktree/clone with `.stella/memories/00-marker.md` containing an instruction the answer must reflect, and any tracked `.stella/rules/*.toml`.\n2. `stella run --no-pipeline \"…\" ` without `STELLA_TRUST_PROJECT` — marker absent from the answer, no warning anywhere.\n3. `stella inspect <exec> --step 0 --full` — system prompt has no memories/rules sections.\n4. Re-run with `STELLA_TRUST_PROJECT=1` — sections present, marker honored.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The precedent is architecture invariant #8's posture notice: a pinned effort against an Unsupported provider surfaces a one-line boot notice, never a silent drop. This is the same shape: configuration the user wrote, dropped without a word.\n- The notice must not leak content (no memory/rule text), just the fact: counts withheld and the opt-in (`STELLA_TRUST_PROJECT=1`). It belongs on stderr and, for `--output-format stream-json`/`json`, in the event/summary stream so harnesses see it too.\n- Keep the interactive path unchanged if the deck already prompts for trust; this is about headless.\n- The notice must be byte-stable-safe: it goes to the session surfaces, never into the system prompt itself.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nA headless run in an untrusted workspace that has any of: memories, rules, project scripts, or exploration maps emits one clearly-worded notice naming what was withheld (counts, not content) and how to opt in — with a witness test proving the notice appears exactly on that branch (untrusted + steering present) and not when the workspace is trusted or has nothing to withhold.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2302[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"headless run in an untrusted workspace silently withholds memories/rules — no notice names the suppression or the opt-in"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
