    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\narenabench's `premature-complete` monitor rule fires when the agent declared complete after few steps AND the verifier resolved False. That predicate cannot distinguish \"the agent gave up early\" (a capability signal) from \"the agent was forcibly terminated by a terminal provider error mid-trial\" (an operational abort — e.g. an OpenRouter HTTP 402 when credit runs out, the failure mode that corrupted 13/20 trials in the first `opus5-h2h-20task` attempt on 2026-08-07). Both shapes look identical to the rule, so an aborted trial gets narrated as an agent defect.\n\nRelated but distinct: #2220 (zero-telemetry trials scored as losses — the scoring side of the same family). This issue is about the monitor/narration side.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/` — the monitor rules (search for `premature-complete`)\n- Reference traces: `~/.arenabench/matches/` — the 2026-08-07 h2h attempt's 402-corrupted trials\n\n## Done\n\nThe rule (or its consumer) checks the trial's late error / terminal event for provider-payment and auth-terminal signatures first, and labels those trials as operational aborts rather than premature completion. A unit test feeds both shapes and asserts the two distinct labels.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2281[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: the premature-complete monitor rule conflates a 402-terminated trial with an agent that gave up"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
