    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nMatch 958b92296de1 (`opus5-stella-only-20task`) was killed at ~78 minutes by a SIGTERM nobody claims. Harbor's `_handle_sigterm` (`harbor/cli/jobs.py:282`) raised KeyboardInterrupt mid-trial-8 (`cobol-modernization__D6RyKww` cancelled — its `exception.txt` holds the traceback), 12 of 20 tasks never started, and `result.json.finished_at` is null. The launcher log (`opus5-stella-only-20task-run.log`) shows no watchdog, no timeout, no balance-guard action — it simply stops at 78.1m. The operator states they did not kill it.\n\nCandidates: another session's cleanup sweeping process groups, macOS resource handling, a stray `kill` from a concurrent script on this shared box. Indistinguishable after the fact because nothing logs signal receipt or sender.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/` — runner signal handling / logging\n- Evidence: `~/.arenabench/matches/958b92296de1/` (`exception.txt`, match log tail), `~/.arenabench/opus5-stella-only-20task-run.log`\n\n## Done\n\nThe runner logs signal receipt (signal number, plus sender pid/uid where obtainable) and writes a one-line shutdown-cause record into the match directory, so the next mystery SIGTERM is attributable from the artifacts alone.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2280[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: match 958b92296de1 killed by an unattributable SIGTERM at ~78min — runner must log signal receipt and shutdown cause"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
