    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nPR #2269 fixed the \"Harbor is too old / missing\" wall on the **Python** side: `arenabench.harbor.resolve_for_dataset` now searches for a Harbor that clears a dataset's floor and installs one with `uv` if none does, keeping the refusal only as a last resort. The result is that `arenabench serve` / `arenabench run` no longer die in preflight on a machine that could satisfy the floor.\n\nThe **shell** lane still hits the same class of failure. `bench/evidence/frontier/env.sh` requires a Harbor that already exists at one exact path:\n\n```sh\ntest \"$(command -v harbor)\" = \"$VENV/bin/harbor\" || {\n    echo \"FATAL: wrong harbor on PATH — expected $VENV/bin/harbor\"\n    echo \"       Create this lane's venv with: bench/evidence/frontier/setup_venv.sh\"\n    return 1; }\ntest \"$(harbor --version)\" = \"$FB_HARBOR_VERSION\" || {\n    echo \"FATAL: harbor $(harbor --version) != $FB_HARBOR_VERSION\"\n    ...\n```\n\nOn a fresh clone, a fresh CI runner, or the AWS rig after a scale-to-zero rebuild, `bench/evidence/frontier/.venv` does not exist, and every script that sources `env.sh` stops with a FATAL that the operator has to resolve by hand — even though `~/.arenabench/harbor/0.20.0/bin/harbor` may already be sitting there, installed by arenabench, at exactly the pinned version.\n\nThis is the same shape as the original bug: a floor treated only as something to check, never as something to satisfy.\n\n## Why it is worth fixing rather than leaving\n\n`env.sh`'s strictness is correct and must not be relaxed — Harbor 0.6.1 silently drops Frontier-Bench's `[verifier] environment_mode = \"separate\"` and grades against the wrong container topology, producing a complete run with plausible wrong numbers. The ask is **not** \"warn instead of failing\". It is \"look in one more place, and build one if it is missing, before failing\".\n\n## Files\n\n- `bench/evidence/frontier/env.sh` — `fb_preflight`, and the `VENV` / `PATH` exports above it\n- `bench/evidence/frontier/setup_venv.sh` — the builder that currently must be run by hand\n- `arenabench/arenabench/harbor.py` — `managed_root()`, `provision()`, `MANAGED_HOME_ENV`, `PROVISION_TIMEOUT`; the Python-side prior art to mirror\n\n## Suggested shape\n\nBefore the `command -v harbor` assertion, resolve in this order and export `PATH` accordingly:\n\n1. `$VENV/bin/harbor` when it exists at `$FB_HARBOR_VERSION` — today's behaviour, unchanged, so an already-set-up lane is byte-identical to what it is now.\n2. `${ARENABENCH_HARBOR_HOME:-$HOME/.arenabench/harbor}/$FB_HARBOR_VERSION/bin/harbor` when it exists and reports that exact version.\n3. Otherwise build one — either by calling `setup_venv.sh` automatically, or with `uv venv --relocatable` + `uv pip install \"harbor[modal]==$FB_HARBOR_VERSION\"`.\n4. Otherwise the FATAL exactly as it reads today.\n\nTwo constraints carried over from #2269:\n\n- **Keep the exact-version equality check.** The Python side uses a `>=` floor; this lane deliberately asserts `==` because it is an audited constant for an evidence claim. Do not weaken it to `>=`.\n- **Do not touch the Terminal-Bench lane.** `bench/evidence/run/env.sh` is pinned to 0.6.1 and is sourced by this file; it must keep resolving to `/opt/homebrew/bin/harbor` (or whatever 0.6.1 the rig has). A shared resolver that upgrades it silently is a measurement change, not a fix.\n\nNote the lane needs `harbor[modal]`, not plain `harbor`, when `FB_ENV=modal` — `fb_assert_backend` imports `modal` from `$VENV`. #2269 deliberately installs plain `harbor` because every arena match launches `--env docker`; this lane cannot make that assumption.\n\n## Verify\n\n1. `mv bench/evidence/frontier/.venv /tmp/venv-backup` (or use a clean clone).\n2. `source bench/evidence/frontier/env.sh && fb_preflight` — currently FATALs on the missing venv; should instead resolve or build a 0.20.0 and pass.\n3. With `~/.arenabench/harbor/0.20.0/` present and `.venv` absent, it must resolve to the managed copy without a network round trip.\n4. `source bench/evidence/run/env.sh && preflight` (the Terminal-Bench lane) must still resolve harbor **0.6.1** — the regression that matters most.\n5. `make gate` (`shellcheck` covers these scripts).\n\n## Done when\n\nA fresh clone with no `bench/evidence/frontier/.venv` can run `bench/evidence/frontier/`'s scripts without a hand-run setup step, the exact-version assertion still refuses anything that is not `$FB_HARBOR_VERSION`, and the Terminal-Bench lane's 0.6.1 resolution is unchanged and covered by step 4 above.\n\nRefs #2269.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2270[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench(frontier): the shell lane still hard-fails on a missing Harbor that arenabench would now find or build"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
