    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Follow-up to #2203 (PR landing the class-level sweep in `bench/harbor_adapter/tests/test_manifest_parity.py`). Three blind spots are declared in that module’s docstring rather than closed; this issue tracks closing them or deciding not to.\n\n## What is covered today\n\n`test_manifest_parity.py::test_every_caller_in_the_tree_still_binds_to_the_live_adapter` sweeps the repository and checks, against the live `stella_harbor`:\n\n| Seam | How | Count today |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.py` imports + call keywords/arity | `ast` + `inspect.signature` | 139 imports, 419 calls |\n| `.sh` / `.bash` / `.md` / `.mdx` embedded imports | textual `from stella_harbor… import …` | 4 |\n| `module:attribute` entry-point specs, any text file | regex + `getattr` | 51 |\n\n## The three gaps\n\n**1. Heredoc Python gets name resolution, not signature checking.**\n`bench/evidence/run/witness_ab.sh` and `bench/evidence/frontier/setup_venv.sh` embed Python in a `<<'PY'` heredoc; `bench/RUNBOOK.md` and `bench/harbor_adapter/README.md` embed it in `python -c '…'`. The sweep resolves the *imported names* in those blocks — the #2182 shape — but cannot AST-parse the block, so a call inside one passing a renamed keyword (`_validated_verifier(spec=…)` after `spec` becomes `model`) is invisible. No embedded block passes keywords today, which is why this was not built: untested extraction machinery is worse than a declared gap.\n\n*Possible approach*: from each textual import hit, expand downward line-by-line while `ast.parse` of the accumulated block succeeds, and run the existing `_check_call` over whatever parses. Conservative by construction — anything recovered is genuinely Python; anything not recovered is no worse than today. Needs a fixture proving it catches a stale keyword in a heredoc, and an anti-vacuity assertion that it recovered a non-zero number of blocks (otherwise it silently degrades to today’s behaviour).\n\n**2. `**splat` callers and `**kwargs` callees are skipped.**\n`_check_call` returns `False` (uncounted, unchecked) when the caller splats a mapping or the callee declares `VAR_KEYWORD`. The per-seam manifest test forbids splats at the one seam that matters (`test_every_keyword_the_manifest_passes_exists_on_the_live_callee`), but nothing forbids them elsewhere. Deciding this is fine, or extending the splat ban to every adapter call site, is a judgement call for the maintainer.\n\n**3. Documentation is exempt from the workflow-reachability assertion.**\n`test_the_bench_workflow_runs_when_a_caller_changes` asserts `.github/workflows/bench.yml`’s scope filter matches every caller file the sweep reads, *except* `.md`/`.mdx`. `website/content/docs/guides/terminal-bench-head-to-head.mdx` carries a `stella_harbor:StellaAgent` entry-point spec and sits outside the filter, so a PR editing only that guide does not run the sweep; the staleness is caught on the next push to `main` (where the filter does not apply) instead of on the PR. Widening the filter to every `.md`/`.mdx` would run six pytest suites on prose changes forever. Alternatives: name that one guide in the filter, or move the copy-pasteable command into a file under `bench/`.\n\n## Files\n\n- `bench/harbor_adapter/tests/test_manifest_parity.py` — the sweep, `_sweep_embedded`, `_check_call`, `_require_non_vacuous`, `TestSweepAntiVacuity`\n- `bench/evidence/run/witness_ab.sh`, `bench/evidence/frontier/setup_venv.sh` — the heredoc callers\n- `bench/RUNBOOK.md`, `bench/harbor_adapter/README.md` — the `python -c` callers\n- `.github/workflows/bench.yml` — the scope filter\n\n## Verify\n\n```\ncd bench/harbor_adapter && uv sync --locked --extra dev && uv run --no-sync pytest -q tests/test_manifest_parity.py\n```\n\nTo see gap 1 concretely, add a keyword the adapter does not accept to the `_validated_verifier(...)` call inside `bench/evidence/run/witness_ab.sh`’s heredoc and observe the suite stay green.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nEither (a) heredoc blocks are AST-checked with a fixture proving a stale keyword inside one fails and an anti-vacuity assertion on the number of blocks recovered, or (b) the gap is closed by a maintainer decision recorded in the module docstring. Same for (2) and (3). Do not close by deleting the declaration — an undeclared blind spot is the failure mode #2203 exists to retire.\n\n## Related\n\n- #2203 / the PR that added the sweep — the class-level ratchet this refines\n- #2182 / #2202 — the two stranded callers, one of them a heredoc import\n- #2049 — `make shellcheck` skips `bench/evidence/run/*.sh`. The sweep now resolves adapter import *names* inside those scripts, repo-wide; it checks nothing about the shell itself (quoting, unset variables, exit-code handling), so #2049 is not subsumed."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2227[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench: the adapter-caller sweep reads heredoc Python textually — a stale keyword inside one is still invisible"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nThe zero-spend guard in `MetricsReader.read`\n(`arenabench/arenabench/telemetry.py`) refuses to score a trial that \"ran\"\nwithout one observed token — the #1480 rule that stops a swallowed 401/429\nfrom reading as an agent loss. But it is gated on `steps > 0`:\n\n```python\nif (\n    metrics.resolved is False\n    and metrics.steps > 0          # <-- never fires for a trial with no stream\n    and metrics.tokens_in == 0\n    and metrics.tokens_out == 0\n    and metrics.total_cost == 0.0\n):\n    metrics.infrastructure = True\n    metrics.resolved = None\n```\n\nA trial that produced **no telemetry at all** has `steps == 0`, so the guard\nskips it and it stays `resolved = False` — a scored agent loss.\n\nObserved on match `cc00894779ff` (artifacts under\n`~/.arenabench/matches/cc00894779ff/`): four of ten trials — `fix-git`,\n`git-leak-recovery`, `prove-plus-comm`, `sanitize-git-repo` — have an\n`agent/` directory containing nothing but `setup`, `agent_result: null`, and\n`exception_info.exception_type: \"RuntimeError\"`. The agent binary never ran.\nThe scoreboard reported **40% (4/10)**; over the six trials that actually\nstarted it is **67% (4/6)**.\n\nThe *cause* of those particular RuntimeErrors is **#2127** (the server reads\nharbor-adapter sources from its launch worktree, and deleting that worktree\nmid-match breaks every later trial install). This issue is the **ingest-side\ndefence**, which is a different file and applies whatever the cause: a trial\nthat measured nothing was never a fair attempt, and #1480's whole argument\n(\"classified on observed spend, because the exception name is exactly what\nlied\") applies with more force when there is no spend *and* no stream.\n\n## Now cheap to fix\n\n#2132 added `TrialMetrics.usage_measured` — a property that is `False`\nexactly when no source published usage. The guard's predicate can become\n`metrics.resolved is False and not metrics.usage_measured`, which drops the\n`steps > 0` special case and covers both shapes with one rule.\n\nCare needed: the guard must not swallow a genuine agent failure that\nhappens to have produced no tokens for an agent-side reason. Decide and state\nwhether `DeliberateStopError` / `SelfReportedVerificationFailureError` (see\n`bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/__init__.py`) should stay scored.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- A trial with no usage measurement and an agent-named exception is left\n  unjudged (`resolved is None`, `infrastructure = True`) and excluded from\n  the solve rate, counted in `aggregate()[\"infrastructure\"]` where a reader\n  sees it.\n- A witness test that fails on today's code: build a trial directory with a\n  `result.json` carrying `exception_info` and no `agent/` artifacts, and\n  assert `resolved is None`. Today it is `False`.\n- `outcome_reason()` gives it a `void_*` label (the Group A prefix), so the\n  #2076 taxonomy and the trends composition panel agree with the solve rate.\n- Re-read match `cc00894779ff` and confirm the seat reports 4/6, not 4/10.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/telemetry.py` (`MetricsReader.read`, `outcome_reason`,\n  `INFRASTRUCTURE_FAILURES`)\n- `arenabench/tests/test_telemetry.py`\n  (`TestInfrastructureFailuresAreNotLosses` is the neighbourhood)\n- `arenabench/tests/test_series.py` if the taxonomy label changes\n\nTests: `cd arenabench && python3 -m pytest tests/test_telemetry.py tests/test_series.py -q`.\n\nRelated: #2127 (root cause of these four), #1480 (the original guard),\n#2066/#2076 (the two-facts rule and the taxonomy), #2132 (`usage_measured`).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2220[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: a trial that produced no telemetry at all is still scored as an agent loss — the zero-spend guard is gated on steps > 0"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
