    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n#2196 made a broken snapshot capture self-identifying: `CaptureStatus` is written to\n`arena/snapshots/capture.json` during the run, and rides into `arena/flip.json` as\n`FlipResult.capture`. `arenabench flip` reads it and refuses to print \"no snapshot\npassed\" alone when capture is what failed.\n\n**The scoreboard does not.** `arenabench/arenabench/telemetry.py` reads `flip.json`\nand takes exactly two fields:\n\n```python\nflip = _load_json(trial_dir / FLIP_NAME)\nif flip is not None:\n    elapsed = flip.get(\"flip_elapsed\")\n    wasted = flip.get(\"wasted_elapsed\")\n    ...\n```\n\nThe new `capture` block is ignored, so the dashboard and the aggregate rollup still\npresent a trial whose capture broke exactly like one that captured cleanly and never\nflipped. `flip_trials` (`sum(1 for t in trials if t.wasted_elapsed is not None)`) is\nthe denominator for the flip statistics and silently includes never-measured trials.\n\nThis is the remaining half of #2196's third suggested-direction bullet: *\"A trial\nthat captured nothing should be distinguishable from one that captured and never\nflipped, in whatever the operator reads (`flip.json` / **the dashboard**).\"* The\n`flip.json` half shipped; the dashboard half did not.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe whole point of the capture record is that a downstream consumer can **refuse**\nto read `flip_index=None` as \"the agent never solved it\". The scoreboard is the\nmost-read downstream consumer and currently cannot.\n\n## Suggested direction\n\n- In `telemetry.py`, read `flip[\"capture\"]` (via `arenabench.snapshot.CaptureStatus.from_json`,\n  which already tolerates a missing/older record by returning `None`) and carry the\n  state onto the per-trial metrics.\n- A trial whose capture state is `failed`/`unavailable`, or whose `snapshots` is 0,\n  should be **excluded from the flip denominator** rather than counted as a\n  no-flip — and named somewhere an operator sees, the way operational aborts are\n  named and excluded rather than silently dropped.\n- `None` (no record) must stay *unknown*, never a clean bill of health — the trial\n  may predate the record. Do not treat absence as consent.\n- The UI under `arenabench/ui/` likely needs the matching column/badge.\n\n## How to verify\n\n`arenabench/tests/test_telemetry.py` already has the fixture shape for this — see\nthe tests that write a `flip.json` with `flip_index: 6` and with `flip_index: null`\nand assert on the scoreboard rollup. Add one with a `capture` block in the `failed`\nstate and assert it does not land in the flip denominator.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nThe scoreboard distinguishes \"captured and never flipped\" from \"never measured\",\nnever counts the latter in the flip statistics, and a test asserts both. A trial\nwith no capture record is still treated as unknown rather than as either.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- `arenabench` is stdlib-only (`pyproject.toml` has deliberately empty\n  `dependencies`).\n- `ruff check` is red on `arenabench/` with pre-existing findings tracked in #2146 /\n  #2193 — do not fold those in, and never run `ruff format`.\n- \"Measure honestly\": excluding a never-measured trial must be *reported*, not\n  silent — the same discipline as naming and excluding operational aborts.\n\nRelated: #2196 (which added the record and the `flip.json` half), #2215, #1590.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2217[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: the scoreboard ignores flip.json's capture record, so a never-measured trial still counts as 'captured and never flipped'"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
