    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`SnapshotSupervisor._snapshot` still reports a **failed patch write** at `log.debug`,\nwhich is the one silent branch #2196 deliberately did not fold in (to keep that fix\nscoped to the capture-outcome record).\n\n`arenabench/arenabench/snapshot.py`, in `_snapshot`:\n\n```python\nif code == 0 and patch.strip():\n    patch_name = f\"{capture.index:04d}.patch\"\n    try:\n        (snap_dir / patch_name).write_text(patch, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    except OSError as exc:\n        log.debug(\"could not write patch for %s: %s\", trial_dir.name, exc)\n        patch_name = None\n```\n\nThis is a silent-wrong of the same family as #2196, one layer down. When the write\nfails, `patch_name` is set back to `None` and the manifest entry is written with\n`patch: null`. But `patch: null` already has a **different, load-bearing meaning**:\n\n```python\ndef unpatched_indices(entries):\n    \"\"\"Snapshots with no patch — identical to the trial's first snapshot.\"\"\"\n    return [e.index for e in entries if e.patch is None]\n```\n\nSo a snapshot whose patch was *lost to an OSError* becomes indistinguishable from a\nsnapshot that was *genuinely identical to the pristine workspace*. Replay's\n`_Probe.__call__` skips `_apply` entirely when `entry.patch` is falsy, so it probes\nthe **pristine image** and scores that snapshot \"did not pass\".\n\n## Why it matters\n\nA run whose disk filled mid-trial (the realistic trigger) produces a manifest of\nentries that all look \"unchanged\", every probe reads the pristine state, and the\nflip search reports `flip_index=None` — \"the agent never solved it\". Same wrong\nbenchmark conclusion as #2196, reached by a different silent branch.\n\n## Suggested direction\n\n- Distinguish \"no patch because nothing changed\" from \"no patch because the write\n  failed\". A third state on `SnapshotEntry` (e.g. `patch_error: str | None`) or a\n  sentinel is fine; the constraint is that `unpatched_indices` must stop conflating\n  them, and replay must treat a *lost* patch as **unknown** (like a probe that could\n  not run) rather than as \"did not pass\" — `bisect_first_pass` already handles `None`\n  correctly and steps past it.\n- Raise the log level. #2196 added `SnapshotSupervisor._capture_failed`, which\n  already implements the once-per-trial `warning`-then-`debug` anti-spam shape; a\n  full disk would otherwise log every interval. Reusing it is probably right, but\n  note this attempt *did* land a manifest entry, so it must not be counted as a\n  failed capture (`attempts`/`failures` accounting in `CaptureStatus`).\n- Consider whether `SnapshotEntry.to_json` gaining a field needs the same\n  `from_json` back-compatibility treatment the `workspace` field got (it does).\n\n## How to verify\n\n`arenabench/tests/test_snapshot_status.py` shows the pattern: stub `snapshot._exec`\nand `snapshot._container_running` (the module's only two doors to Docker) and drive\n`SnapshotSupervisor._consider` directly — no Docker, no clock. For this bug,\nadditionally monkeypatch the patch write to raise `OSError`, then assert the\nresulting manifest entry is **not** reported by `unpatched_indices`, and that replay\ntreats it as unknown.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nA snapshot whose patch write failed is distinguishable from one that was identical\nto the pristine workspace, in the manifest and to `replay_flip`; a test asserts it;\nand the failure is reported above `debug` without spamming a full-disk run.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- `arenabench` is stdlib-only (`pyproject.toml` has deliberately empty\n  `dependencies`) — do not add a dependency.\n- `ruff check` is red on `arenabench/` with pre-existing findings tracked in #2146 /\n  #2193 — do not fold those in, and never run `ruff format`.\n- Measurement must not be able to cost a benchmark (module docstring): this must not\n  become a run-fatal error.\n\nRelated: #2196 (the capture-outcome record this builds on), #2114, #2197.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2215[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: a lost snapshot patch is indistinguishable from an unchanged workspace, so replay probes the pristine image and reports 'never solved'"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
