    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"The verification half of #2131's definition of done, which the fixing PR could not perform: it needs the rig, a container, and a real Harbor trial.\n\n## What was proven, and where it stops\n\nThe fix (`bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/timeout_reap.py`) is proven at two levels:\n\n- **Local process tests** (`bench/harbor_adapter/tests/test_timeout_reap.py`) — a cancelled await now reaps a stand-in agent that a host-side signal cannot reach, and the journal it was writing stops growing. Both assertions fail on the pre-fix code.\n- **A real Linux container** — the reap program run in `debian:bookworm-slim` against an agent shaped like a `docker exec` one (session leader, a tool child in its group, a `setsid` daemon beside it) took the agent and the tool and left the daemon running.\n\nWhat neither covers is the end-to-end claim #2131 actually stated:\n\n> After a forced timeout in a test trial: no stella process survives in the container when the verifier starts, and `result.json`'s usage equals the jsonl's totals.\n\n## How to confirm it\n\n1. Run one Terminal-Bench task with `agent_timeout_sec` set low enough to force a timeout (`--agent-kwarg agent_timeout_sec=<seconds>`; see `stella_harbor.turn_budget` for why that kwarg is the supported route).\n2. While the verifier runs, `docker compose exec main sh -c 'ls -l /proc/*/exe'` (or re-run the reap program, which reports `no agent process is running` when clean). Expect no process whose `exe` is `/usr/local/bin/stella`.\n3. After the trial: compare `agent/stella-events.jsonl`'s final `budget_tick` / summed `step_usage` against the trial's `stella_accounting` metadata and `result.json`. #2131 measured −16% to −35% here; expect equality.\n4. Record the trial's stderr log: the reap prints a greppable `stella-harbor-reap:` line naming the pids it signalled and any survivors, so step 2's answer is also in the artifact.\n\n## If it does not hold\n\nThe most likely residual is **ordering**, not the reap: `populate_context_post_run` reconstructs the timed-out envelope from `_read_log(_STREAM_EVENTS_NAME)`, which reads Harbor's host-side copy. That copy arrives by download from the container (see `_write_log`'s docstring in `bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/__init__.py`, \"downloaded by Harbor, often root-owned\"). If on the timeout path that download lands *after* the hook, the host copy can be short of the container's file even with the writer dead — a different bug from the one #2131 fixed, and it would need its own issue.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nBoth assertions recorded on this issue against a named trial directory, or a new issue naming what still breaks them.\n\n## Related\n\n#2131 (the fix), #2135 (per-task deadline never acted), #2110 (idle to `AgentTimeoutError`), #2189 (the reap's group boundary)"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2190[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench: confirm #2131's reap on a real forced-timeout trial — no surviving agent, and reported usage equal to the journal's totals"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Follow-up to #2131, filed by the PR that added the reap so the trade-off it made is tracked rather than buried in a module docstring.\n\n## Problem\n\n`bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/timeout_reap.py` reaps a timed-out trial by signalling the **process group** `docker exec` created for the Stella process: `SIGTERM`, bounded wait, `SIGKILL`. That group holds Stella and the shells it spawned for its tools — the work that must stop — and, verified in a real `debian:bookworm-slim` container, a service started with `setsid` has left that group and survives.\n\nA service the agent started with a bare `cmd &` or `nohup cmd &` from a bash tool did **not** leave the group, and is killed.\n\nThat is a deliberate line and it is documented, but it is a judgement call with a cost: on a Terminal-Bench task whose verifier probes a service (`sshd`, `nginx`, a dev server), a trial that timed out *after* correctly setting the service up would now fail verification it might otherwise have passed. The opposite policy has a cost too — #2131's whole premise is that an orphan mutating the filesystem during verification can flip a verdict either way — so this is not obviously wrong, it is unmeasured.\n\n## Why it was drawn here\n\n- #2131's own fix direction says \"kill/reap the agent process group in the container\".\n- #2122 (`stream_release.py`) preserves daemons deliberately, but that is the **completion** branch: a run that proved it finished has a claim on what it left behind. A run that never finished does not.\n- The kernel already draws the line: `setsid` is the difference between \"a service\" and \"a job of the shell Stella spawned\".\n\n## How to decide it\n\n1. Census the affected surface: across a recent match's timeout trials, how many tasks (a) require a live service at verification time and (b) timed out with that service in the agent's process group? `~/.arenabench/matches/<match>/jobs/*/`, and the container-side shape can be reproduced by the recipe in `timeout_reap.py`'s docstring.\n2. If the count is non-zero, the refinement is bounded: exclude from the group signal any pid whose `/proc/<pid>/stat` session id differs from the agent's, *or* whose `exe` is not a shell and whose parent has already exited. Both are readable from the same `/proc` fields the program already parses.\n3. Whichever way it goes, pin it with a container-level test in the shape of `bench/harbor_adapter/tests/test_timeout_reap.py::TestReapProgram::test_the_reap_program_kills_the_agent_process_group` — that test already runs the real program against a real process group and is skipped off Linux.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nEither evidence that the current line costs nothing measurable (recorded on this issue, issue closed), or a refined exclusion with a test that fails on today's program and passes on the new one.\n\n## Files\n\n- `bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/timeout_reap.py` — `container_reap_program`\n- `bench/harbor_adapter/tests/test_timeout_reap.py` — `TestReapProgram`\n\n## Related\n\n#2131, #2122, #2110"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2189[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench(harbor adapter): the timeout reap takes a service the agent backgrounded without setsid — decide whether that line is right"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
