    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Split out of #2131, whose third bullet was a stream-capture question rather than the process-lifetime bug the rest of that issue was about. #2131 is being closed by the reap fix; this half is untouched and needs its own answer, because its definition of done was *\"confirmed (and split into its own issue) or ruled out as model output\"*.\n\n## Problem\n\nIn match `cc00894779ff` (SUT 447f3393, 2026-08-07), the `cobol-modernization__kt3nQsB` trace's final reasoning buffer contains:\n\n- one paragraph duplicated **verbatim**, and\n- two fragments spliced **mid-word**, e.g. `\"…MOVE from X(n) frank\\n\\nible 2. '0' is 0x30…\"` — the shape of `frank` + `ible` being two halves of a word that never met.\n\nEither the reasoning-delta capture is replaying/splicing buffers, or the model genuinely emitted it. Nobody has looked.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nReasoning text rides the same stream path as everything else the adapter reads (`stella-events.jsonl` → `_stream_to_envelope` → ATIF trajectory). If deltas can be duplicated or spliced, the defect is in a path that also carries `step_usage`, tool payloads, and the proof strings a bench conclusion is read from — and CLAUDE.md's standing rule is that a bench conclusion comes from that trace. A splice there is a correctness problem for the measurement, not a cosmetic one.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `~/.arenabench/matches/cc00894779ff/jobs/cc00894779ff-stella-sonnet-5-full-pipeline/cobol-modernization__kt3nQsB/agent/stella-events.jsonl` — the raw journal, which is ground truth over `result.json`/`trajectory.json`.\n- Sibling trials in the same match: `count-dataset-tokens__zitF9qC`, `openssl-selfsigned-cert__5VMc6i2`.\n\n## How to answer it\n\n1. Read the **raw** journal lines, not the rendered trajectory: find the `reasoning`/thinking delta events for the affected step and concatenate them in emission order. If the concatenation is clean and only the *rendered* buffer is spliced, the defect is in rendering (`stella_harbor/atif.py` / `_stream_to_envelope` in `bench/harbor_adapter/stella_harbor/__init__.py`). If the raw deltas themselves duplicate or overlap, the defect is upstream in the provider adapter's SSE folding (`crates/stella-model/src/*.rs`).\n2. Note that all three trials carry `stream_complete: false` — they were **timeout** trials whose exec stream was truncated. Rule that in or out first: a truncated stream plus a host-side reconstruction is an obvious candidate for producing a spliced buffer, and it is cheap to check by comparing a completed trial's buffer against a timed-out one's.\n3. Since #2131 landed, the container-side agent is reaped on timeout, so a fresh timeout trial's journal is final rather than still growing while it is read — re-running one is now a clean control that was not available when this was first observed.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nEither a named defect with a witness test (and a fix, or its own issue), or a written finding on this issue that the text is model output, citing the raw delta sequence that shows it.\n\n## Related\n\n- #2131 (the process-lifetime half, closed by the reap fix)\n- #2110 (trial idles from final answer to `AgentTimeoutError`) — the same match's other timeout pathology"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2188[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bench(harbor adapter): confirm or rule out the reasoning-delta splice in the cc00894779ff traces (split from #2131)"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`arenabench/arenabench/pricing.py`'s `PRICES` is a hand-maintained table, and\nnothing ties it to the set of models a match can actually seat. The failure\nmode is silent and has now recurred three times:\n\n- #1566 — a pipeline seat's triage model (`glm-4.5-air`) had no row, blanking\n  every pipeline trial's cost in that match.\n- #2108 — no `kimi` model had a row at all, so an entire Kimi K3 arm rendered\n  no cost on match `14d0127b8ca7`, beside a GLM arm showing $0.56, in a\n  head-to-head billed as a cost comparison.\n- The same shape is latent for the next model anyone seats.\n\n#2108's fix added the missing rows and made the gap *loud* at read time\n(`TrialMetrics.unpriced_models`, rolled into `aggregate()` totals, printed by\nthe CLI and named in the arena's cost tile). That converts a silent blank into\na visible one — but it still fires only *after* a match has run and spent\nmoney. Nothing fails before the match starts.\n\n## What a gate could check\n\n`PRICES` and the Stella seed catalog (`crates/stella-model/src/catalog.rs`)\ndeliberately carry the same numbers from the same source — see the module\ndocstring and every rate comment in `pricing.py`, which cite the catalog row\nby name. Two candidate guards, either or both:\n\n1. **Parity.** Every catalog entry whose provider is one ArenaBench can seat\n   has a `PRICES` row, and the two agree to the cent. `bench/harbor_adapter`'s\n   `test_posture.py::TestOutputCeilingParity` is the working precedent: it\n   parses `catalog.rs` from Python and asserts against it, and\n   `.github/workflows/bench.yml` already lists `crates/stella-model/src/catalog.rs`\n   in the arenabench/bench scope filter for exactly that test, so the wiring\n   exists.\n2. **Preflight.** `arenabench run` already refuses to start a match whose SUT\n   it cannot build (`sut.sut_problem_for`, `cli.py::_cmd_run`). A seat whose\n   `engine.model` has no `PRICES` row could warn there — before any container\n   starts — rather than being discovered in the results.\n\n## Verify / definition of done\n\n- A test that fails when a catalog model an ArenaBench seat can run has no\n  `PRICES` row (delete the `kimi-k3` row added in #2108 and watch it go red),\n  and passes on the current tree.\n- The test names its source of truth the way `tests/test_pricing.py` does, so\n  a rate that moves fails a test before it drifts.\n- If parity is chosen: pick the tie-breaker deliberately and say so — the\n  catalog is Rust and the table is Python, and a number in two places is how\n  the last one died (see AGENTS.md on `scripts/file-size-baseline.txt`).\n\n## Constraints\n\n- `pricing.py` is deliberately NOT a price oracle (module docstring): it\n  covers the models people actually seat, and anything else reports no cost\n  rather than a guess. A gate must not turn into \"seed every model\".\n- The two-tier keying is load-bearing: bare ids carry the gateway rate,\n  route-qualified ids the first-party rate, and only `price_for_route` /\n  `price_on_route` reach the second tier (#1498). A parity check has to\n  respect that, not flatten it.\n- `arenabench/` is being prepared for ejection into its own repo; a guard\n  that reads `crates/stella-model/src/catalog.rs` by path adds a coupling\n  that ejection will have to answer for. Worth deciding now, not at the split.\n\nRelated: #2108, #1566, #1498, #2146 (ruff is configured but ungated).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 2171[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: nothing gates PRICES against the models a match can seat — a new seat's cost blanks silently"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
