    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n#1839 made the prompt-cache window configurable (`CacheTtl::{FiveMinutes, OneHour}`) and taught the *live* deck seam to read it (`crates/stella-cli/src/cache_insight.rs`). Three consumers that reason about the same window were left on the static default, because they read historical telemetry and have no session config in hand:\n\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/stats.rs` (~line 197) — `provider_cache_ttl_secs(&gap.provider)` decides whether a recorded call was a cache-expired rewrite (`is_cache_expired_rewrite`).\n- `crates/stella-cli/src/fleet_warmth.rs` (~line 74) — `provider_cache_ttl_secs(provider_id)` drives the fleet's warmth lookup.\n- `crates/stella-model/src/cache_economics.rs::diagnose_cache_with_idle` — refines `PrefixInstability` into `CacheCause::IdleBeyondTtl` when the idle gap reaches `provider_cache_ttl_secs(provider)`.\n\nFor a session that ran the 1-hour window, all three use 300s. Concretely: a 20-minute gap on a 1-hour-window session had a **live** prefix, but `stella stats` will call it a cache-expired rewrite and `diagnose_cache_with_idle` will report `IdleBeyondTtl` — \"you stepped away past the TTL\" — when the real cause was something else entirely. That is exactly the confident-and-wrong diagnosis #1525 existed to eliminate, reintroduced through a different door.\n\nCost accounting has the mirror-image gap: `Pricing::cache_savings_usd_for` (the row-derived 1.25x premium) is what `stats.rs` bills historical rows at, but a 1-hour-window turn really wrote at 2x. `Pricing::cache_savings_usd_configured` exists for the live path; historical rows have no way to reach it.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe configured window is a **per-request** choice and is not observable in the usage envelope, so nothing downstream can recover it after the fact. The store records no TTL column. Until it does, every historical reader is guessing, and today it guesses 5 minutes.\n\n## Fix direction\n\nPersist the window alongside the call. Sketch:\n\n1. Add a nullable `cache_ttl_secs` (or a `\"5m\"`/`\"1h\"` text) column to the per-call telemetry table in `crates/stella-store/src/ddl.rs`, with a schema-version bump — see the existing `session_id` (schema v8) precedent for the migration shape.\n2. Stamp it where the call is recorded, from the same `Config::effective_cache_ttl()` the live seam uses.\n3. Have `stats.rs` / `fleet_warmth.rs` prefer the recorded value and fall back to `provider_cache_ttl_secs` for pre-migration rows (an honest \"we do not know, assume the default\"), rather than asserting the default for everything.\n4. Give `diagnose_cache_with_idle` a TTL parameter instead of looking it up, so the caller — which by then has the recorded value — decides. Its current signature hard-codes the lookup.\n\nNote `crates/stella-store/README.md`'s pruning contract: dropping an execution cascades to the tables keyed off `executions.id`, and the schema declares no foreign keys, so a new column needs no cascade work but the prune path should be re-read before touching the DDL.\n\n## Also worth checking in the same pass\n\n`stella-tui`'s `AgentEntry::cache_diagnosis` re-derives `diagnose_cache`'s gate by hand (the TUI cannot depend on `stella-model`), including the gap-vs-TTL refinement, off a TTL the CLI producer hands it. `cache_insight.rs` now sends the configured window, so the TUI copy should already be correct — but `cache_economics.rs`'s module docs explicitly warn that nothing cross-checks the two. Confirm the deck's countdown and `stella stats` agree for a 1-hour session before closing.\n\n## Verify\n\n- A store round-trip test: record a call under `CacheTtl::OneHour`, read it back, assert the recorded window is 3600 and not the 300 default.\n- A `stats.rs` table test: a 20-minute gap on a 1-hour-window row is **not** an expired rewrite, while the same gap on a 5-minute-window row **is**. This fails on today's code.\n- A `diagnose_cache_with_idle` case: gap 1200s, 1-hour window, writes greater than zero, low reads reports `PrefixInstability`, not `IdleBeyondTtl`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n`stella stats` and the fleet warmth lookup report the window the session actually ran, pre-migration rows degrade to the documented default rather than silently asserting it, and the savings figure for a 1-hour row charges the 2x write premium.\n\nRefs #1839, #1525\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 1988[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"stats, fleet warmth, diagnose_cache_with_idle assume a 5-minute cache window — a 1-hour session is misdiagnosed as IdleBeyondTtl"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
