    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n#1839 landed a configurable prompt-cache window (`CacheTtl::{FiveMinutes, OneHour}`) that reaches the wire through the Anthropic Messages adapter only. `crates/stella-model/src/cache_economics.rs::provider_honors_cache_ttl` is the gate:\n\n```rust\npub fn provider_honors_cache_ttl(provider: &str) -> bool {\n    provider == \"anthropic\"\n}\n```\n\nBedrock and OpenRouter both front the same Anthropic prompt cache and both carry a `CachePosture::OptIn` row in `crates/stella-model/src/provider_parity.rs`, but neither adapter forwards the configured window. So a user on `bedrock/us.anthropic.claude-*` or an OpenRouter Claude route who sets `providers.<id>.cache_ttl` to `\"1h\"` gets nothing: the setting parses, resolves onto `Config::cache_ttl`, reaches `ProviderParts::cache_ttl`, and is then dropped by the factory arm.\n\nThis is deliberately *inert* rather than half-wired — `configured_cache_ttl_secs` returns the static 300s for them, so the deck's warmth countdown does not count down a window nobody granted — but it means the knob silently does nothing on two of the three opt-in providers.\n\n## Files\n\n- `crates/stella-model/src/cache_economics.rs` — `provider_honors_cache_ttl` (the one predicate every consumer branches on; extending support should be a one-line change here plus the adapter work)\n- `crates/stella-model/src/bedrock.rs` — `cachePoint` blocks; needs the Converse spelling of a TTL, if one exists\n- `crates/stella-model/src/zai.rs` — the OpenRouter identity's request-root `cache_control` (search for the openrouter identity gating)\n- `crates/stella-model/src/factory.rs` — the `Dialect::Bedrock` and `Dialect::OpenaiCompatible` arms currently ignore `spec.cache_ttl`\n- `crates/stella-model/src/provider_parity.rs` — the `CACHE_POSTURE` rows for both, whose `mechanism` text must name the new capability\n\n## Constraints discovered in #1839\n\n- **Verify the provider actually supports it before wiring.** Bedrock's Converse `cachePoint` may have no TTL field at all, and OpenRouter's pass-through of `cache_control` to upstream Anthropic is undocumented on the TTL axis. If a provider genuinely cannot express the window, the correct outcome is to *document that on its `CachePosture` row* and close this — not to send a field that 400s.\n- **Both halves ship together or neither.** On Anthropic the `ttl` field requires the `extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11` beta header; field-without-header is rejected and header-without-field changes nothing. Expect a similar pairing.\n- **The write premium must move with the window.** `CacheTtl::write_premium_multiplier` returns 2.0 for the 1-hour window vs 1.25 for 5 minutes, and `Pricing::cache_savings_usd_configured` only applies it for providers `provider_honors_cache_ttl` names. Extending the predicate without confirming the provider really bills 2x would mis-price every write.\n- `cache_economics.rs::the_local_write_premium_and_ttl_tables_agree_with_the_posture_matrix` asserts `provider_honors_cache_ttl` can only ever name an opt-in-cache provider; keep it passing.\n\n## Verify\n\nA wiremock witness per provider, mirroring `crates/stella-model/src/anthropic/tests/cache_breakpoints.rs`:\n\n- `one_hour_ttl_sends_the_ttl_field_and_the_beta_header` — a request matcher that only accepts a body carrying the TTL marker AND whatever header gates it\n- `the_default_window_sends_no_ttl_field_and_no_beta_header` — the byte-stability mirror (invariant 7)\n\nPlus `configured_cache_ttl_secs(\"bedrock\", CacheTtl::OneHour) == Some(3600)` replacing the current `Some(300)` assertion in `configured_ttl_reaches_exactly_the_providers_whose_adapter_sends_it`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nEither (a) both providers forward the window, with the witnesses above and updated `CACHE_POSTURE` mechanism text; or (b) a documented finding on each `CachePosture` row explaining which provider cannot express a TTL and why, with `provider_honors_cache_ttl` left as-is.\n\nRefs #1839\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 1987[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"bedrock, openrouter: the 1-hour prompt-cache window is unreachable — their adapters never forward CacheTtl"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
