    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nPR #1825 (issue #1777) made a *template-declared* credential contract loud: a seat whose `[contestant.env] required = [...]` names all resolve to nothing now fails `POST /api/matches` with a 400 before any container exists.\n\nA seat with **no declaration** — e.g. built in the web UI wizard, or a JSON payload that simply omits `env` — still launches when none of its provider/agent-derived candidates (`missing_credentials` in `arenabench/arenabench/agents.py`) is present. The only signal is `run.warnings` (`MatchRunner._launch`, `arenabench/arenabench/runner.py` ~line 485: \"no credential in this seat's env — expected one of: ...\"), and the arm then 401s and scores a `0.0` indistinguishable from an agent loss. #1777's definition of done (\"a seat whose provider declares required names and has none of them should refuse to start\") covers this case too; #1825 deliberately scoped the hard refusal to declared seats to avoid breaking the wizard flow and its tests.\n\n## What done looks like\n\n`ArenaServer.create_match` (`arenabench/arenabench/server.py`) refuses — after `apply_ambient_credentials` + `apply_saved_credentials` — any seat for which `missing_credentials(contestant)` is non-empty, with the same actionable ValueError shape the declared path uses (names + `credentials_path()`), plus an explicit opt-out for deliberate credential-less runs (mirror the CLI's `--allow-missing-env`, e.g. an `allow_missing_env` payload flag the UI can set).\n\n## Constraints / notes\n\n- The UI wizard prompts for env via `parse_template`'s `required_env` map, so the normal flow should already carry credentials; audit `ui/components/setup/setup-view.tsx` for how it behaves when the operator pastes nothing, and add the flag there if a bypass is wanted.\n- `arenabench run` already refuses (with `--allow-missing-env`) — only the server path is lenient.\n- Tests to touch: `arenabench/tests/test_credentials.py::TestDeclaredRequiredEnv::test_match_creation_refuses_a_seat_with_none_of_its_declared_names` is the pattern; add the underived twin and check no existing server test creates credential-less matches expecting success.\n- Ambient resolution must stay declaration-only (`apply_ambient_credentials`'s docstring): the refusal may consider derived names, but ambient env must not be *wired* into undeclared seats — that would reopen the scrub bypass `test_an_ambient_subscription_token_never_reaches_a_seat` guards.\n\nRefs #1777, #1825."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 1827[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: a wizard-built seat with no credential still launches from POST /api/matches (warning only)"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
  [1;37m{[m
    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\nWhen the Docker daemon is not running, `arenabench` still launches one `harbor run` subprocess per contestant; each exits within ~2s printing `Docker daemon is not running. Please start Docker and try again.` to its seat log. Since PR #1772 the match now correctly lands `failed` with that line in `match.note` — but the arena still spent a launch, wrote provenance, started recorder/snapshot supervisors if configured, and only tells the operator *after* the fact. Observed live on match `1eb525153bc5`.\n\n## Proposal\n\nIn `MatchRunner.start` (`arenabench/arenabench/runner.py`), before launching any seat, probe Docker the same way the Harbor version floor is probed (`harbor.require_for_dataset` is the exemplar — refusal, not warning): e.g. `docker info` with a short timeout, or the cheapest equivalent Harbor itself uses. If the daemon is unreachable, refuse the start with an actionable error that reaches the HTTP API / UI (`match.note` + a 4xx from the start endpoint), naming the fix ('start Docker Desktop / colima').\n\nScope note: only matches whose spec runs `--env docker` (currently all of them) need the probe.\n\n## Files\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/runner.py` — `MatchRunner.start`, `_launch`\n- `arenabench/arenabench/harbor.py` — where the probe helper likely belongs, beside `require_for_dataset`\n- `arenabench/tests/test_arena.py` — `TestFailedMatchStatus` (added in PR #1772) shows the Match/ContestantRun test conventions\n\n## Done when\n\nA match started with Docker down never launches a seat process, the start surface reports the refusal with the daemon-down message, and a witness test pins it (monkeypatch the probe at the `arenabench.harbor` seam, per `_fake_harbor` in `tests/test_arena.py`)."[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 1773[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: preflight Docker availability at match start instead of letting both seats crash into it"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
