    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## The ask\n\nArenaBench today is built, documented, and tested as a two-arm head-to-head: every committed match is \"X vs Y\", the watcher voids the whole match when either arm dies, and the resource math in the match templates assumes exactly two task containers. Convert it into an N-contestant system that also supports **solo runs** — one contestant through the task list, reported as a baseline, not a race.\n\n## What is already N-ready (verified — do not redo)\n\nA fresh agent should know the conversion is smaller than it looks. The data model and most of the plumbing already speak N:\n\n- `arenabench/arenabench/model.py` — `MatchSpec.contestants` is a tuple, validation requires \"at least one contestant\" (line ~501), seat colours auto-assign `ARENA_COLORS[seat % len(ARENA_COLORS)]` (line ~414), and slugs disambiguate.\n- `arenabench/arenabench/runner.py` — one `ContestantRun` per contestant, launched in a loop (`_launch`, line ~339). Nothing indexes `[0]`/`[1]`.\n- `arenabench/arenabench/telemetry.py::leaders()` (line ~576) — already N-way: ties return every tied contestant, a seat missing a number is excluded per-dimension, unjudged seats are excluded everywhere.\n- `arenabench/ui/components/setup/setup-view.tsx` — seats are a dynamic array with add/remove (remove disabled only below 1 seat), so the browser can already *launch* a 1-seat or 5-seat match.\n- `arenabench/ui/components/arena/arena-view.tsx` (line ~147) — lane grid renders `contestants.length` lanes, capped at 3 columns.\n- `arenabench/arenabench/server.py` — the launch API takes a `contestants` array with no count check.\n\nSo a 3-seat or 1-seat match parses, launches, and runs **today** — but it produces wrong or misleading results, for the reasons below. The work is semantic, not structural.\n\n## Gap 1 — match-global voiding is wrong for N seats (the core of this ticket)\n\n`arenabench/arenabench/monitor.py:401-404`: `MonitorState.invalidating` is `critical > 0` across **all** seats, and both `arenabench watch` and `arenabench run` exit 3 (\"do not publish these numbers\") on it (`arenabench/arenabench/cli.py`, run path around line 136-141, watch documented at line ~376). That contract is correct for 2 arms — if one arm's credentials died, the comparison is dead. For N ≥ 3 it throws away good data: one seat hitting `zero-token` (a swallowed 401) should void **that seat**, and the match should survive as a comparison among the remaining seats.\n\nDesign:\n- A critical detection voids the *seat* it is attributed to (`Detection.agent` already carries the attribution — `monitor.py:376-394` `scan()` stamps it).\n- Match-level void becomes: **fewer than 2 unvoided seats remain** in a multi-seat match, or the only seat voided in a solo run.\n- `summary_json()`'s `end` event (`monitor.py:406`) gains an additive `voided: [seat, ...]` field. The protocol is emitter-agnostic JSONL (`docs/spec/agent-monitor-protocol.md`) — update the spec in the same PR; additive fields keep old readers working.\n- Voided seats are excluded from `leaders()` and from the snapshot's scoreboard the same way unjudged seats already are (`telemetry.py:582-597` documents the existing exclusion pattern to copy).\n- **Exit-code contract is load-bearing**: `scripts/fullauto/commands/fullauto/bench.md` and `scripts/fullauto.sh` read exit 3 as \"match void\". Keep exit 3 meaning \"these numbers must not be published\" (now: match-level void). Per-seat void with a surviving match must NOT exit 3 — it prints the seat's `!!` line and the report marks that seat voided.\n\n## Gap 2 — solo runs report as a race with one runner\n\nWith one contestant, `leaders()` crowns the lone seat on every dimension the moment it has one judged trial — every crown in the UI, all gold, all meaningless. The final report (`cli.py` `_cmd_run` tail, line ~114-141) prints a comparative scoreboard, and the void message says \"match invalidated\".\n\nDesign:\n- Derive the mode: `solo = len(spec.contestants) == 1`. No new config key — the TOML already expresses it.\n- In solo mode: `leaders()` returns `{}` (or callers suppress crowns — pick whichever leaves the fewest call sites aware of the mode); the CLI report prints absolute numbers (solve rate, priced cost, cache hit rate, steps) with no crown/winner framing; UI hides the crown row of the scoreboard.\n- **Naming hazard**: in this codebase a \"trial\" is one `(contestant, task)` cell of the grid — `model.py:9` says a match is `len(tasks) x len(contestants)` trials, and the setup UI prints that arithmetic. The user-facing word for a 1-contestant run should be **\"solo run\"**, never \"trial\", or every existing doc sentence becomes ambiguous. Do not rename the existing \"trial\" concept.\n- `arenabench template` (`cli.py:144`, `_cmd_template`) emits a hard-coded 2-seat TOML. Add `--solo` (one Stella seat) and `--seats N`.\n\n## Gap 3 — no global container budget (the practical blocker for N > 2)\n\n`runner.py:395` passes `spec.concurrency` straight through as `--n-concurrent` to **each** contestant's Harbor job, so total concurrent load is `N × concurrency` task containers plus N recorders. The committed match templates document the math for 2: `matches/fable5-claude-code-vs-stella.toml:41-43` — \"1 per contestant = 2 task containers (~2GB each) + 2 recorders. Colima is 10GB\". Nothing enforces it for N; a 4-seat match at concurrency 1 will thrash a 10GB Colima and nothing warns.\n\nDesign:\n- Add a match-level `max_containers` (default: `N × concurrency`, i.e. today's behaviour — existing TOMLs unchanged).\n- When `N × concurrency > max_containers`, the runner staggers seats in waves of `floor(max_containers / concurrency)` seats.\n- **Fairness caveat to document**: staggered seats no longer share wall-clock conditions (provider load, time of day become confounds). The report must mark a staggered match as such — the same honesty rule as voiding, and consistent with how `docs/glm-headtohead.md` treats shared-quota confounds. Default stays fully parallel; staggering is the operator's explicit trade.\n\n## Gap 4 — fixtures, tests, docs all assume 2\n\n- Every fixture match is 2-seat (`tests/fixtures/matches/dd52a57a6f49/`); `tests/test_arena.py`, `test_snapshot.py`, `test_telemetry.py`, `test_leaderboard.py` exercise only 2.\n- All committed `matches/*.toml` are \"vs\" pairs; README's pitch and the setup UI's comment (\"Default seating: the head-to-head this tool exists for\", `setup-view.tsx:156`) frame the tool as strictly head-to-head.\n- Lane grid caps at 3 columns (`arena-view.tsx:147`) — check N=4..6 wraps acceptably; scoreboard and transcript picker need an eyeball at N=1 and N≥4.\n\n## Plan (one PR per phase; each lands green independently)\n\n1. **Per-seat voiding** — monitor + exit codes + spec + `leaders()`/snapshot exclusion. The semantic core; everything else reads its output.\n2. **Solo mode** — derived flag, non-comparative report, crown suppression, `template --solo`, \"solo run\" naming in copy.\n3. **Container budget** — `max_containers`, wave scheduling, staggered-match marking in report + docs.\n4. **Fixtures + witness tests + docs** — 1-seat and 3-seat fixtures; README/matches/UI copy updated from \"head-to-head\" to \"N seats, 2 is the classic\".\n\n## Witness tests (the definition of done)\n\nEach fails on today's code and passes after:\n\n1. **3-seat survival**: a 3-seat fixture where one seat trips `zero-token` → that seat is voided, `leaders()` excludes it, the match reports the surviving pair, exit code is **not** 3. (Today: exit 3, whole match void.)\n2. **2-seat degeneration**: same fixture reduced to 2 seats → one critical detection still voids the match, exit 3. (The existing contract, now as a regression guard.)\n3. **Solo crowns**: a 1-seat fixture with judged trials → `leaders()` yields no crowns and the report contains no winner framing. (Today: the lone seat is crowned on every dimension.)\n4. **Budget wave**: `max_containers = 2` with 4 seats at concurrency 1 → at most 2 seats run concurrently and the snapshot marks the match staggered. (Today: 4 containers launch at once.)\n5. **`end` event**: `summary_json()` carries `voided` and the spec's field table lists it (`docs/spec/agent-monitor-protocol.md`).\n\n## Constraints a fresh agent needs\n\n- **Exit 3 is a published contract** — fullauto's bench phase and CI read it. Its meaning (\"do not publish\") must not drift; only *when* it fires changes.\n- The monitor protocol is consumed by emitters other than arenabench (see the spec) — additive JSONL fields only.\n- `priced_cost` is already per-seat via the route recorded at launch (#1498/#1565) and `leaders()` already handles unpriced seats — pricing needs **no** changes for N; do not touch it.\n- Existing 2-seat TOMLs and the browser flow must run byte-identically: defaults preserve today's behaviour everywhere.\n- Python side has no gate ratchet, but `arenabench/tests` run in CI (`bench.yml` — note all six suites share one job; a failure in an earlier suite hides later ones).\n\nRefs #1480 (the watch/void machinery this builds on), #1536 (flip.json wiring — a solo-run report is a natural consumer).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 1584[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"arenabench: N contestants and solo runs — per-seat voiding, a global container budget, non-comparative reporting"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
