    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## Problem\n\n`scripts/fullauto.sh bench h2h --rig` starts the EC2 Terminal-Bench rig, runs the\nClaude Code vs Stella match, copies results back, and stops the instance via an\nEXIT/INT/TERM trap. Every piece is written from the documented procedure\n(`bench/RUNBOOK.md`, the rig access notes) but **the path has never actually\nexecuted** — it was not exercised during the initial build because starting the\nrig costs $1.90/hr.\n\nThe untested parts are the ones that cost money if wrong:\n\n1. The stop trap. If it does not fire, the rig bills $45.56/day. Leaving it idle\n   once already pushed a ~$68/month account to a $1,006 forecast and tripped a\n   budget alarm.\n2. The remote command assumes `~/stella` exists on the rig and that `arenabench`\n   is on the remote PATH. Neither is asserted before the instance is started.\n3. `scp` of `/tmp/h2h.json` assumes the match wrote results there — if the match\n   fails early the file is absent and the function warns but still returns a path\n   that does not exist.\n\n## Where\n\n- `scripts/fullauto.sh` — `bench_h2h`, the `--rig` branch\n- `bench/RUNBOOK.md` — the procedure it encodes\n- `docs/design/stella-bench-handoff/tb909-key.pem` — the key path it assumes\n\n## Reproduce / verify\n\n    scripts/fullauto.sh bench h2h --rig\n\nCosts real money. Verify the cheap parts first with the instance already\nstopped: the key-path check, the `aws` preflight, and that the trap fires on a\nforced early exit.\n\n## Constraints already discovered\n\n- Instance `i-07d46341dcc9a31b3` (`stella-vs-cc-rig`), us-east-1, user `ubuntu`.\n  The public IP changes across stop/start — it must always be read from AWS.\n- SSH is refused for up to a minute after `instance-running`; the code polls, but\n  the poll bound (20 x 10s) is a guess.\n- `verifier_result.rewards.reward` is the real reward field;\n  `verifier_result.reward` is always null and scores every run as zero.\n\n## Done when\n\nThe `--rig` path has been run once end-to-end, the results file parses, and the\ninstance is confirmed stopped afterwards via `aws ec2 describe-instances`. Any\ndivergence from the written procedure is fixed in the same PR. Add a\n`--rig --dry-run` mode that performs every check and prints the commands without\nstarting the instance, so the path is verifiable for free from then on.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 1550[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"fullauto: 'bench h2h --rig' has never been run end-to-end"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
