    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## What\n\nWhen a streamed model call dies mid-response, Stella now salvages whatever the adapter had already been told and reports it as a flagged lower bound (see the partial-usage work that added `PartialUsage`, `ProviderError::with_partial`, and the `partial` field on `AgentEvent::UsageIncomplete`).\n\nThat recovers **tokens**. It does not recover the **actual billed cost** — we price the salvaged tokens against the catalog, which is a list-price estimate, not what the provider charged.\n\nOpenRouter is the one provider where the real number is retrievable after the fact. It exposes a per-generation lookup keyed by an id that arrives in the **first** SSE chunk, so it is available even for a stream that dies immediately afterward:\n\n```\nGET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/generation?id=<gen_id>\n```\n\nThe response carries the actual `total_cost`, native token counts, and the upstream provider that served the request.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThree things this closes that the current fix cannot:\n\n1. **Exact cost for dropped attempts.** Today a salvaged attempt records a catalog-priced estimate. OpenRouter's own figure would let that row graduate from `usage_complete = false` to a real, attested number.\n2. **The routing confound.** OpenRouter can serve the same model slug from different upstream providers with different pricing and different behavior. The generation record names which one actually served the call — the confound noted in the head-to-head benchmarking work, currently invisible.\n3. **Cache accounting.** OpenRouter's normalized usage reports cache reads that our SSE parse does not always see.\n\n## Sketch\n\n- Capture the generation `id` from the first chunk in the OpenAI-shaped aggregator (it is present on every chunk; the first is enough).\n- Attach it to `PartialUsage` (or a sibling field) so it survives the error the same way the token counts now do.\n- A reconciliation pass — deferred, not inline; the record is not immediately consistent and blocking the retry on an HTTP round trip would be wrong — looks up any `usage_complete = false` OpenRouter row and re-stamps it with the attested cost, flipping the flag.\n- Reconciliation is the natural home for a `stella stats --reconcile` or a background sweep at session close.\n\n## Scope / non-goals\n\n- **OpenRouter only.** Anthropic, OpenAI, and the z.ai endpoints expose no equivalent post-hoc lookup. This is deliberately a per-provider capability, not a general mechanism, and should not grow a trait until a second provider offers one.\n- Does not change the retry path. The dying call still fails and still retries; this only improves what the ledger says afterward.\n- Requires an API key with permission to read generation metadata — worth confirming the coding-plan keys can, before building.\n\n## Context\n\nFiled as the deferred third tier of the dropped-stream accounting work. Tiers 1 (honest labeling) and 2 (salvage the tokens) are implemented; this is the only remaining piece that turns an estimate into an attested figure.\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 1386[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Recover attested cost for dropped OpenRouter calls via the generation lookup"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
