    [1;34m"body"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"## What's going on\n\nStella has two separate ways to give a task more than one shot:\n\n- **Revisions** — if the check says the work is wrong, try again to fix it. Currently 2.\n- **Parallel attempts** — run the task 2 or more times independently and keep the best result. Currently off.\n\nUntil #1241 neither could be set from a benchmark run at all. They were fully built and connected to nothing. Now both can be selected. **Nobody has tuned them.**\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe two cost very different amounts, and it is easy to get this backwards.\n\n**Revisions are nearly free.** A revision only happens after a check has already failed. A task that works on the first try costs exactly the same whether the limit is 2 or 4. Raising it only changes what happens to near-misses.\n\n**Parallel attempts are not free.** Running 2 attempts doubles the cost of *every* task, including all the ones a single attempt would have solved.\n\nSo the obvious first move is to raise revisions and leave parallel attempts alone — but that is a guess, and this issue is about replacing the guess with numbers.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Run the same task set with revisions at 2, 3, and 4. Record tasks solved and total cost each time.\n2. Separately, run with 2 parallel attempts on the tasks that currently fail. This is where it should help — parallel attempts do nothing for tasks that already pass.\n3. Pick the settings where the extra spend actually buys extra solved tasks, and write down the numbers behind the choice.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Parallel attempts want isolation to be useful, so each attempt works on its own copy and only the winner is kept. #1232 runs them concurrently and #1225 gives each task folder the version control that isolation needs. Check both are on.\n- Guidance already fires after a second failure in a row (#868), so revisions are not blind retries.\n\n## Done when\n\n- We have solved-tasks-and-cost numbers for each setting\n- The benchmark's default values are set from those numbers\n- The reasoning is written down where the next person will find it\n\n## Background\n\n#1211 §6.7 and §6.8. Settings landed in #1241 (`STELLA_MAX_REVISIONS`, `STELLA_CANDIDATES`).\n"[m[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"number"[m[1;37m:[m 1289[1;37m,[m
    [1;34m"title"[m[1;37m:[m [32m"Decide how many retries and parallel attempts a benchmark task should get"[m
  [1;37m}[m[1;37m,[m
